#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:3
msgid "virt-drivers - Detect bootloader, kernel and drivers inside guest"
msgstr "virt-drivers - noteikt sāknētāju, kodolu un draiverus viesī"

#. type: verbatim
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-drivers [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-drivers [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-drivers [--options] -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-drivers [--options] -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:13
msgid ""
"This tool can detect the bootloader, kernel and drivers inside some guests "
"from only the disk image.  It can detect, for example, whether a disk image "
"needs BIOS or UEFI to boot, and whether it supports virtio or requires "
"slower emulated devices."
msgstr ""
"Šis rīks var noteikt dažu viesu sāknētāju, kodolu un draiverus tikai no "
"diska attēla.  Piemēram, tas var noteikt, vai diska attēla sāknēšanai vajag "
"BIOS vai UEFI un vai tas atbalsta virtio vai tam vajadzīgas lēnākas emulētas "
"ierīces."

#. type: =head2
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:18
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "Piezīmes"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:20
msgid ""
"Normally you should distribute hypervisor metadata (eg. libvirt XML or OVF) "
"alongside disk images to tell the hypervisor how to boot them.  This tool is "
"used when this metadata has not been provided.  Work with the supplier of "
"the disk image to get them to provide proper metadata."
msgstr ""
"Parasti kopā ar disku attēliem jāizplata hipervizora metadati (piem., "
"libvirt XML vai OVF), kas norāda hipervizoram, kā tos sāknēt.  Šo rīku "
"izmanto, ja šie metadati nav nodrošināti.  Sadarbojieties ar diska attēla "
"piegādātāju, lai tas nodrošinātu pareizus metadatus."

#. type: =head1
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:25 inspector/virt-inspector.pod:181
msgid "XML FORMAT"
msgstr "XML FORMĀTS"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:27
msgid ""
"The output is an XML document.  At the top level it lists the operating "
"systems found (the same as L<virt-inspector(1)>):"
msgstr ""
"Izvade ir XML dokuments.  Augšējā līmenī tas uzskaita atrastās "
"operētājsistēmas (tāpat kā L<virt-inspector(1)>):"

#. type: verbatim
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:30
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>linux</name>\n"
"     <arch>x86_64</arch>\n"
"     <distro>fedora</distro>\n"
"     ...\n"
"   </operatingsystem>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sdb1</root>\n"
"     ...\n"
"   </operatingsystem>\n"
" </operatingsystems>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>linux</name>\n"
"     <arch>x86_64</arch>\n"
"     <distro>fedora</distro>\n"
"     ...\n"
"   </operatingsystem>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sdb1</root>\n"
"     ...\n"
"   </operatingsystem>\n"
" </operatingsystems>\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:44
msgid "E<lt>firmwareE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>firmwareE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:46
msgid ""
"The E<lt>firmwareE<gt> element lists the firmware which is required to boot "
"the guest.  For UEFI it will additionally show the EFI system partition "
"(\"ESP\").  Guests may support multiple boot firmwares.  For example this "
"guest is detected as using UEFI boot, and the UEFI ESP is the first "
"partition of the first disk:"
msgstr ""
"Elements E<lt>firmwareE<gt> uzskaita programmaparatūru, kas vajadzīga viesa "
"sāknēšanai.  UEFI gadījumā tas papildus parāda EFI sistēmas nodalījumu („ESP"
"”).  Viesi var atbalstīt vairākas sāknēšanas programmaparatūras.  Piemēram, "
"šis viesis ir noteikts kā UEFI sāknēšanas izmantotājs, un UEFI ESP ir pirmā "
"diska pirmais nodalījums:"

#. type: verbatim
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <firmware type='uefi'>/dev/sda1</firmware>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <firmware type='uefi'>/dev/sda1</firmware>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:57
msgid "E<lt>bootloaderE<gt> and E<lt>kernelE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>bootloaderE<gt> un E<lt>kernelE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:59
msgid ""
"The E<lt>bootloaderE<gt> element shows the bootloader found in the Linux "
"guest.  If known, this may contain information about what Linux kernels are "
"provided.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"Elements E<lt>bootloaderE<gt> parāda Linux viesī atrasto sāknētāju.  Ja "
"zināms, tas var saturēt informāciju par nodrošinātajiem Linux kodoliem.  "
"Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <firmware type='bios'/>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>linux</name>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <bootloader type='grub2' config='/boot/grub2/grub.cfg'>\n"
"       <kernel>\n"
"         <name>kernel</name>\n"
"         <version>6.1.0-0.rc6.46.fc38.x86_64</version>\n"
"         <vmlinuz>/boot/vmlinuz-6.1.0-0.rc6.46.fc38.x86_64</vmlinuz>\n"
"         <modules>\n"
"           ...\n"
"         </modules>\n"
"         <supports_virtio_blk/>\n"
"         <supports_virtio_net/>\n"
"         ...\n"
"       </kernel>\n"
"     </bootloader>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <firmware type='bios'/>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>linux</name>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <bootloader type='grub2' config='/boot/grub2/grub.cfg'>\n"
"       <kernel>\n"
"         <name>kernel</name>\n"
"         <version>6.1.0-0.rc6.46.fc38.x86_64</version>\n"
"         <vmlinuz>/boot/vmlinuz-6.1.0-0.rc6.46.fc38.x86_64</vmlinuz>\n"
"         <modules>\n"
"           ...\n"
"         </modules>\n"
"         <supports_virtio_blk/>\n"
"         <supports_virtio_net/>\n"
"         ...\n"
"       </kernel>\n"
"     </bootloader>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:83
msgid ""
"Many more fields are usually available for Linux guests, including a "
"complete list of kernel modules and information about support for virtio.  "
"For a complete example see: "
"L<https://github.com/libguestfs/guestfs-tools/tree/master/drivers>"
msgstr ""
"Linux viesiem parasti ir pieejams daudz vairāk lauku, ieskaitot pilnu kodola "
"moduļu sarakstu un informāciju par virtio atbalstu.  Pilnu piemēru skatiet: "
"L<https://github.com/libguestfs/guestfs-tools/tree/master/drivers>"

#. type: =head2
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:88
msgid "E<lt>driversE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>driversE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:90
msgid ""
"The E<lt>driversE<gt> element lists information about drivers found in "
"Windows guests:"
msgstr ""
"Elements E<lt>driversE<gt> uzskaita informāciju par Windows viesos "
"atrastajiem draiveriem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <firmware type='bios'/>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>windows</name>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <drivers>\n"
"       <driver>\n"
"         <name>scsidev</name>\n"
"         <pci vendor='1077' device='1216' subsystem='8471101E'/>\n"
"         <pci vendor='1077' device='1216' subsystem='8493101E'/>\n"
"       </driver>\n"
"       ...\n"
"     </drivers>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <firmware type='bios'/>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>windows</name>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <drivers>\n"
"       <driver>\n"
"         <name>scsidev</name>\n"
"         <pci vendor='1077' device='1216' subsystem='8471101E'/>\n"
"         <pci vendor='1077' device='1216' subsystem='8493101E'/>\n"
"       </driver>\n"
"       ...\n"
"     </drivers>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:108
msgid ""
"The driver name (eg. C<scsidev>) corresponds to the Windows driver F<.INF> "
"file (eg. F<scsidev.inf>).  The list of PCI, USB etc devices are the "
"matching devices which would cause this driver to load at boot."
msgstr ""
"Draivera nosaukums (piem., C<scsidev>) atbilst Windows draivera F<.INF> "
"failam (piem., F<scsidev.inf>).  PCI, USB u. c. ierīču saraksts ir "
"atbilstošās ierīces, kuru dēļ šis draiveris tiktu ielādēts sāknēšanas laikā."

#. type: =item
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:137 get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:47
msgid "B<--blocksize> B<512>"
msgstr "B<--blocksize> B<512>"

#. type: =item
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:139 get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:49
msgid "B<--blocksize> B<4096>"
msgstr "B<--blocksize> B<4096>"

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:141 get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:51
msgid ""
"This parameter sets the sector size of the disk image added with I<-a> "
"option and is ignored for libvirt guest added with I<-d> option.  See also "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts>."
msgstr ""
"Šis parametrs iestata ar opciju I<-a> pievienotā diska attēla sektora izmēru "
"un tiek ignorēts ar opciju I<-d> pievienotam libvirt viesim.  Skatīt arī "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts>."

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:173 get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:83
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, virt-get-kernel normally turns "
"echoing off so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried "
"about Tempest attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify "
"this flag to see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, virt-get-kernel parasti izslēdz "
"atbalsi, lai nevarētu redzēt, ko rakstāt.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest "
"uzbrukumiem un telpā neviena cita nav, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu, "
"ko rakstāt."

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:182 get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:92
msgid ""
"The default for the I<-a> option is to auto-detect the format of the disk "
"image.  Using this forces the disk format for the I<-a> option on the "
"command line."
msgstr ""
"Opcijai I<-a> pēc noklusējuma diska attēla formāts tiek noteikts "
"automātiski.  Šī opcija piespiež diska formātu opcijai I<-a> komandrindā."

#. type: textblock
#: drivers/virt-drivers.pod:236
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestmount(1)>, L<virt-get-kernel(1)>, "
"L<virt-inspector(1)>, L<virt-v2v(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestmount(1)>, L<virt-get-kernel(1)>, "
"L<virt-inspector(1)>, L<virt-v2v(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:3
msgid "virt-edit - Edit a file in a virtual machine"
msgstr "virt-edit - rediģēt failu virtuālajā mašīnā"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit [--options] -d domname file [file ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit [--options] -d domname file [file ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...] file [file ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...] file [file ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit [-d domname|-a disk.img] file -e 'expr'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit [-d domname|-a disk.img] file -e 'expr'\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit domname file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit domname file\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:17 edit/virt-edit.pod:220
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit disk.img [disk.img ...] file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit disk.img [disk.img ...] file\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:21
msgid ""
"C<virt-edit> is a command line tool to edit C<file> where each C<file> "
"exists in the named virtual machine (or disk image)."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-edit> ir komandrindas rīks, kas rediģē C<file>, ja katrs C<file> "
"eksistē nosauktajā virtuālajā mašīnā (vai diska attēlā)."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:24
msgid ""
"Multiple filenames can be given, in which case they are each edited in "
"turn.  Each filename must be a full path, starting at the root directory "
"(starting with '/')."
msgstr ""
"Var norādīt vairākus failu nosaukumus — tādā gadījumā katrs tiek rediģēts "
"pēc kārtas.  Katram faila nosaukumam jābūt pilnam ceļam, sākot ar saknes "
"direktoriju (sākot ar '/')."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:28
msgid "If you want to just view a file, use L<virt-cat(1)>."
msgstr "Ja vēlaties failu tikai apskatīt, izmantojiet L<virt-cat(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:30
msgid ""
"For more complex cases you should look at the L<guestfish(1)> tool (see "
"L</USING GUESTFISH> below)."
msgstr ""
"Sarežģītākos gadījumos apskatiet rīku L<guestfish(1)> (skatiet L</GUESTFISH "
"IZMANTOŠANA> tālāk)."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:33
msgid ""
"C<virt-edit> cannot be used to create a new file.  L<guestfish(1)> can do "
"that and much more."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-edit> nevar izmantot jauna faila izveidei.  L<guestfish(1)> to var un "
"vēl daudz ko citu."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:38
msgid "Edit the named files interactively:"
msgstr "Rediģēt nosauktos failus interaktīvi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /boot/grub/grub.conf\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /boot/grub/grub.conf\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /etc/passwd\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:44
msgid "For Windows guests, some Windows paths are understood:"
msgstr "Windows viesiem tiek saprasti daži Windows ceļi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d mywindomain 'c:\\autoexec.bat'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d mywindomain 'c:\\autoexec.bat'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:48
msgid ""
"If Perl is installed, you can also edit files non-interactively (see "
"L</NON-INTERACTIVE EDITING> below).  To change the init default level to 5:"
msgstr ""
"Ja ir instalēts Perl, failus var rediģēt arī neinteraktīvi (skatiet L</"
"NEINTERAKTĪVA REDIĢĒŠANA> tālāk).  Lai mainītu noklusējuma init līmeni uz 5:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /etc/inittab -e 's/^id:.*/id:5:initdefault:/'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /etc/inittab -e 's/^id:.*/id:5:initdefault:/'\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:79
msgid "B<-b> EXTENSION"
msgstr "B<-b> EXTENSION"

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:81
msgid "B<--backup> EXTENSION"
msgstr "B<--backup> EXTENSION"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:83
msgid ""
"Create a backup of the original file I<in the guest disk image>.  The backup "
"has the original filename with C<extension> added."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot oriģinālā faila dublējumu I<viesa diska attēlā>.  Dublējumam ir "
"oriģinālā faila nosaukums ar pievienotu C<extension>."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:86
msgid ""
"Usually the first character of C<extension> would be a dot C<.> so you would "
"write:"
msgstr ""
"Parasti C<extension> pirmā rakstzīme būtu punkts C<.>, tāpēc jūs rakstītu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -b .orig [etc]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -b .orig [etc]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:91
msgid "By default, no backup file is made."
msgstr "Pēc noklusējuma dublējuma fails netiek veidots."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:102 win-reg/virt-win-reg.in:132
msgid ""
"If you specify guest block devices directly, then libvirt is not used at "
"all."
msgstr "Ja viesa bloku ierīces norādāt tieši, libvirt netiek izmantots vispār."

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:105
msgid "B<-d> GUEST"
msgstr "B<-d> GUEST"

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:107
msgid "B<--domain> GUEST"
msgstr "B<--domain> GUEST"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:114
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, virt-edit normally turns echoing "
"off so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried about "
"Tempest attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify this "
"flag to see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, virt-edit parasti izslēdz atbalsi, lai "
"nevarētu redzēt, ko rakstāt.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest uzbrukumiem un "
"telpā neviena cita nav, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu, ko rakstāt."

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:119
msgid "B<-e> EXPR"
msgstr "B<-e> EXPR"

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:121
msgid "B<--edit> EXPR"
msgstr "B<--edit> EXPR"

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:123
msgid "B<--expr> EXPR"
msgstr "B<--expr> EXPR"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:125
msgid ""
"Instead of launching the external editor, non-interactively apply the Perl "
"expression C<EXPR> to each line in the file.  See L</NON-INTERACTIVE "
"EDITING> below."
msgstr ""
"Ārējā redaktora palaišanas vietā neinteraktīvi lietot Perl izteiksmi C<EXPR> "
"katrai faila rindai.  Skatiet L</NEINTERAKTĪVA REDIĢĒŠANA> tālāk."

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit --format=raw -a disk.img file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit --format=raw -a disk.img file\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:149
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img file\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:218
msgid "Previous versions of virt-edit allowed you to write either:"
msgstr "Iepriekšējās virt-edit versijas ļāva rakstīt gan:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:224
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit guestname file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit guestname file\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:232
msgid "NON-INTERACTIVE EDITING"
msgstr "NEINTERAKTĪVA REDIĢĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:234
msgid ""
"C<virt-edit> normally calls out to C<$EDITOR> (or vi) so the system "
"administrator can interactively edit the file."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-edit> parasti izsauc C<$EDITOR> (vai vi), lai sistēmas administrators "
"varētu failu rediģēt interaktīvi."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:237
msgid ""
"There are two ways also to use C<virt-edit> from scripts in order to make "
"automated edits to files.  (Note that although you I<can> use C<virt-edit> "
"like this, it’s less error-prone to write scripts directly using the "
"libguestfs API and Augeas for configuration file editing.)"
msgstr ""
"C<virt-edit> var izmantot skriptos automatizētai failu rediģēšanai arī divos "
"veidos.  (Ņemiet vērā: lai gan C<virt-edit> I<var> tā izmantot, mazāk kļūdu "
"rada skriptu rakstīšana tieši ar libguestfs API un Augeas konfigurācijas "
"failu rediģēšanai.)"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:243
msgid ""
"The first method is to temporarily set C<$EDITOR> to any script or program "
"you want to run.  The script is invoked as C<$EDITOR tmpfile> and it should "
"update C<tmpfile> in place however it likes."
msgstr ""
"Pirmā metode ir uz laiku iestatīt C<$EDITOR> uz jebkuru skriptu vai "
"programmu, ko vēlaties izpildīt.  Skripts tiek izsaukts kā C<$EDITOR tmpfile>"
", un tam jāatjaunina C<tmpfile> uz vietas, kā vien vēlas."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:247
msgid ""
"The second method is to use the I<-e> parameter of C<virt-edit> to run a "
"short Perl snippet in the style of L<sed(1)>.  For example to replace all "
"instances of C<foo> with C<bar> in a file:"
msgstr ""
"Otrā metode ir izmantot C<virt-edit> parametru I<-e>, lai izpildītu īsu Perl "
"fragmentu L<sed(1)> stilā.  Piemēram, lai failā aizstātu visus C<foo> ar "
"C<bar>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:251
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d domname filename -e 's/foo/bar/'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d domname filename -e 's/foo/bar/'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:253
msgid ""
"The full power of Perl regular expressions can be used (see L<perlre(1)>).  "
"For example to delete root’s password you could do:"
msgstr ""
"Var izmantot visu Perl regulāro izteiksmju jaudu (skatiet L<perlre(1)>).  "
"Piemēram, lai izdzēstu root paroli, varētu izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:256
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d domname /etc/passwd -e 's/^root:.*?:/root::/'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d domname /etc/passwd -e 's/^root:.*?:/root::/'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:258
msgid ""
"What really happens is that the snippet is evaluated as a Perl expression "
"for each line of the file.  The line, including the final C<\\n>, is passed "
"in C<$_> and the expression should update C<$_> or leave it unchanged."
msgstr ""
"Patiesībā fragments tiek novērtēts kā Perl izteiksme katrai faila rindai.  "
"Rinda, ieskaitot beigu C<\\n>, tiek nodota C<$_>, un izteiksmei jāatjaunina "
"C<$_> vai jāatstāj tas nemainīts."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:263
msgid ""
"To delete a line, set C<$_> to the empty string.  For example, to delete the "
"C<apache> user account from the password file you can do:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izdzēstu rindu, iestatiet C<$_> uz tukšu virkni.  Piemēram, lai no "
"paroļu faila izdzēstu lietotāja kontu C<apache>, varat izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:266
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /etc/passwd -e '$_ = \"\" if /^apache:/'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-edit -d mydomain /etc/passwd -e '$_ = \"\" if /^apache:/'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:268
msgid ""
"To insert a line, prepend or append it to C<$_>.  However appending lines to "
"the end of the file is rather difficult this way since there is no concept "
"of \"last line of the file\" - your expression just doesn't get called "
"again.  You might want to use the first method (setting C<$EDITOR>) if you "
"want to do this."
msgstr ""
"Lai ievietotu rindu, pievienojiet to C<$_> sākumā vai beigās.  Tomēr rindu "
"pievienošana faila beigās šādā veidā ir diezgan sarežģīta, jo nav jēdziena „"
"faila pēdējā rinda” — jūsu izteiksme vienkārši vairs netiek izsaukta.  Ja "
"vēlaties to darīt, varat izmantot pirmo metodi (C<$EDITOR> iestatīšanu)."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:274
msgid ""
"The variable C<$lineno> contains the current line number.  As is "
"traditional, the first line in the file is number C<1>."
msgstr ""
"Mainīgais C<$lineno> satur pašreizējās rindas numuru.  Kā ierasts, faila "
"pirmās rindas numurs ir C<1>."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:277
msgid ""
"The return value from the expression is ignored, but the expression may call "
"C<die> in order to abort the whole program, leaving the original file "
"untouched."
msgstr ""
"Izteiksmes atgrieztā vērtība tiek ignorēta, taču izteiksme var izsaukt C<die>"
", lai pārtrauktu visu programmu, atstājot oriģinālo failu neskartu."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:281
msgid ""
"Remember when matching the end of a line that C<$_> may contain the final "
"C<\\n>, or (for DOS files) C<\\r\\n>, or if the file does not end with a "
"newline then neither of these.  Thus to match or substitute some text at the "
"end of a line, use this regular expression:"
msgstr ""
"Atrodot rindas beigas, atcerieties, ka C<$_> var saturēt beigu C<\\n> vai "
"(DOS failiem) C<\\r\\n>, vai, ja fails nebeidzas ar jaunu rindu, nevienu no "
"tiem.  Tāpēc, lai atrastu vai aizstātu tekstu rindas beigās, izmantojiet šo "
"regulāro izteiksmi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:286
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" /some text(\\r?\\n)?$/\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" /some text(\\r?\\n)?$/\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:288
msgid ""
"Alternately, use the perl C<chomp> function, being careful not to chomp "
"C<$_> itself (since that would remove all newlines from the file):"
msgstr ""
"Vai arī izmantojiet perl funkciju C<chomp>, uzmanoties neizpildīt chomp "
"pašam C<$_> (jo tas noņemtu visas jaunās rindas no faila):"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:292
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" my $m = $_; chomp $m; $m =~ /some text$/\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" my $m = $_; chomp $m; $m =~ /some text$/\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:296
msgid ""
"C<virt-edit> has a limited ability to understand Windows drive letters and "
"paths (eg. F<E:\\foo\\bar.txt>)."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-edit> ierobežoti saprot Windows disku burtus un ceļus (piem., F<E:\\f"
"oo\\bar.txt>)."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:315
msgid ""
"The path is resolved case insensitively to locate the file that should be "
"edited."
msgstr "Ceļš tiek atrisināts reģistrnejutīgi, lai atrastu rediģējamo failu."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:336
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)> is a more powerful, lower level tool which you can use when "
"C<virt-edit> doesn't work."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)> ir jaudīgāks, zemāka līmeņa rīks, ko var izmantot, kad "
"C<virt-edit> nedarbojas."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:339
msgid "Using C<virt-edit> is approximately equivalent to doing:"
msgstr "C<virt-edit> izmantošana ir aptuveni līdzvērtīga šim:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:341
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname edit /file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname edit /file\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:343
msgid ""
"where C<domname> is the name of the libvirt guest, and F</file> is the full "
"path to the file."
msgstr ""
"kur C<domname> ir libvirt viesa nosaukums un F</file> ir pilns ceļš uz failu."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:346
msgid ""
"The command above uses libguestfs’s guest inspection feature and so does not "
"work on guests that libguestfs cannot inspect, or on things like arbitrary "
"disk images that don't contain guests.  To edit a file on a disk image "
"directly, use:"
msgstr ""
"Iepriekšējā komanda izmanto libguestfs viesu inspicēšanas līdzekli, tāpēc tā "
"nedarbojas ar viesiem, kurus libguestfs nevar inspicēt, vai ar patvaļīgiem "
"diska attēliem, kuros nav viesu.  Lai rediģētu failu tieši diska attēlā, "
"izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:351
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -a disk.img -m /dev/sda1 edit /file\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -a disk.img -m /dev/sda1 edit /file\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:353
msgid ""
"where F<disk.img> is the disk image, F</dev/sda1> is the filesystem within "
"the disk image to edit, and F</file> is the full path to the file."
msgstr ""
"kur F<disk.img> ir diska attēls, F</dev/sda1> ir rediģējamā failu sistēma "
"diska attēlā un F</file> ir pilns ceļš uz failu."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:357
msgid ""
"C<virt-edit> cannot create new files.  Use the guestfish commands C<touch>, "
"C<write> or C<upload> instead:"
msgstr ""
"C<virt-edit> nevar izveidot jaunus failus.  Tā vietā izmantojiet guestfish "
"komandas C<touch>, C<write> vai C<upload>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:360
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname touch /newfile\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname touch /newfile\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname write /newfile \"new content\"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname write /newfile \"new content\"\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:364
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname upload localfile /newfile\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish --rw -i -d domname upload localfile /newfile\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:370
msgid "C<EDITOR>"
msgstr "C<EDITOR>"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:372
msgid ""
"If set, this string is used as the editor.  It may contain arguments, "
"eg. C<\"emacs -nw\">"
msgstr ""
"Ja iestatīts, šī virkne tiek izmantota kā redaktors.  Tā var saturēt "
"argumentus, piem., C<\"emacs -nw\">"

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:375
msgid "If not set, C<vi> is used."
msgstr "Ja nav iestatīts, tiek izmantots C<vi>."

#. type: textblock
#: edit/virt-edit.pod:386
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, "
"L<virt-tar-in(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<perl(1)>, L<perlre(1)>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-in(1)>, L<virt-"
"tar-in(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>, L<perl(1)>, L<perlre(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:3
msgid ""
"virt-filesystems - List filesystems, partitions, block devices, LVM in a "
"virtual machine or disk image"
msgstr ""
"virt-filesystems - uzskaitīt failu sistēmas, nodalījumus, bloku ierīces, LVM "
"virtuālajā mašīnā vai diska attēlā"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:13
msgid ""
"This tool allows you to discover filesystems, partitions, logical volumes, "
"and their sizes in a disk image or virtual machine.  It is a replacement for "
"L<virt-list-filesystems(1)> and L<virt-list-partitions(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Šis rīks ļauj atklāt failu sistēmas, nodalījumus, loģiskos sējumus un to "
"izmērus diska attēlā vai virtuālajā mašīnā.  Tas aizstāj L<virt-list-"
"filesystems(1)> un L<virt-list-partitions(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:18
msgid ""
"One use for this tool is from shell scripts to iterate over all filesystems "
"from a disk image:"
msgstr ""
"Viens šī rīka lietojums ir čaulas skriptos, lai izietu cauri visām diska "
"attēla failu sistēmām:"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" for fs in $(virt-filesystems -a disk.img); do\n"
"   # ...\n"
" done\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" for fs in $(virt-filesystems -a disk.img); do\n"
"   # ...\n"
" done\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:25
msgid ""
"Another use is to list partitions before using another tool to modify those "
"partitions (such as L<virt-resize(1)>).  If you are curious about what an "
"unknown disk image contains, use this tool along with L<virt-inspector(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Vēl viens lietojums ir nodalījumu uzskaitīšana pirms citu rīku izmantošanas "
"to mainīšanai (piemēram, L<virt-resize(1)>).  Ja jūs interesē, kas ir "
"nezināmā diska attēlā, izmantojiet šo rīku kopā ar L<virt-inspector(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:30
msgid ""
"Various command line options control what this program displays.  You need "
"to give either I<-a> or I<-d> options to specify the disk image or libvirt "
"guest respectively.  If you just specify that then the program shows "
"filesystems found, one per line, like this:"
msgstr ""
"Dažādas komandrindas opcijas nosaka, ko šī programma parāda.  Jānorāda vai "
"nu opcija I<-a>, vai I<-d>, lai attiecīgi norādītu diska attēlu vai libvirt "
"viesi.  Ja norādāt tikai to, programma parāda atrastās failu sistēmas, pa "
"vienai rindā, šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img\n"
" /dev/sda1\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img\n"
" /dev/sda1\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:39
msgid "If you add I<-l> or I<--long> then the output includes extra information:"
msgstr "Ja pievienojat I<-l> vai I<--long>, izvadē ir papildu informācija:"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img -l\n"
" Name                   Type         VFS   Label  Size\n"
" /dev/sda1              filesystem   ext4  boot   524288000\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root  filesystem   ext4  root   10212081664\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img -l\n"
" Name                   Type         VFS   Label  Size\n"
" /dev/sda1              filesystem   ext4  boot   524288000\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root  filesystem   ext4  root   10212081664\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:47
msgid ""
"If you add I<--extra> then non-mountable (swap, unknown) filesystems are "
"shown as well:"
msgstr ""
"Ja pievienojat I<--extra>, tiek parādītas arī nemontējamas (swap, nezināmas) "
"failu sistēmas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img --extra\n"
" /dev/sda1\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_swap\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_data\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img --extra\n"
" /dev/sda1\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_swap\n"
" /dev/vg_guest/lv_data\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:56
msgid "If you add I<--partitions> then partitions are shown instead of filesystems:"
msgstr ""
"Ja pievienojat I<--partitions>, failu sistēmu vietā tiek parādīti nodalījumi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img --partitions\n"
" /dev/sda1\n"
" /dev/sda2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a disk.img --partitions\n"
" /dev/sda1\n"
" /dev/sda2\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:62
msgid ""
"Similarly you can use I<--logical-volumes>, I<--volume-groups>, "
"I<--physical-volumes>, I<--block-devices> to list those items."
msgstr ""
"Līdzīgi var izmantot I<--logical-volumes>, I<--volume-groups>, I<--physical-"
"volumes>, I<--block-devices>, lai uzskaitītu šos vienumus."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:65
msgid ""
"You can use these options in combination as well (if you want a combination "
"including filesystems, you have to add I<--filesystems>).  Notice that some "
"items fall into several categories (eg. F</dev/sda1> might be both a "
"partition and a filesystem).  These items are listed several times.  To get "
"a list which includes absolutely everything that virt-filesystems knows "
"about, use the I<--all> option."
msgstr ""
"Šīs opcijas var izmantot arī kombinācijā (ja vēlaties kombināciju ar failu "
"sistēmām, jāpievieno I<--filesystems>).  Ievērojiet, ka daži vienumi "
"ietilpst vairākās kategorijās (piem., F</dev/sda1> var būt gan nodalījums, "
"gan failu sistēma).  Šādi vienumi tiek uzskaitīti vairākkārt.  Lai iegūtu "
"sarakstu, kas ietver pilnīgi visu, ko virt-filesystems zina, izmantojiet "
"opciju I<--all>."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:72
msgid ""
"UUIDs (because they are quite long) are not shown by default.  Add the "
"I<--uuid> option to display device and filesystem UUIDs in the long output."
msgstr ""
"UUID (tā kā tie ir diezgan gari) pēc noklusējuma netiek rādīti.  "
"Pievienojiet opciju I<--uuid>, lai garajā izvadē parādītu ierīču un failu "
"sistēmu UUID."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:76
msgid ""
"I<--all --long --uuid> is a useful combination to display all possible "
"information about everything."
msgstr ""
"I<--all --long --uuid> ir noderīga kombinācija visas iespējamās informācijas "
"parādīšanai par visu."

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a win.img --all --long --uuid -h\n"
" Name      Type       VFS  Label           Size Parent   UUID\n"
" /dev/sda1 filesystem ntfs System Reserved 100M -        F81C92571C92112C\n"
" /dev/sda2 filesystem ntfs -               20G  -        F2E8996AE8992E3B\n"
" /dev/sda1 partition  -    -               100M /dev/sda -\n"
" /dev/sda2 partition  -    -               20G  /dev/sda -\n"
" /dev/sda  device     -    -               20G  -        -\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-filesystems -a win.img --all --long --uuid -h\n"
" Name      Type       VFS  Label           Size Parent   UUID\n"
" /dev/sda1 filesystem ntfs System Reserved 100M -        F81C92571C92112C\n"
" /dev/sda2 filesystem ntfs -               20G  -        F2E8996AE8992E3B\n"
" /dev/sda1 partition  -    -               100M /dev/sda -\n"
" /dev/sda2 partition  -    -               20G  /dev/sda -\n"
" /dev/sda  device     -    -               20G  -        -\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:87
msgid "For machine-readable output, use I<--csv> to get Comma-Separated Values."
msgstr ""
"Mašīnlasāmai izvadei izmantojiet I<--csv>, lai iegūtu ar komatiem atdalītas "
"vērtības."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:116
msgid ""
"Display everything.  This is currently the same as specifying these options: "
"I<--filesystems>, I<--extra>, I<--partitions>, I<--block-devices>, "
"I<--logical-volumes>, I<--volume-groups>, I<--physical-volumes>.  (More may "
"be added to this list in future)."
msgstr ""
"Parādīt visu.  Pašlaik tas ir tas pats, kas norādīt šīs opcijas: I<--"
"filesystems>, I<--extra>, I<--partitions>, I<--block-devices>, I<--logical-"
"volumes>, I<--volume-groups>, I<--physical-volumes>.  (Nākotnē šim sarakstam "
"var tikt pievienots vairāk.)"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:121
msgid "See also I<--long>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī I<--long>."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:123
msgid "B<--blkdevs>"
msgstr "B<--blkdevs>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:125
msgid "B<--block-devices>"
msgstr "B<--block-devices>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:127
msgid "Display block devices."
msgstr "Parādīt bloku ierīces."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:156
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, virt-filesystems normally turns "
"echoing off so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried "
"about Tempest attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify "
"this flag to see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, virt-filesystems parasti izslēdz "
"atbalsi, lai nevarētu redzēt, ko rakstāt.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest "
"uzbrukumiem un telpā neviena cita nav, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu, "
"ko rakstāt."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:161
msgid "B<--extra>"
msgstr "B<--extra>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:163
msgid ""
"This causes filesystems that are not ordinary, mountable filesystems to be "
"displayed.  This category includes swapspace, and filesystems that are empty "
"or contain unknown data."
msgstr ""
"Liek parādīt failu sistēmas, kas nav parastas, montējamas failu sistēmas.  "
"Šajā kategorijā ietilpst maiņatmiņa un failu sistēmas, kas ir tukšas vai "
"satur nezināmus datus."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:167
msgid "This option implies I<--filesystems>."
msgstr "Šī opcija ietver I<--filesystems>."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:169
msgid "B<--filesystems>"
msgstr "B<--filesystems>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:171
msgid ""
"Display mountable filesystems.  If no display option was selected then this "
"option is implied."
msgstr ""
"Parādīt montējamās failu sistēmas.  Ja nav izvēlēta neviena attēlošanas "
"opcija, šī opcija tiek pieņemta."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:174
msgid "With I<--extra>, non-mountable filesystems are shown too."
msgstr "Ar I<--extra> tiek parādītas arī nemontējamās failu sistēmas."

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:191
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:200
msgid "B<--fs-version>"
msgstr "B<--fs-version>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:202
msgid "B<--fs-versions>"
msgstr "B<--fs-versions>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:204
msgid ""
"In I<--long> mode, display the filesystem version.  Currently this only has "
"any effect for XFS, displaying either C<4> (for XFS v4) or C<5> (for XFS "
"v5).  XFS v4 support will be removed from Linux in 2030."
msgstr ""
"Režīmā I<--long> parādīt failu sistēmas versiju.  Pašlaik tas ietekmē tikai "
"XFS, parādot C<4> (XFS v4) vai C<5> (XFS v5).  XFS v4 atbalsts no Linux tiks "
"noņemts 2030. gadā."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:212
msgid "In I<--long> mode, display sizes in human-readable format."
msgstr "Režīmā I<--long> parādīt izmērus cilvēkam lasāmā formātā."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:216 ls/virt-ls.pod:397
msgid "B<-l>"
msgstr "B<-l>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:218 ls/virt-ls.pod:399
msgid "B<--long>"
msgstr "B<--long>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:220
msgid "Display extra columns of data (\"long format\")."
msgstr "Parādīt papildu datu kolonnas („garais formāts”)."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:222
msgid "A title row is added unless you also specify I<--no-title>."
msgstr "Tiek pievienota virsrakstu rinda, ja vien nenorādāt arī I<--no-title>."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:224
msgid ""
"The extra columns displayed depend on what output you select, and the "
"ordering of columns may change in future versions.  Use the title row, "
"I<--csv> output and/or L<csvtool(1)> to match columns to data in external "
"programs."
msgstr ""
"Parādītās papildu kolonnas ir atkarīgas no izvēlētās izvades, un kolonnu "
"secība nākamajās versijās var mainīties.  Lai ārējās programmās saskaņotu "
"kolonnas ar datiem, izmantojiet virsrakstu rindu, I<--csv> izvadi un/vai "
"L<csvtool(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:229
msgid ""
"Use I<-h> if you want sizes to be displayed in human-readable format.  The "
"default is to show raw numbers of I<bytes>."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet I<-h>, ja vēlaties, lai izmēri tiktu rādīti cilvēkam lasāmā "
"formātā.  Pēc noklusējuma tiek rādīti neapstrādāti I<baitu> skaitļi."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:232
msgid "Use I<--fs-version> to display filesystem versions."
msgstr "Izmantojiet I<--fs-version>, lai parādītu failu sistēmu versijas."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:234
msgid "Use I<--uuid> to display UUIDs."
msgstr "Izmantojiet I<--uuid>, lai parādītu UUID."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:236
msgid "B<--lvs>"
msgstr "B<--lvs>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:238
msgid "B<--logvols>"
msgstr "B<--logvols>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:240
msgid "B<--logical-volumes>"
msgstr "B<--logical-volumes>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:242
msgid ""
"Display LVM logical volumes.  In this mode, these are displayed irrespective "
"of whether the LVs contain filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Parādīt LVM loģiskos sējumus.  Šajā režīmā tie tiek parādīti neatkarīgi no "
"tā, vai LV satur failu sistēmas."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:245
msgid "B<--no-title>"
msgstr "B<--no-title>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:247
msgid "In I<--long> mode, don’t add a title row."
msgstr "Režīmā I<--long> nepievienot virsrakstu rindu."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:249
msgid ""
"Note that the order of the columns is not fixed, and may change in future "
"versions of virt-filesystems, so using this option may give you unexpected "
"surprises."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka kolonnu secība nav fiksēta un nākamajās virt-filesystems "
"versijās var mainīties, tāpēc šīs opcijas izmantošana var sagādāt negaidītus "
"pārsteigumus."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:253
msgid "B<--parts>"
msgstr "B<--parts>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:255
msgid "B<--partitions>"
msgstr "B<--partitions>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:257
msgid ""
"Display partitions.  In this mode, these are displayed irrespective of "
"whether the partitions contain filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Parādīt nodalījumus.  Šajā režīmā tie tiek parādīti neatkarīgi no tā, vai "
"nodalījumi satur failu sistēmas."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:260
msgid "B<--pvs>"
msgstr "B<--pvs>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:262
msgid "B<--physvols>"
msgstr "B<--physvols>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:264
msgid "B<--physical-volumes>"
msgstr "B<--physical-volumes>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:266
msgid "Display LVM physical volumes."
msgstr "Parādīt LVM fiziskos sējumus."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:270
msgid "B<--uuids>"
msgstr "B<--uuids>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:272
msgid "In I<--long> mode, display UUIDs as well."
msgstr "Režīmā I<--long> parādīt arī UUID."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:286
msgid "B<--vgs>"
msgstr "B<--vgs>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:288
msgid "B<--volgroups>"
msgstr "B<--volgroups>"

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:290
msgid "B<--volume-groups>"
msgstr "B<--volume-groups>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:292
msgid "Display LVM volume groups."
msgstr "Parādīt LVM sējumu grupas."

#. type: =head1
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:300
msgid "COLUMNS"
msgstr "KOLONNAS"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:302
msgid ""
"Note that columns in the output are subject to reordering and change in "
"future versions of this tool."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka izvades kolonnu secība nākamajās šī rīka versijās var "
"mainīties."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:307
msgid "B<Name>"
msgstr "B<Name>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:309
msgid "The filesystem, partition, block device or LVM name."
msgstr "Failu sistēmas, nodalījuma, bloku ierīces vai LVM nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:311
msgid ""
"For device and partition names these are displayed as canonical libguestfs "
"names, so that for example F</dev/sda2> is the second partition on the first "
"device."
msgstr ""
"Ierīču un nodalījumu nosaukumi tiek parādīti kā kanoniskie libguestfs "
"nosaukumi, piemēram, F</dev/sda2> ir pirmās ierīces otrais nodalījums."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:315
msgid ""
"If the I<--long> option is B<not> specified, then only the name column is "
"shown in the output."
msgstr ""
"Ja opcija I<--long> B<nav> norādīta, izvadē tiek rādīta tikai nosaukuma "
"kolonna."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:318
msgid "B<Type>"
msgstr "B<Type>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:320
msgid "The object type, for example C<filesystem>, C<lv>, C<device> etc."
msgstr "Objekta tips, piemēram, C<filesystem>, C<lv>, C<device> u. c."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:322
msgid "B<VFS>"
msgstr "B<VFS>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:324
msgid ""
"If there is a filesystem, then this column displays the filesystem type if "
"one could be detected, eg. C<ext4>."
msgstr ""
"Ja ir failu sistēma, šajā kolonnā tiek parādīts failu sistēmas tips, ja to "
"izdevās noteikt, piem., C<ext4>."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:327
msgid "B<Label>"
msgstr "B<Label>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:329
msgid ""
"If the object has a label (used for identifying and mounting filesystems) "
"then this column contains the label."
msgstr ""
"Ja objektam ir etiķete (ko izmanto failu sistēmu identificēšanai un "
"montēšanai), šajā kolonnā ir etiķete."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:332
msgid "B<MBR>"
msgstr "B<MBR>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:334
msgid ""
"The partition type byte, displayed as a two digit hexadecimal number.  A "
"comprehensive list of partition types can be found here: "
"L<http://www.win.tue.nl/~aeb/partitions/partition_types-1.html>"
msgstr ""
"Nodalījuma tipa baits, parādīts kā divciparu heksadecimāls skaitlis.  "
"Visaptverošs nodalījumu tipu saraksts atrodams šeit: L<http://www.win.tue.nl/"
"~aeb/partitions/partition_types-1.html>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:338
msgid "This is only applicable for DOS (MBR) partitions."
msgstr "Tas attiecas tikai uz DOS (MBR) nodalījumiem."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:340
msgid "B<Size>"
msgstr "B<Size>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:342
msgid ""
"The size of the object in bytes.  If the I<--human> option is used then the "
"size is displayed in a human-readable form."
msgstr ""
"Objekta izmērs baitos.  Ja izmantota opcija I<--human>, izmērs tiek parādīts "
"cilvēkam lasāmā formā."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:345
msgid "B<Parent>"
msgstr "B<Parent>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:347
msgid "The parent column records the parent relationship between objects."
msgstr "Vecāka kolonna fiksē vecāka attiecību starp objektiem."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:349
msgid ""
"For example, if the object is a partition, then this column contains the "
"name of the containing device.  If the object is a logical volume, then this "
"column is the name of the volume group."
msgstr ""
"Piemēram, ja objekts ir nodalījums, šajā kolonnā ir to saturošās ierīces "
"nosaukums.  Ja objekts ir loģiskais sējums, šī kolonna ir sējumu grupas "
"nosaukums."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:353
msgid ""
"If there is more than one parent, then this column is (internal to the "
"column) a comma-separated list, eg. C</dev/sda,/dev/sdb>."
msgstr ""
"Ja ir vairāki vecāki, šī kolonna ir (kolonnas iekšienē) ar komatiem atdalīts "
"saraksts, piem., C</dev/sda,/dev/sdb>."

#. type: =item
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:356
msgid "B<UUID>"
msgstr "B<UUID>"

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:358
msgid ""
"If the object has a UUID (used for identifying and mounting filesystems and "
"block devices) then this column contains the UUID as a string."
msgstr ""
"Ja objektam ir UUID (ko izmanto failu sistēmu un bloku ierīču "
"identificēšanai un montēšanai), šajā kolonnā ir UUID kā virkne."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:362
msgid "The UUID is only displayed if the I<--uuid> option is given."
msgstr "UUID tiek parādīts tikai tad, ja norādīta opcija I<--uuid>."

#. type: textblock
#: filesystems/virt-filesystems.pod:397
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-df(1)>, "
"L<virt-drivers(1)>, L<virt-list-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-list-partitions(1)>, "
"L<csvtool(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-df(1)>, L<virt-drivers"
"(1)>, L<virt-list-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-list-partitions(1)>, L<csvtool(1)>"
", L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:3
msgid "virt-format - Erase and make a blank disk"
msgstr "virt-format - izdzēst un izveidot tukšu disku"

#. type: verbatim
#: format/virt-format.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-format [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-format [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:11
msgid ""
"Virt-format takes an existing disk file (or it can be a host partition, LV "
"etc), B<erases all data on it>, and formats it as a blank disk.  It can "
"optionally create partition tables, empty filesystems, logical volumes and "
"more."
msgstr ""
"Virt-format ņem esošu diska failu (vai tas var būt resursdatora nodalījums, "
"LV u. c.), B<izdzēš visus tajā esošos datus> un formatē to kā tukšu disku.  "
"Pēc izvēles tas var izveidot nodalījumu tabulas, tukšas failu sistēmas, "
"loģiskos sējumus u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:16
msgid ""
"To create a disk containing data, you may be better to use "
"L<virt-make-fs(1)>.  If you are creating a blank disk to use in "
"L<guestfish(1)>, you should instead use the guestfish I<-N> option."
msgstr ""
"Lai izveidotu disku ar datiem, iespējams, labāk izmantot L<virt-make-fs(1)>"
".  Ja veidojat tukšu disku izmantošanai L<guestfish(1)>, tā vietā "
"izmantojiet guestfish opciju I<-N>."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:20
msgid "Normal usage would be something like this:"
msgstr "Parasti lietojums būtu apmēram šāds:"

#. type: verbatim
#: format/virt-format.pod:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-format -a disk.qcow\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-format -a disk.qcow\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:24
msgid "or this:"
msgstr "vai šāds:"

#. type: verbatim
#: format/virt-format.pod:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-format -a /dev/VG/LV\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-format -a /dev/VG/LV\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:28
msgid ""
"F<disk.qcow> or F</dev/VG/LV> must exist already.  B<Any data on these disks "
"will be erased by these commands>.  These commands will create a single "
"empty partition covering the whole disk, with no filesystem inside it."
msgstr ""
"F<disk.qcow> vai F</dev/VG/LV> jau jāeksistē.  B<Šīs komandas izdzēsīs visus "
"datus šajos diskos>.  Šīs komandas izveidos vienu tukšu nodalījumu visa "
"diska apjomā, bez failu sistēmas tajā."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:33
msgid ""
"Additional parameters can be used to control the creation of partitions, "
"filesystems, etc.  The most commonly used options are:"
msgstr ""
"Nodalījumu, failu sistēmu u. c. izveides vadībai var izmantot papildu "
"parametrus.  Visbiežāk izmantotās opcijas ir:"

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:38
msgid "B<--filesystem=[ext3|ntfs|vfat|...]>"
msgstr "B<--filesystem=[ext3|ntfs|vfat|...]>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:40
msgid "Create an empty filesystem (C<ext3>, C<ntfs> etc) inside the partition."
msgstr "Izveidot tukšu failu sistēmu (C<ext3>, C<ntfs> u. c.) nodalījumā."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:42
msgid "B<--lvm[=/dev/VG/LV]>"
msgstr "B<--lvm[=/dev/VG/LV]>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:44
msgid ""
"Create a Linux LVM2 logical volume on the disk.  When used with "
"I<--filesystem>, the filesystem is created inside the LV."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot diskā Linux LVM2 loģisko sējumu.  Kopā ar I<--filesystem> failu "
"sistēma tiek izveidota LV iekšpusē."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:49
msgid "For more information about these and other options, see L</OPTIONS> below."
msgstr "Plašāku informāciju par šīm un citām opcijām skatiet L</OPCIJAS> tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:52
msgid ""
"The format of the disk is normally auto-detected, but you can also force it "
"by using the I<--format> option (q.v.).  In situations where you do not "
"trust the existing content of the disk, then it is advisable to use this "
"option to avoid possible exploits."
msgstr ""
"Diska formāts parasti tiek noteikts automātiski, taču to var arī piespiest "
"ar opciju I<--format> (skatīt to).  Ja neuzticaties esošajam diska saturam, "
"ieteicams izmantot šo opciju, lai izvairītos no iespējamām ļaunprātīgām "
"izmantošanām."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:69
msgid "Add I<file>, a disk image, host partition, LV, external USB disk, etc."
msgstr ""
"Pievienot I<file> — diska attēlu, resursdatora nodalījumu, LV, ārēju USB "
"disku u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:74
msgid "B<Any existing data on the disk is erased.>"
msgstr "B<Visi diskā esošie dati tiek izdzēsti.>"

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:84
msgid "B<--filesystem=ext3|ntfs|vfat|...>"
msgstr "B<--filesystem=ext3|ntfs|vfat|...>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:86
msgid ""
"Create an empty filesystem of the specified type.  Many filesystem types are "
"supported by libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot norādītā tipa tukšu failu sistēmu.  Libguestfs atbalsta daudzus "
"failu sistēmu tipus."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:89
msgid "B<--filesystem=none>"
msgstr "B<--filesystem=none>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:91
msgid "Create no filesystem.  This is the default."
msgstr "Neveidot failu sistēmu.  Tas ir noklusējums."

#. type: verbatim
#: format/virt-format.pod:104
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-format --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-format --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: format/virt-format.pod:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-format --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-format --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:117 make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:191
msgid "B<--label=>LABEL"
msgstr "B<--label=>LABEL"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:119 make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:193
msgid "Set the filesystem label."
msgstr "Iestatīt failu sistēmas etiķeti."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:121
msgid "B<--lvm=/dev/I<VG>/I<LV>>"
msgstr "B<--lvm=/dev/I<VG>/I<LV>>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:123
msgid ""
"Create a Linux LVM2 logical volume called F</dev/I<VG>/I<LV>>.  You can "
"change the name of the volume group and logical volume."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot Linux LVM2 loģisko sējumu ar nosaukumu F</dev/I<VG>/I<LV>>.  Sējumu "
"grupas un loģiskā sējuma nosaukumu var mainīt."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:126
msgid "B<--lvm>"
msgstr "B<--lvm>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:128
msgid "Create a Linux LVM2 logical volume with the default name (F</dev/VG/LV>)."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot Linux LVM2 loģisko sējumu ar noklusējuma nosaukumu (F</dev/VG/LV>)."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:131
msgid "B<--lvm=none>"
msgstr "B<--lvm=none>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:133
msgid "Create no logical volume.  This is the default."
msgstr "Neveidot loģisko sējumu.  Tas ir noklusējums."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:135 make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:195
msgid "B<--partition>"
msgstr "B<--partition>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:137
msgid ""
"Create either an MBR or GPT partition covering the whole disk.  MBR is "
"chosen if the disk size is E<lt> 2 TB, GPT if E<ge> 2 TB."
msgstr ""
"Izveidot visa diska apjoma MBR vai GPT nodalījumu.  MBR tiek izvēlēts, ja "
"diska izmērs ir E<lt> 2 TB, GPT — ja E<ge> 2 TB."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:142
msgid "B<--partition=gpt>"
msgstr "B<--partition=gpt>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:144
msgid "Create a GPT partition."
msgstr "Izveidot GPT nodalījumu."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:146
msgid "B<--partition=mbr>"
msgstr "B<--partition=mbr>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:148
msgid "Create an MBR partition."
msgstr "Izveidot MBR nodalījumu."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:150
msgid "B<--partition=none>"
msgstr "B<--partition=none>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:152
msgid ""
"Create no partition table.  Note that Windows may not be able to see these "
"disks."
msgstr ""
"Neveidot nodalījumu tabulu.  Ņemiet vērā, ka Windows šos diskus var neredzēt."

#. type: =item
#: format/virt-format.pod:167
msgid "B<--wipe>"
msgstr "B<--wipe>"

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:169
msgid ""
"Normally virt-format does not wipe data from the disk (because that takes a "
"long time).  Thus if there is data on the disk, it is only hidden and "
"partially overwritten by virt-format, and it might be recovered by disk "
"editing tools."
msgstr ""
"Parasti virt-format neizdzēš datus no diska (jo tas aizņem ilgu laiku).  "
"Tāpēc, ja diskā ir dati, virt-format tos tikai paslēpj un daļēji pārraksta, "
"un tos var atgūt ar disku rediģēšanas rīkiem."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:174
msgid ""
"If you use this option, virt-format writes zeroes over the whole disk so "
"that previous data is not recoverable."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat šo opciju, virt-format visā diskā ieraksta nulles, lai "
"iepriekšējos datus nevarētu atgūt."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:185
msgid "This program returns C<0> on success, or C<1> on failure."
msgstr "Šī programma atgriež C<0>, ja izdevās, vai C<1>, ja neizdevās."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:189
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-make-fs(1)>, "
"L<virt-rescue(1)>, L<virt-resize(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-make-fs(1)>, "
"L<virt-rescue(1)>, L<virt-resize(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: format/virt-format.pod:203
msgid "Copyright (C) 2012 Red Hat Inc."
msgstr "Copyright (C) 2012 Red Hat Inc."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:3
msgid "virt-get-kernel - Extract kernel and ramdisk from guests"
msgstr "virt-get-kernel - izvilkt kodolu un ramdisk no viesiem"

#. type: verbatim
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-get-kernel [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-get-kernel [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-get-kernel [--options] -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-get-kernel [--options] -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:13
msgid "This program extracts the kernel and initramfs from a guest."
msgstr "Šī programma izvelk kodolu un initramfs no viesa."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:18
msgid ""
"In the case where the guest contains multiple kernels, the one with the "
"highest version number is chosen.  To extract arbitrary kernels from the "
"disk image, see L<guestfish(1)>.  To extract the entire C</boot> directory "
"of a guest, see L<virt-copy-out(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Ja viesī ir vairāki kodoli, tiek izvēlēts tas, kuram ir lielākais versijas "
"numurs.  Patvaļīgu kodolu izvilkšanai no diska attēla skatiet L<guestfish(1)>"
".  Visas viesa direktorijas C</boot> izvilkšanai skatiet L<virt-copy-out(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:112
msgid "B<-o> directory"
msgstr "B<-o> directory"

#. type: =item
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:114
msgid "B<--output> directory"
msgstr "B<--output> directory"

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:116
msgid ""
"This option specifies the output directory where kernel and initramfs from "
"the guest are written."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija norāda izvades direktoriju, kurā tiek ierakstīts viesa kodols un "
"initramfs."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:119
msgid "If not specified, the default output is the current directory."
msgstr "Ja nav norādīta, noklusējuma izvade ir pašreizējā direktorija."

#. type: =item
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:121
msgid "B<--prefix> prefix"
msgstr "B<--prefix> prefix"

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:123
msgid "This option specifies a prefix for the extracted files."
msgstr "Šī opcija norāda izvilkto failu priedēkli."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:125
msgid ""
"If a prefix is specified, then there will be a dash (C<->) after the prefix "
"and before the rest of the file name; for example, a kernel in the guest "
"like C<vmlinuz-3.19.0-20-generic> is saved as "
"C<mydistro-vmlinuz-3.19.0-20-generic> when the prefix is C<mydistro>."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādīts priedēklis, pēc priedēkļa un pirms pārējā faila nosaukuma būs "
"defise (C<->); piemēram, viesa kodols C<vmlinuz-3.19.0-20-generic> tiek "
"saglabāts kā C<mydistro-vmlinuz-3.19.0-20-generic>, ja priedēklis ir "
"C<mydistro>."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:130
msgid "See also I<--unversioned-names>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī I<--unversioned-names>."

#. type: =item
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:138
msgid "B<--unversioned-names>"
msgstr "B<--unversioned-names>"

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:140
msgid "This option affects the destination file name of extracted files."
msgstr "Šī opcija ietekmē izvilkto failu mērķa faila nosaukumu."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:142
msgid ""
"If enabled, files will be saved locally just with the base name; for "
"example, kernel and ramdisk in the guest like C<vmlinuz-3.19.0-20-generic> "
"and C<initrd.img-3.19.0-20-generic> are saved respectively as C<vmlinuz> and "
"C<initrd.img>."
msgstr ""
"Ja iespējota, faili tiks saglabāti lokāli tikai ar bāzes nosaukumu; "
"piemēram, viesa kodols un ramdisk C<vmlinuz-3.19.0-20-generic> un "
"C<initrd.img-3.19.0-20-generic> tiek saglabāti attiecīgi kā C<vmlinuz> un "
"C<initrd.img>."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:147
msgid "See also I<--prefix>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī I<--prefix>."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:175
msgid ""
"The I<--machine-readable> option can be used to make the output more machine "
"friendly, which is useful when calling virt-get-kernel from other programs, "
"GUIs etc."
msgstr ""
"Opciju I<--machine-readable> var izmantot, lai padarītu izvadi ērtāku "
"mašīnapstrādei, kas noder, izsaucot virt-get-kernel no citām programmām, "
"grafiskām saskarnēm u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:179
msgid ""
"Use the option on its own to query the capabilities of the virt-get-kernel "
"binary.  Typical output looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet opciju vienu pašu, lai noskaidrotu virt-get-kernel binārā faila "
"spējas.  Tipiska izvade izskatās šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-get-kernel --machine-readable\n"
" virt-get-kernel\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-get-kernel --machine-readable\n"
" virt-get-kernel\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:203
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestmount(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-drivers(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<guestmount(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-drivers(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: get-kernel/virt-get-kernel.pod:216
msgid "Copyright (C) 2013-2025 Red Hat Inc."
msgstr "Copyright (C) 2013-2025 Red Hat Inc."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:3
msgid ""
"virt-inspector - Display operating system version and other information "
"about a virtual machine"
msgstr ""
"virt-inspector - parādīt virtuālās mašīnas operētājsistēmas versiju un citu "
"informāciju"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:15 inspector/virt-inspector.pod:169
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector disk.img [disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector disk.img [disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:19
msgid ""
"B<virt-inspector> examines a virtual machine or disk image and tries to "
"determine the version of the operating system and other information about "
"the virtual machine."
msgstr ""
"B<virt-inspector> pārbauda virtuālo mašīnu vai diska attēlu un mēģina "
"noteikt operētājsistēmas versiju un citu informāciju par virtuālo mašīnu."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:23
msgid "Virt-inspector produces XML output for feeding into other programs."
msgstr "Virt-inspector rada XML izvadi padošanai citām programmām."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:25
msgid ""
"In the normal usage, use C<virt-inspector -d domname> where C<domname> is "
"the libvirt domain (see: C<virsh list --all>)."
msgstr ""
"Parasti izmantojiet C<virt-inspector -d domname>, kur C<domname> ir libvirt "
"domēns (skatiet: C<virsh list --all>)."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:28
msgid ""
"You can also run virt-inspector directly on disk images from a single "
"virtual machine.  Use C<virt-inspector -a disk.img>.  In rare cases a domain "
"has several block devices, in which case you should list several I<-a> "
"options one after another, with the first corresponding to the guest’s "
"F</dev/sda>, the second to the guest’s F</dev/sdb> and so on."
msgstr ""
"Virt-inspector var palaist arī tieši ar vienas virtuālās mašīnas disku "
"attēliem.  Izmantojiet C<virt-inspector -a disk.img>.  Retos gadījumos "
"domēnam ir vairākas bloku ierīces — tad jānorāda vairākas opcijas I<-a> "
"viena pēc otras, pirmajai atbilstot viesa F</dev/sda>, otrajai — viesa F</"
"dev/sdb> u. tml."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:35
msgid ""
"You can also run virt-inspector on install disks, live CDs, bootable USB "
"keys and similar."
msgstr ""
"Virt-inspector var palaist arī ar instalēšanas diskiem, Live CD, sāknējamām "
"USB atmiņām u. tml."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:38
msgid ""
"Virt-inspector can only inspect and report upon I<one domain at a time>.  To "
"inspect several virtual machines, you have to run virt-inspector several "
"times (for example, from a shell script for-loop)."
msgstr ""
"Virt-inspector var inspicēt un ziņot tikai par I<vienu domēnu vienlaikus>.  "
"Lai inspicētu vairākas virtuālās mašīnas, virt-inspector jāpalaiž vairākkārt "
"(piemēram, no čaulas skripta for cikla)."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:43
msgid ""
"Because virt-inspector needs direct access to guest images, it won’t "
"normally work over remote libvirt connections."
msgstr ""
"Tā kā virt-inspector vajadzīga tieša piekļuve viesu attēliem, tas parasti "
"nedarbosies caur attāliem libvirt savienojumiem."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:46
msgid ""
"All of the information available from virt-inspector is also available "
"through the core libguestfs inspection API (see L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION>).  "
"The same information can also be fetched using guestfish or via libguestfs "
"bindings in many programming languages (see L</GETTING INSPECTION DATA FROM "
"THE LIBGUESTFS API>)."
msgstr ""
"Visa virt-inspector pieejamā informācija ir pieejama arī caur libguestfs "
"pamata inspicēšanas API (skatiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>).  To pašu "
"informāciju var iegūt arī ar guestfish vai caur libguestfs saistījumiem "
"daudzās programmēšanas valodās (skatiet L</INSPICĒŠANAS DATU IEGŪŠANA NO "
"LIBGUESTFS API>)."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:52
msgid ""
"Additional information about bootloader, kernel and drivers inside a guest "
"can be found using L<virt-drivers(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Papildu informāciju par sāknētāju, kodolu un draiveriem viesī var atrast ar "
"L<virt-drivers(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:89
msgid ""
"Libvirt is only used if you specify a C<domname> on the command line.  If "
"you specify guest block devices directly (I<-a>), then libvirt is not used "
"at all."
msgstr ""
"Libvirt tiek izmantots tikai tad, ja komandrindā norādāt C<domname>.  Ja "
"viesa bloku ierīces norādāt tieši (I<-a>), libvirt netiek izmantots vispār."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:102
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, virt-inspector normally turns "
"echoing off so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried "
"about Tempest attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify "
"this flag to see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, virt-inspector parasti izslēdz "
"atbalsi, lai nevarētu redzēt, ko rakstāt.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest "
"uzbrukumiem un telpā neviena cita nav, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu, "
"ko rakstāt."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:111 win-reg/virt-win-reg.in:141
msgid ""
"Specify the format of disk images given on the command line.  If this is "
"omitted then the format is autodetected from the content of the disk image."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt komandrindā doto disku attēlu formātu.  Ja tas izlaists, formāts "
"tiek automātiski noteikts no diska attēla satura."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:115 win-reg/virt-win-reg.in:145
msgid ""
"If disk images are requested from libvirt, then this program asks libvirt "
"for this information.  In this case, the value of the format parameter is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"Ja disku attēli tiek pieprasīti no libvirt, šī programma prasa šo "
"informāciju libvirt.  Šajā gadījumā formāta parametra vērtība tiek ignorēta."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:119 resize/virt-resize.pod:424
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:522 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:209
#: win-reg/virt-win-reg.in:149
msgid ""
"If working with untrusted raw-format guest disk images, you should ensure "
"the format is always specified."
msgstr ""
"Strādājot ar neuzticamiem raw formāta viesu disku attēliem, nodrošiniet, ka "
"formāts vienmēr ir norādīts."

#. type: =item
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:126
msgid "B<--no-applications>"
msgstr "B<--no-applications>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:128
msgid ""
"By default the output of virt-inspector includes the list of all the "
"applications installed in the guest, if available."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma virt-inspector izvadē ir viesī instalēto lietotņu saraksts, "
"ja tas ir pieejams."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:131 inspector/virt-inspector.pod:138
msgid "Specify this option to disable this part of the resulting XML."
msgstr "Norādiet šo opciju, lai atspējotu šo iegūtā XML daļu."

#. type: =item
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:133
msgid "B<--no-icon>"
msgstr "B<--no-icon>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:135
msgid ""
"By default the output of virt-inspector includes the icon of the guest, if "
"available (see L</icon>)."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma virt-inspector izvadē ir viesa ikona, ja tā ir pieejama "
"(skatiet L</icon>)."

#. type: =item
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:156
msgid "B<--xpath> query"
msgstr "B<--xpath> query"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:158
msgid ""
"Perform an XPath query on the XML on stdin, and print the result on stdout.  "
"In this mode virt-inspector simply runs an XPath query; all other inspection "
"functions are disabled.  See L</XPATH QUERIES> below for some examples."
msgstr ""
"Veikt XPath vaicājumu standartievades XML un izdrukāt rezultātu "
"standartizvadē.  Šajā režīmā virt-inspector tikai izpilda XPath vaicājumu; "
"visas pārējās inspicēšanas funkcijas ir atspējotas.  Dažus piemērus skatiet "
"L</XPATH VAICĀJUMI> tālāk."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:167
msgid "Previous versions of virt-inspector allowed you to write either:"
msgstr "Iepriekšējās virt-inspector versijas ļāva rakstīt gan:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector guestname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector guestname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:183
msgid ""
"The virt-inspector XML is described precisely in a RELAX NG schema file "
"F<virt-inspector.rng> which is supplied with libguestfs.  This section is "
"just an overview."
msgstr ""
"Virt-inspector XML ir precīzi aprakstīts RELAX NG shēmas failā F<virt-"
"inspector.rng>, kas tiek piegādāts kopā ar libguestfs.  Šī sadaļa ir tikai "
"pārskats."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:187
msgid ""
"The top-level element is E<lt>operatingsystemsE<gt>, and it contains one or "
"more E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt> elements.  You would only see more than one "
"E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt> element if the virtual machine is multi-boot, "
"which is vanishingly rare in real world VMs."
msgstr ""
"Augšējā līmeņa elements ir E<lt>operatingsystemsE<gt>, un tas satur vienu "
"vai vairākus elementus E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt>.  Vairāk nekā vienu "
"elementu E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt> jūs redzētu tikai tad, ja virtuālā mašīna "
"ir ar vairāku OS sāknēšanu, kas reālās VM ir ārkārtīgi reti."

#. type: =head2
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:192
msgid "E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:194
msgid ""
"In the E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt> tag are various optional fields that "
"describe the operating system, its architecture, the descriptive \"product "
"name\" string, the type of OS and so on, as in this example:"
msgstr ""
"Tagā E<lt>operatingsystemE<gt> ir dažādi neobligāti lauki, kas apraksta "
"operētājsistēmu, tās arhitektūru, aprakstošo „produkta nosaukuma” virkni, OS "
"tipu u. c., kā šajā piemērā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:198
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>windows</name>\n"
"     <arch>i386</arch>\n"
"     <distro>windows</distro>\n"
"     <product_name>Windows 7 Enterprise</product_name>\n"
"     <product_variant>Client</product_variant>\n"
"     <major_version>6</major_version>\n"
"     <minor_version>1</minor_version>\n"
"     <windows_systemroot>/Windows</windows_systemroot>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     <root>/dev/sda2</root>\n"
"     <name>windows</name>\n"
"     <arch>i386</arch>\n"
"     <distro>windows</distro>\n"
"     <product_name>Windows 7 Enterprise</product_name>\n"
"     <product_variant>Client</product_variant>\n"
"     <major_version>6</major_version>\n"
"     <minor_version>1</minor_version>\n"
"     <windows_systemroot>/Windows</windows_systemroot>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:210
msgid ""
"In brief, E<lt>nameE<gt> is the class of operating system (something like "
"C<linux> or C<windows>), E<lt>distroE<gt> is the distribution (eg. C<fedora> "
"but many other distros are recognized) and E<lt>archE<gt> is the guest "
"architecture.  The other fields are fairly self-explanatory, but because "
"these fields are taken directly from the libguestfs inspection API you can "
"find precise information from L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION>."
msgstr ""
"Īsumā: E<lt>nameE<gt> ir operētājsistēmas klase (kaut kas līdzīgs C<linux> "
"vai C<windows>), E<lt>distroE<gt> ir distribūcija (piem., C<fedora>, bet "
"tiek atpazītas arī daudzas citas) un E<lt>archE<gt> ir viesa arhitektūra.  "
"Pārējie lauki ir diezgan pašsaprotami, taču, tā kā šie lauki ņemti tieši no "
"libguestfs inspicēšanas API, precīzu informāciju var atrast L<guestfs(3)/"
"INSPICĒŠANA>."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:218
msgid ""
"The E<lt>rootE<gt> element is the root filesystem device, but from the point "
"of view of libguestfs (block devices may have completely different names "
"inside the VM itself)."
msgstr ""
"Elements E<lt>rootE<gt> ir saknes failu sistēmas ierīce, taču no libguestfs "
"skatpunkta (pašā VM bloku ierīcēm var būt pavisam citi nosaukumi)."

#. type: =head2
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:222
msgid "E<lt>mountpointsE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>mountpointsE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:224
msgid ""
"Un*x-like guests typically have multiple filesystems which are mounted at "
"various mountpoints, and these are described in the E<lt>mountpointsE<gt> "
"element which looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Un*x līdzīgiem viesiem parasti ir vairākas failu sistēmas, kas montētas "
"dažādos montēšanas punktos, un tās aprakstītas elementā E<lt>mountpointsE<gt>"
", kas izskatās šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:228
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <mountpoints>\n"
"       <mountpoint dev=\"/dev/vg_f13x64/lv_root\">/</mountpoint>\n"
"       <mountpoint dev=\"/dev/sda1\">/boot</mountpoint>\n"
"     </mountpoints>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <mountpoints>\n"
"       <mountpoint dev=\"/dev/vg_f13x64/lv_root\">/</mountpoint>\n"
"       <mountpoint dev=\"/dev/sda1\">/boot</mountpoint>\n"
"     </mountpoints>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:236
msgid ""
"As with E<lt>rootE<gt>, devices are from the point of view of libguestfs, "
"and may have completely different names inside the guest.  Only mountable "
"filesystems appear in this list, not things like swap devices."
msgstr ""
"Tāpat kā ar E<lt>rootE<gt>, ierīces ir no libguestfs skatpunkta, un viesī "
"tām var būt pavisam citi nosaukumi.  Šajā sarakstā parādās tikai montējamas "
"failu sistēmas, nevis, piemēram, maiņatmiņas ierīces."

#. type: =head2
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:241
msgid "E<lt>filesystemsE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>filesystemsE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:243
msgid ""
"E<lt>filesystemsE<gt> is like E<lt>mountpointsE<gt> but covers I<all> "
"filesystems belonging to the guest, including swap and empty partitions.  "
"(In the rare case of a multi-boot guest, it covers filesystems belonging to "
"this OS or shared with this OS and other OSes)."
msgstr ""
"E<lt>filesystemsE<gt> ir līdzīgs E<lt>mountpointsE<gt>, taču aptver I<visas> "
"viesim piederošās failu sistēmas, ieskaitot maiņatmiņu un tukšus "
"nodalījumus.  (Retajā vairāku OS sāknēšanas viesa gadījumā tas aptver šai OS "
"piederošas vai ar šo un citām OS kopīgas failu sistēmas.)"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:249
msgid "You might see something like this:"
msgstr "Jūs varētu redzēt kaut ko līdzīgu šim:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:251
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <filesystems>\n"
"       <filesystem dev=\"/dev/vg_f13x64/lv_root\">\n"
"         <type>ext4</type>\n"
"         <label>Fedora-13-x86_64</label>\n"
"         <uuid>e6a4db1e-15c2-477b-ac2a-699181c396aa</uuid>\n"
"       </filesystem>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <filesystems>\n"
"       <filesystem dev=\"/dev/vg_f13x64/lv_root\">\n"
"         <type>ext4</type>\n"
"         <label>Fedora-13-x86_64</label>\n"
"         <uuid>e6a4db1e-15c2-477b-ac2a-699181c396aa</uuid>\n"
"       </filesystem>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:261
msgid ""
"The optional elements within E<lt>filesystemE<gt> are the filesystem type, "
"the label, and the UUID."
msgstr ""
"Neobligātie elementi E<lt>filesystemE<gt> iekšpusē ir failu sistēmas tips, "
"etiķete un UUID."

#. type: =head2
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:264
msgid "E<lt>applicationsE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>applicationsE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:266
msgid ""
"The related elements E<lt>package_formatE<gt>, E<lt>package_managementE<gt> "
"and E<lt>applicationsE<gt> describe applications installed in the virtual "
"machine."
msgstr ""
"Saistītie elementi E<lt>package_formatE<gt>, E<lt>package_managementE<gt> un "
"E<lt>applicationsE<gt> apraksta virtuālajā mašīnā instalētās lietotnes."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:270
msgid ""
"E<lt>package_formatE<gt>, if present, describes the packaging system used.  "
"Typical values would be C<rpm> and C<deb>."
msgstr ""
"E<lt>package_formatE<gt>, ja ir, apraksta izmantoto pakošanas sistēmu.  "
"Tipiskas vērtības būtu C<rpm> un C<deb>."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:273
msgid ""
"E<lt>package_managementE<gt>, if present, describes the package manager.  "
"Typical values include C<yum>, C<up2date> and C<apt>"
msgstr ""
"E<lt>package_managementE<gt>, ja ir, apraksta pakotņu pārvaldnieku.  "
"Tipiskas vērtības ir C<yum>, C<up2date> un C<apt>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:276
msgid "E<lt>applicationsE<gt> lists the packages or applications installed."
msgstr "E<lt>applicationsE<gt> uzskaita instalētās pakotnes vai lietotnes."

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:279
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <applications>\n"
"       <application>\n"
"         <name>coreutils</name>\n"
"         <version>8.5</version>\n"
"         <release>1</release>\n"
"       </application>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <applications>\n"
"       <application>\n"
"         <name>coreutils</name>\n"
"         <version>8.5</version>\n"
"         <release>1</release>\n"
"       </application>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:289
msgid ""
"The version and release fields may not be available for some types guests.  "
"Other fields are possible, see "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_inspect_list_applications>."
msgstr ""
"Dažu tipu viesiem versijas un laidiena lauki var nebūt pieejami.  Iespējami "
"arī citi lauki, skatiet L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_inspect_list_applications>."

#. type: =head2
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:293
msgid "E<lt>drive_mappingsE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>drive_mappingsE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:295
msgid ""
"For operating systems like Windows which use drive letters, virt-inspector "
"is able to find out how drive letters map to filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Operētājsistēmām, piemēram, Windows, kas izmanto disku burtus, virt-"
"inspector spēj noskaidrot, kā disku burti atbilst failu sistēmām."

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:299
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <drive_mappings>\n"
"       <drive_mapping name=\"C\">/dev/sda2</drive_mapping>\n"
"       <drive_mapping name=\"E\">/dev/sdb1</drive_mapping>\n"
"     </drive_mappings>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <drive_mappings>\n"
"       <drive_mapping name=\"C\">/dev/sda2</drive_mapping>\n"
"       <drive_mapping name=\"E\">/dev/sdb1</drive_mapping>\n"
"     </drive_mappings>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:307
msgid ""
"In the example above, drive C maps to the filesystem on the second partition "
"on the first disk, and drive E maps to the filesystem on the first partition "
"on the second disk."
msgstr ""
"Iepriekšējā piemērā disks C atbilst failu sistēmai pirmā diska otrajā "
"nodalījumā, bet disks E — failu sistēmai otrā diska pirmajā nodalījumā."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:311
msgid ""
"Note that this only covers permanent local filesystem mappings, not things "
"like network shares.  Furthermore NTFS volume mount points may not be listed "
"here."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka tas aptver tikai pastāvīgos lokālos failu sistēmu "
"kartējumus, nevis, piemēram, tīkla koplietojumus.  Turklāt NTFS sējumu "
"montēšanas punkti šeit var nebūt uzskaitīti."

#. type: =head2
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:315
msgid "E<lt>iconE<gt>"
msgstr "E<lt>iconE<gt>"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:317
msgid ""
"Virt-inspector is sometimes able to extract an icon or logo for the guest.  "
"The icon is returned as base64-encoded PNG data.  Note that the icon can be "
"very large and high quality."
msgstr ""
"Virt-inspector dažreiz spēj izvilkt viesa ikonu vai logotipu.  Ikona tiek "
"atgriezta kā base64 kodēti PNG dati.  Ņemiet vērā, ka ikona var būt ļoti "
"liela un augstas kvalitātes."

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:321
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <icon>\n"
"       iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAGAAAABg[.......]\n"
"       [... many lines of base64 data ...]\n"
"     </icon>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" <operatingsystems>\n"
"   <operatingsystem>\n"
"     ...\n"
"     <icon>\n"
"       iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAGAAAABg[.......]\n"
"       [... many lines of base64 data ...]\n"
"     </icon>\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:329
msgid ""
"To display the icon, you have to extract it and convert the base64 data back "
"to a binary file.  Use an XPath query or simply an editor to extract the "
"data, then use the coreutils L<base64(1)> program to do the conversion back "
"to a PNG file:"
msgstr ""
"Lai parādītu ikonu, tā jāizvelk un base64 dati jāpārveido atpakaļ binārā "
"failā.  Datu izvilkšanai izmantojiet XPath vaicājumu vai vienkārši "
"redaktoru, pēc tam ar coreutils programmu L<base64(1)> pārveidojiet atpakaļ "
"PNG failā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:334
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" base64 -i -d < icon.data > icon.png\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" base64 -i -d < icon.data > icon.png\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:336
msgid "XPATH QUERIES"
msgstr "XPATH VAICĀJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:338
msgid ""
"Virt-inspector includes built in support for running XPath queries.  The "
"reason for including XPath support directly in virt-inspector is simply that "
"there are no good and widely available command line programs that can do "
"XPath queries.  The only good one is L<xmlstarlet(1)> and that is not "
"available on Red Hat Enterprise Linux."
msgstr ""
"Virt-inspector ir iebūvēts XPath vaicājumu izpildes atbalsts.  XPath "
"atbalsts iekļauts tieši virt-inspector vienkārši tāpēc, ka nav labu un plaši "
"pieejamu komandrindas programmu, kas var izpildīt XPath vaicājumus.  Vienīgā "
"labā ir L<xmlstarlet(1)>, un tā nav pieejama Red Hat Enterprise Linux."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:345
msgid ""
"To perform an XPath query, use the I<--xpath> option.  Note that in this "
"mode, virt-inspector simply reads XML from stdin and outputs the query "
"result on stdout.  All other inspection features are disabled in this mode."
msgstr ""
"Lai izpildītu XPath vaicājumu, izmantojiet opciju I<--xpath>.  Ņemiet vērā, "
"ka šajā režīmā virt-inspector tikai nolasa XML no standartievades un izvada "
"vaicājuma rezultātu standartizvadē.  Šajā režīmā visi pārējie inspicēšanas "
"līdzekļi ir atspējoti."

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:352
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-inspector -d Guest | virt-inspector --xpath '//filesystems'\n"
" <filesystems>\n"
"      <filesystem dev=\"/dev/vg_f13x64/lv_root\">\n"
"        <type>ext4</type>\n"
" [...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-inspector -d Guest | virt-inspector --xpath '//filesystems'\n"
" <filesystems>\n"
"      <filesystem dev=\"/dev/vg_f13x64/lv_root\">\n"
"        <type>ext4</type>\n"
" [...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:358
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-inspector -d Guest | \\\n"
"     virt-inspector --xpath "
"\"string(//filesystem[@dev='/dev/sda1']/type)\"\n"
" ext4\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-inspector -d Guest | \\\n"
"     virt-inspector --xpath \"string(//filesystem[@dev='/dev/sda1']/type)\"\n"
" ext4\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:362
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-inspector -d Guest | \\\n"
"     virt-inspector --xpath 'string(//icon)' | base64 -i -d | display -\n"
" [displays the guest icon, if there is one]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-inspector -d Guest | \\\n"
"     virt-inspector --xpath 'string(//icon)' | base64 -i -d | display -\n"
" [displays the guest icon, if there is one]\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:366
msgid "GETTING INSPECTION DATA FROM THE LIBGUESTFS API"
msgstr "INSPICĒŠANAS DATU IEGŪŠANA NO LIBGUESTFS API"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:368
msgid ""
"In early versions of libguestfs, virt-inspector was a large Perl script that "
"contained many heuristics for inspecting guests.  This had several problems: "
"in order to do inspection from other tools (like guestfish) we had to call "
"out to this Perl script; and it privileged Perl over other languages that "
"libguestfs supports."
msgstr ""
"Agrīnās libguestfs versijās virt-inspector bija liels Perl skripts ar "
"daudzām heiristikām viesu inspicēšanai.  Tam bija vairākas problēmas: lai "
"veiktu inspicēšanu no citiem rīkiem (piemēram, guestfish), bija jāizsauc šis "
"Perl skripts; un tas deva priekšroku Perl pār citām libguestfs atbalstītajām "
"valodām."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:374
msgid ""
"By libguestfs 1.8 we had rewritten the Perl code in C, and incorporated it "
"all into the core libguestfs API (L<guestfs(3)>).  Now virt-inspector is "
"simply a thin C program over the core C API.  All of the inspection "
"information is available from all programming languages that libguestfs "
"supports, and from guestfish."
msgstr ""
"Līdz libguestfs 1.8 mēs Perl kodu bijām pārrakstījuši C valodā un visu "
"iekļāvuši libguestfs pamata API (L<guestfs(3)>).  Tagad virt-inspector ir "
"tikai plāna C programma virs pamata C API.  Visa inspicēšanas informācija ir "
"pieejama no visām libguestfs atbalstītajām programmēšanas valodām un no "
"guestfish."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:380
msgid "For a description of the C inspection API, read L<guestfs(3)/INSPECTION>."
msgstr "C inspicēšanas API aprakstu lasiet L<guestfs(3)/INSPICĒŠANA>."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:383
msgid ""
"For example code using the C inspection API, look for F<inspect-vm.c> which "
"ships with libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Koda piemēru ar C inspicēšanas API meklējiet failā F<inspect-vm.c>, kas tiek "
"piegādāts ar libguestfs."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:386
msgid ""
"F<inspect-vm.c> has also been translated into other languages.  For example, "
"F<inspect_vm.pl> is the Perl translation, and there are other translations "
"for OCaml, Python, etc.  See L<guestfs(3)/USING LIBGUESTFS WITH OTHER "
"PROGRAMMING LANGUAGES> for a list of man pages which contain this example "
"code."
msgstr ""
"F<inspect-vm.c> ir tulkots arī citās valodās.  Piemēram, F<inspect_vm.pl> ir "
"Perl tulkojums, un ir arī citi tulkojumi OCaml, Python u. c.  Rokasgrāmatas "
"lapu sarakstu ar šo koda piemēru skatiet L<guestfs(3)/LIBGUESTFS IZMANTOŠANA "
"AR CITĀM PROGRAMMĒŠANAS VALODĀM>."

#. type: =head2
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:392
msgid "GETTING INSPECTION DATA FROM GUESTFISH"
msgstr "INSPICĒŠANAS DATU IEGŪŠANA NO GUESTFISH"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:394
msgid ""
"If you use the guestfish I<-i> option, then the main C inspection API "
"L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_inspect_os> is called.  This is equivalent to the "
"guestfish command C<inspect-os>.  You can also call this guestfish command "
"by hand."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat guestfish opciju I<-i>, tiek izsaukts galvenais C inspicēšanas "
"API L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_inspect_os>.  Tas ir līdzvērtīgs guestfish komandai "
"C<inspect-os>.  Šo guestfish komandu var izsaukt arī manuāli."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:399
msgid ""
"C<inspect-os> performs inspection on the current disk image, returning the "
"list of operating systems found.  Each OS is represented by its root "
"filesystem device.  In the majority of cases, this command prints nothing "
"(no OSes found), or a single root device, but beware that it can print "
"multiple lines if there are multiple OSes or if there is an install CD "
"attached to the guest."
msgstr ""
"C<inspect-os> veic pašreizējā diska attēla inspicēšanu, atgriežot atrasto "
"operētājsistēmu sarakstu.  Katru OS attēlo tās saknes failu sistēmas "
"ierīce.  Vairumā gadījumu šī komanda neizdrukā neko (OS nav atrastas) vai "
"vienu saknes ierīci, taču ņemiet vērā, ka tā var izdrukāt vairākas rindas, "
"ja ir vairākas OS vai ja viesim ir pievienots instalēšanas CD."

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:406
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ guestfish --ro -a F15x32.img\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" ><fs> inspect-os\n"
" /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ guestfish --ro -a F15x32.img\n"
" ><fs> run\n"
" ><fs> inspect-os\n"
" /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:411
msgid "Using the root device, you can fetch further information about the guest:"
msgstr "Izmantojot saknes ierīci, var iegūt papildu informāciju par viesi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:414
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> inspect-get-type /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" linux\n"
" ><fs> inspect-get-distro /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" fedora\n"
" ><fs> inspect-get-major-version /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" 15\n"
" ><fs> inspect-get-product-name /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" Fedora release 15 (Lovelock)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> inspect-get-type /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" linux\n"
" ><fs> inspect-get-distro /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" fedora\n"
" ><fs> inspect-get-major-version /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" 15\n"
" ><fs> inspect-get-product-name /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" Fedora release 15 (Lovelock)\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:423
msgid ""
"Limitations of guestfish make it hard to assign the root device to a "
"variable (since guestfish doesn't have variables), so if you want to do this "
"reproducibly you are better off writing a script using one of the other "
"languages that the libguestfs API supports."
msgstr ""
"Guestfish ierobežojumi apgrūtina saknes ierīces piešķiršanu mainīgajam (jo "
"guestfish nav mainīgo), tāpēc, ja vēlaties to darīt atkārtojami, labāk "
"uzrakstiet skriptu kādā no citām libguestfs API atbalstītajām valodām."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:428
msgid "To list applications, you have to first mount up the disks:"
msgstr "Lai uzskaitītu lietotnes, vispirms jāmontē diski:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:430
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> inspect-get-mountpoints /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" /: /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" /boot: /dev/vda1\n"
" ><fs> mount-ro /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root /\n"
" ><fs> mount-ro /dev/vda1 /boot\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> inspect-get-mountpoints /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" /: /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root\n"
" /boot: /dev/vda1\n"
" ><fs> mount-ro /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root /\n"
" ><fs> mount-ro /dev/vda1 /boot\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:436
msgid "and then call the inspect-list-applications API:"
msgstr "un tad jāizsauc API inspect-list-applications:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:438
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> inspect-list-applications /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root | head -28\n"
" [0] = {\n"
"   app_name: ConsoleKit\n"
"   app_display_name:\n"
"   app_epoch: 0\n"
"   app_version: 0.4.5\n"
"   app_release: 1.fc15\n"
"   app_install_path:\n"
"   app_trans_path:\n"
"   app_publisher:\n"
"   app_url:\n"
"   app_source_package:\n"
"   app_summary:\n"
"   app_description:\n"
" }\n"
" [1] = {\n"
"   app_name: ConsoleKit-libs\n"
"   app_display_name:\n"
"   app_epoch: 0\n"
"   app_version: 0.4.5\n"
"   app_release: 1.fc15\n"
"   app_install_path:\n"
"   app_trans_path:\n"
"   app_publisher:\n"
"   app_url:\n"
"   app_source_package:\n"
"   app_summary:\n"
"   app_description:\n"
" }\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> inspect-list-applications /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root | head -28\n"
" [0] = {\n"
"   app_name: ConsoleKit\n"
"   app_display_name:\n"
"   app_epoch: 0\n"
"   app_version: 0.4.5\n"
"   app_release: 1.fc15\n"
"   app_install_path:\n"
"   app_trans_path:\n"
"   app_publisher:\n"
"   app_url:\n"
"   app_source_package:\n"
"   app_summary:\n"
"   app_description:\n"
" }\n"
" [1] = {\n"
"   app_name: ConsoleKit-libs\n"
"   app_display_name:\n"
"   app_epoch: 0\n"
"   app_version: 0.4.5\n"
"   app_release: 1.fc15\n"
"   app_install_path:\n"
"   app_trans_path:\n"
"   app_publisher:\n"
"   app_url:\n"
"   app_source_package:\n"
"   app_summary:\n"
"   app_description:\n"
" }\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:468
msgid ""
"To display an icon for the guest, note that filesystems must also be mounted "
"as above.  You can then do:"
msgstr ""
"Lai parādītu viesa ikonu, ņemiet vērā, ka arī failu sistēmām jābūt montētām, "
"kā iepriekš.  Tad varat izpildīt:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:471
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ><fs> inspect-get-icon /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root | display -\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ><fs> inspect-get-icon /dev/vg_f15x32/lv_root | display -\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:473
msgid "OLD VERSIONS OF VIRT-INSPECTOR"
msgstr "VECAS VIRT-INSPECTOR VERSIJAS"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:475
msgid ""
"As described above, early versions of libguestfs shipped with a different "
"virt-inspector program written in Perl (the current version is written in "
"C).  The XML output of the Perl virt-inspector was different and it could "
"also output in other formats like text."
msgstr ""
"Kā aprakstīts iepriekš, agrīnās libguestfs versijas tika piegādātas ar citu, "
"Perl rakstītu virt-inspector programmu (pašreizējā versija ir rakstīta C).  "
"Perl virt-inspector XML izvade bija atšķirīga, un tas varēja izvadīt arī "
"citos formātos, piemēram, tekstā."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:480
msgid "The old virt-inspector is no longer supported or shipped with libguestfs."
msgstr ""
"Vecais virt-inspector vairs netiek atbalstīts vai piegādāts ar libguestfs."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:483
msgid ""
"To confuse matters further, in Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6 we ship two "
"versions of virt-inspector with different names:"
msgstr ""
"Lai situāciju sarežģītu vēl vairāk, Red Hat Enterprise Linux 6 piegādājam "
"divas virt-inspector versijas ar atšķirīgiem nosaukumiem:"

#. type: verbatim
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:486
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-inspector     Old Perl version.\n"
" virt-inspector2    New C version.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-inspector     Old Perl version.\n"
" virt-inspector2    New C version.\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:496
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<http://www.w3.org/TR/xpath/>, "
"L<base64(1)>, L<xmlstarlet(1)>, L<virt-drivers(1)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<http://www.w3.org/TR/xpath/>, L<base64(1)>"
", L<xmlstarlet(1)>, L<virt-drivers(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: inspector/virt-inspector.pod:514
msgid "Matthew Booth L<mbooth@redhat.com>"
msgstr "Matthew Booth L<mbooth@redhat.com>"

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:3
msgid "virt-log - Display log files from a virtual machine"
msgstr "virt-log - parādīt žurnālu failus no virtuālās mašīnas"

#. type: verbatim
#: log/virt-log.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-log [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-log [--options] -d domname\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: log/virt-log.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-log [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-log [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:13
msgid ""
"C<virt-log> is a command line tool to display the log files from the named "
"virtual machine (or disk image)."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-log> ir komandrindas rīks, kas parāda nosauktās virtuālās mašīnas "
"(vai diska attēla) žurnālu failus."

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:16
msgid ""
"This tool understands and displays both plain text log files "
"(eg. F</var/log/messages>) and binary formats such as the systemd journal."
msgstr ""
"Šis rīks saprot un parāda gan vienkārša teksta žurnālu failus (piem., F</var/"
"log/messages>), gan bināros formātus, piemēram, systemd žurnālu."

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:20
msgid ""
"To display other types of files, use L<virt-cat(1)>.  To follow (tail)  text "
"log files, use L<virt-tail(1)>.  To copy files out of a virtual machine, use "
"L<virt-copy-out(1)>.  To display the contents of the Windows Registry, use "
"L<virt-win-reg(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Citu tipu failu parādīšanai izmantojiet L<virt-cat(1)>.  Teksta žurnālu "
"failu sekošanai (tail) izmantojiet L<virt-tail(1)>.  Failu kopēšanai no "
"virtuālās mašīnas izmantojiet L<virt-copy-out(1)>.  Windows reģistra satura "
"parādīšanai izmantojiet L<virt-win-reg(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:27
msgid "Display the complete logs from a guest:"
msgstr "Parādīt visus viesa žurnālus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: log/virt-log.pod:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-log -d mydomain | less\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-log -d mydomain | less\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:31
msgid "Find out what DHCP IP address a VM acquired:"
msgstr "Noskaidrot, kādu DHCP IP adresi ieguva VM:"

#. type: verbatim
#: log/virt-log.pod:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-log -d mydomain | grep 'dhclient.*bound to'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-log -d mydomain | grep 'dhclient.*bound to'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:81
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, virt-log normally turns echoing off "
"so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried about Tempest "
"attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify this flag to "
"see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, virt-log parasti izslēdz atbalsi, lai "
"nevarētu redzēt, ko rakstāt.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest uzbrukumiem un "
"telpā neviena cita nav, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu, ko rakstāt."

#. type: verbatim
#: log/virt-log.pod:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-log --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-log --format=raw -a disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: log/virt-log.pod:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-log --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-log --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: log/virt-log.pod:139
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-tail(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<virt-win-reg(1)>, "
"L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, L<virt-"
"tail(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<virt-win-reg(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:3
msgid "virt-ls - List files in a virtual machine"
msgstr "virt-ls - uzskaitīt failus virtuālajā mašīnā"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls [--options] -d domname directory [directory ...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls [--options] -d domname directory [directory ...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...] directory [directory "
"...]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls [--options] -a disk.img [-a disk.img ...] directory [directory "
"...]\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls [--options] domname directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls [--options] domname directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls [--options] disk.img [disk.img ...] directory\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls [--options] disk.img [disk.img ...] directory\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:19
msgid ""
"C<virt-ls> lists filenames, file sizes, checksums, extended attributes and "
"more from a virtual machine or disk image."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-ls> uzskaita failu nosaukumus, izmērus, kontrolsummas, paplašinātos "
"atribūtus u. c. no virtuālās mašīnas vai diska attēla."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:22
msgid ""
"Multiple directory names can be given, in which case the output from each is "
"concatenated."
msgstr ""
"Var norādīt vairākus direktoriju nosaukumus — tādā gadījumā katras izvade "
"tiek savienota."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:25
msgid ""
"To list directories from a libvirt guest use the I<-d> option to specify the "
"name of the guest.  For a disk image, use the I<-a> option."
msgstr ""
"Lai uzskaitītu libvirt viesa direktorijas, izmantojiet opciju I<-d>, norādot "
"viesa nosaukumu.  Diska attēlam izmantojiet opciju I<-a>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:29
msgid ""
"C<virt-ls> can do many simple file listings.  For more complicated cases you "
"may need to use L<guestfish(1)>, or write a program directly to the "
"L<guestfs(3)> API."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-ls> var veikt daudzas vienkāršas failu uzskaitīšanas.  Sarežģītākos "
"gadījumos, iespējams, jāizmanto L<guestfish(1)> vai jāraksta programma tieši "
"ar L<guestfs(3)> API."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:35
msgid "Get a list of all files and directories in a virtual machine:"
msgstr "Iegūt visu failu un direktoriju sarakstu virtuālajā mašīnā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -R -d guest /\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -R -d guest /\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:39
msgid "List all setuid or setgid programs in a Linux virtual machine:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas setuid vai setgid programmas Linux virtuālajā mašīnā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep '^- [42]'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep '^- [42]'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:43
msgid "List all public-writable directories in a Linux virtual machine:"
msgstr ""
"Uzskaitīt visas publiski rakstāmās direktorijas Linux virtuālajā mašīnā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep '^d ...7'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep '^d ...7'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:47
msgid "List all Unix domain sockets in a Linux virtual machine:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visas Unix domēna ligzdas Linux virtuālajā mašīnā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep '^s'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep '^s'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:51
msgid "List all regular files with filenames ending in ‘.png’:"
msgstr "Uzskaitīt visus parastos failus, kuru nosaukumi beidzas ar ‘.png’:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep -i '^-.*\\.png$'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest / | grep -i '^-.*\\.png$'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:55
msgid "To display files larger than 10MB in home directories:"
msgstr "Lai parādītu par 10MB lielākus failus mājas direktorijās:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest /home | awk '$3 > 10*1024*1024'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest /home | awk '$3 > 10*1024*1024'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:59
msgid "Find everything modified in the last 7 days:"
msgstr "Atrast visu, kas mainīts pēdējo 7 dienu laikā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest --time-days / | awk '$6 <= 7'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest --time-days / | awk '$6 <= 7'\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:63
msgid "Find regular files modified in the last 24 hours:"
msgstr "Atrast parastos failus, kas mainīti pēdējo 24 stundu laikā:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest --time-days / | grep '^-' | awk '$6 < 1'\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls -lR -d guest --time-days / | grep '^-' | awk '$6 < 1'\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:67
msgid "DIFFERENCES IN SNAPSHOTS AND BACKING FILES"
msgstr "ATŠĶIRĪBAS MOMENTUZŅĒMUMOS UN PAMATFAILOS"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:69
msgid ""
"Although it is possible to use virt-ls to look for differences, since "
"libguestfs E<ge> 1.26 a new tool is available called L<virt-diff(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Lai gan atšķirību meklēšanai var izmantot virt-ls, kopš libguestfs E<ge> "
"1.26 ir pieejams jauns rīks L<virt-diff(1)>."

#. type: =head1
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:72
msgid "OUTPUT MODES"
msgstr "IZVADES REŽĪMI"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:74
msgid ""
"C<virt-ls> has four output modes, controlled by different combinations of "
"the I<-l> and I<-R> options."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-ls> ir četri izvades režīmi, ko nosaka dažādas opciju I<-l> un I<-R> "
"kombinācijas."

#. type: =head2
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:77
msgid "SIMPLE LISTING"
msgstr "VIENKĀRŠS SARAKSTS"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:79
msgid "A simple listing is like the ordinary L<ls(1)> command:"
msgstr "Vienkāršs saraksts ir līdzīgs parastajai komandai L<ls(1)>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:81
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-ls -d guest /\n"
" bin\n"
" boot\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-ls -d guest /\n"
" bin\n"
" boot\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:86
msgid "LONG LISTING"
msgstr "GARAIS SARAKSTS"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:88
msgid ""
"With the I<-l> (I<--long>) option, the output is like the C<ls -l> command "
"(more specifically, like the C<guestfs_ll> function)."
msgstr ""
"Ar opciju I<-l> (I<--long>) izvade ir līdzīga komandai C<ls -l> (precīzāk, "
"funkcijai C<guestfs_ll>)."

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-ls -l -d guest /\n"
" total 204\n"
" dr-xr-xr-x.   2 root root   4096 2009-08-25 19:06 bin\n"
" dr-xr-xr-x.   5 root root   3072 2009-08-25 19:06 boot\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-ls -l -d guest /\n"
" total 204\n"
" dr-xr-xr-x.   2 root root   4096 2009-08-25 19:06 bin\n"
" dr-xr-xr-x.   5 root root   3072 2009-08-25 19:06 boot\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:97
msgid ""
"Note that while this is useful for displaying a directory, do not try "
"parsing this output in another program.  Use L</RECURSIVE LONG LISTING> "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā: lai gan tas noder direktorijas parādīšanai, nemēģiniet šo "
"izvadi parsēt citā programmā.  Tā vietā izmantojiet L</REKURSĪVS GARAIS "
"SARAKSTS>."

#. type: =head2
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:101
msgid "RECURSIVE LISTING"
msgstr "REKURSĪVS SARAKSTS"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:103
msgid ""
"With the I<-R> (I<--recursive>) option, C<virt-ls> lists the names of files "
"and directories recursively:"
msgstr ""
"Ar opciju I<-R> (I<--recursive>) C<virt-ls> rekursīvi uzskaita failu un "
"direktoriju nosaukumus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-ls -R -d guest /tmp\n"
" foo\n"
" foo/bar\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-ls -R -d guest /tmp\n"
" foo\n"
" foo/bar\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:111
msgid ""
"To generate this output, C<virt-ls> runs the C<guestfs_find0> function and "
"converts C<\\0> characters to C<\\n>."
msgstr ""
"Šīs izvades ģenerēšanai C<virt-ls> izpilda funkciju C<guestfs_find0> un "
"pārveido rakstzīmes C<\\0> par C<\\n>."

#. type: =head2
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:114
msgid "RECURSIVE LONG LISTING"
msgstr "REKURSĪVS GARAIS SARAKSTS"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:116
msgid ""
"Using I<-lR> options together changes the output to display directories "
"recursively, with file stats, and optionally other features such as "
"checksums and extended attributes."
msgstr ""
"Opcijas I<-lR> kopā maina izvadi, lai parādītu direktorijas rekursīvi ar "
"failu statistiku un pēc izvēles citiem līdzekļiem, piemēram, kontrolsummām "
"un paplašinātajiem atribūtiem."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:120
msgid ""
"Most of the interesting features of C<virt-ls> are only available when using "
"I<-lR> mode."
msgstr ""
"Lielākā daļa interesanto C<virt-ls> līdzekļu ir pieejami tikai režīmā I<-lR>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:123
msgid ""
"The fields are normally space-separated.  Filenames are B<not> quoted, so "
"you cannot use the output in another program (because filenames can contain "
"spaces and other unsafe characters).  If the guest was untrusted and someone "
"knew you were using C<virt-ls> to analyze the guest, they could play tricks "
"on you by creating filenames with embedded newline characters.  To B<safely> "
"parse the output in another program, use the I<--csv> (Comma-Separated "
"Values) option."
msgstr ""
"Lauki parasti ir atdalīti ar atstarpēm.  Failu nosaukumi B<netiek> citēti, "
"tāpēc izvadi nevar izmantot citā programmā (jo failu nosaukumi var saturēt "
"atstarpes un citas nedrošas rakstzīmes).  Ja viesis bija neuzticams un kāds "
"zināja, ka viesa analīzei izmantojat C<virt-ls>, viņi varētu jūs piemānīt, "
"veidojot failu nosaukumus ar iegultām jaunas rindas rakstzīmēm.  Lai "
"B<droši> parsētu izvadi citā programmā, izmantojiet opciju I<--csv> (ar "
"komatiem atdalītas vērtības)."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:131
msgid ""
"Note that this output format is completely unrelated to the C<ls -lR> "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šis izvades formāts nav pilnīgi nekādi saistīts ar komandu "
"C<ls -lR>."

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:134
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-ls -lR -d guest /bin\n"
" d 0555       4096 /bin\n"
" - 0755        123 /bin/alsaunmute\n"
" - 0755      28328 /bin/arch\n"
" l 0777          4 /bin/awk -> gawk\n"
" - 0755      27216 /bin/basename\n"
" - 0755     943360 /bin/bash\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-ls -lR -d guest /bin\n"
" d 0555       4096 /bin\n"
" - 0755        123 /bin/alsaunmute\n"
" - 0755      28328 /bin/arch\n"
" l 0777          4 /bin/awk -> gawk\n"
" - 0755      27216 /bin/basename\n"
" - 0755     943360 /bin/bash\n"
" [etc.]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:143
msgid "These basic fields are always shown:"
msgstr "Šie pamata lauki tiek rādīti vienmēr:"

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:147
msgid "type"
msgstr "type"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:149
msgid ""
"The file type, one of: C<-> (regular file), C<d> (directory), C<c> "
"(character device), C<b> (block device), C<p> (named pipe), C<l> (symbolic "
"link), C<s> (socket) or C<u> (unknown)."
msgstr ""
"Faila tips, viens no: C<-> (parasts fails), C<d> (direktorija), C<c> "
"(rakstzīmju ierīce), C<b> (bloku ierīce), C<p> (nosaukts kanāls), C<l> "
"(simboliskā saite), C<s> (ligzda) vai C<u> (nezināms)."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:159
msgid "permissions"
msgstr "permissions"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:161
msgid "The Unix permissions, displayed as a 4 digit octal number."
msgstr "Unix atļaujas, parādītas kā 4 ciparu astoņnieku skaitlis."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:163
msgid "size"
msgstr "size"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:165
msgid ""
"The size of the file.  This is shown in bytes unless I<-h> or "
"I<--human-readable> option is given, in which case this is shown as a "
"human-readable number."
msgstr ""
"Faila izmērs.  Tas tiek rādīts baitos, ja vien nav norādīta opcija I<-h> vai "
"I<--human-readable> — tad tas tiek rādīts kā cilvēkam lasāms skaitlis."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:169
msgid "path"
msgstr "path"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:171
msgid "The full path of the file or directory."
msgstr "Pilns faila vai direktorijas ceļš."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:173
msgid "link"
msgstr "link"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:175
msgid "For symbolic links only, the link target."
msgstr "Tikai simboliskajām saitēm — saites mērķis."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:179
msgid ""
"In I<-lR> mode, additional command line options enable the display of more "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"Režīmā I<-lR> papildu komandrindas opcijas iespējo vairāk lauku parādīšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:182
msgid ""
"With the I<--uids> flag, these additional fields are displayed before the "
"path:"
msgstr "Ar karogu I<--uids> šie papildu lauki tiek parādīti pirms ceļa:"

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:187
msgid "uid"
msgstr "uid"

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:189
msgid "gid"
msgstr "gid"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:191
msgid ""
"The UID and GID of the owner of the file (displayed numerically).  Note "
"these only make sense in the context of a Unix-like guest."
msgstr ""
"Faila īpašnieka UID un GID (parādīti skaitliski).  Ņemiet vērā, ka tiem ir "
"jēga tikai Unix līdzīga viesa kontekstā."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:196
msgid "With the I<--times> flag, these additional fields are displayed:"
msgstr "Ar karogu I<--times> tiek parādīti šie papildu lauki:"

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:200
msgid "atime"
msgstr "atime"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:202
msgid "The time of last access."
msgstr "Pēdējās piekļuves laiks."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:204
msgid "mtime"
msgstr "mtime"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:206
msgid "The time of last modification."
msgstr "Pēdējās modificēšanas laiks."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:208
msgid "ctime"
msgstr "ctime"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:210
msgid "The time of last status change."
msgstr "Pēdējās statusa maiņas laiks."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:214
msgid ""
"The time fields are displayed as string dates and times, unless one of the "
"I<--time-t>, I<--time-relative> or I<--time-days> flags is given."
msgstr ""
"Laika lauki tiek parādīti kā datumu un laiku virknes, ja vien nav norādīts "
"kāds no karogiem I<--time-t>, I<--time-relative> vai I<--time-days>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:217
msgid "With the I<--extra-stats> flag, these additional fields are displayed:"
msgstr "Ar karogu I<--extra-stats> tiek parādīti šie papildu lauki:"

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:221
msgid "device"
msgstr "device"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:223
msgid ""
"The device containing the file (displayed as major:minor).  This may not "
"match devices as known to the guest."
msgstr ""
"Ierīce, kurā atrodas fails (parādīta kā major:minor).  Tā var neatbilst "
"viesim zināmajām ierīcēm."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:226
msgid "inode"
msgstr "inode"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:228
msgid "The inode number."
msgstr "Inode numurs."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:230
msgid "nlink"
msgstr "nlink"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:232
msgid "The number of hard links."
msgstr "Cieto saišu skaits."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:234
msgid "rdev"
msgstr "rdev"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:236
msgid "For block and char special files, the device (displayed as major:minor)."
msgstr ""
"Bloku un rakstzīmju speciālajiem failiem — ierīce (parādīta kā major:minor)."

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:239
msgid "blocks"
msgstr "blocks"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:241
msgid "The number of 512 byte blocks allocated to the file."
msgstr "Failam piešķirto 512 baitu bloku skaits."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:245
msgid ""
"With the I<--checksum> flag, the checksum of the file contents is shown "
"(only for regular files).  Computing file checksums can take a considerable "
"amount of time."
msgstr ""
"Ar karogu I<--checksum> tiek parādīta faila satura kontrolsumma (tikai "
"parastiem failiem).  Failu kontrolsummu aprēķins var aizņemt ievērojamu "
"laiku."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:280
msgid ""
"Display checksum over file contents for regular files.  With no argument, "
"this defaults to using I<md5>.  Using an argument, you can select the "
"checksum type to use."
msgstr ""
"Parādīt parastu failu satura kontrolsummu.  Bez argumenta pēc noklusējuma "
"tiek izmantots I<md5>.  Ar argumentu var izvēlēties izmantojamo "
"kontrolsummas tipu."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:284 ls/virt-ls.pod:321 ls/virt-ls.pod:354 ls/virt-ls.pod:422
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:432 ls/virt-ls.pod:439 ls/virt-ls.pod:446 ls/virt-ls.pod:453
msgid ""
"This option only has effect in I<-lR> output mode.  See L</RECURSIVE LONG "
"LISTING> above."
msgstr ""
"Šī opcija darbojas tikai izvades režīmā I<-lR>.  Skatiet L</REKURSĪVS GARAIS "
"SARAKSTS> iepriekš."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:312
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, virt-ls normally turns echoing off "
"so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried about Tempest "
"attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify this flag to "
"see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, virt-ls parasti izslēdz atbalsi, lai "
"nevarētu redzēt, ko rakstāt.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest uzbrukumiem un "
"telpā neviena cita nav, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu, ko rakstāt."

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:335
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls --format=raw -a disk.img /dir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls --format=raw -a disk.img /dir\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:339
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img /dir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls --format=raw -a disk.img --format -a another.img /dir\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:401
msgid "B<-R>"
msgstr "B<-R>"

#. type: =item
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:403
msgid "B<--recursive>"
msgstr "B<--recursive>"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:405
msgid ""
"Select the mode.  With neither of these options, C<virt-ls> produces a "
"simple, flat list of the files in the named directory.  See L</SIMPLE "
"LISTING>."
msgstr ""
"Izvēlēties režīmu.  Bez abām šīm opcijām C<virt-ls> rada vienkāršu, plakanu "
"nosauktās direktorijas failu sarakstu.  Skatiet L</VIENKĀRŠS SARAKSTS>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:409
msgid ""
"C<virt-ls -l> produces a \"long listing\", which shows more detail.  See "
"L</LONG LISTING>."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-ls -l> rada „garo sarakstu”, kas rāda vairāk informācijas.  Skatiet "
"L</GARAIS SARAKSTS>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:412
msgid ""
"C<virt-ls -R> produces a recursive list of files starting at the named "
"directory.  See L</RECURSIVE LISTING>."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-ls -R> rada rekursīvu failu sarakstu, sākot ar nosaukto direktoriju.  "
"Skatiet L</REKURSĪVS SARAKSTS>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:415
msgid ""
"C<virt-ls -lR> produces a recursive long listing which can be more easily "
"parsed.  See L</RECURSIVE LONG LISTING>."
msgstr ""
"C<virt-ls -lR> rada rekursīvu garo sarakstu, ko var vieglāk parsēt.  Skatiet "
"L</REKURSĪVS GARAIS SARAKSTS>."

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:476
msgid "Previous versions of virt-ls allowed you to write either:"
msgstr "Iepriekšējās virt-ls versijas ļāva rakstīt gan:"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:478
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls disk.img [disk.img ...] /dir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls disk.img [disk.img ...] /dir\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:482
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-ls guestname /dir\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-ls guestname /dir\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: ls/virt-ls.pod:521
msgid ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, "
"L<virt-diff(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-cat(1)>, L<virt-copy-out(1)>, L<virt-"
"diff(1)>, L<virt-tar-out(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:3
msgid "virt-make-fs - Make a filesystem from a tar archive or files"
msgstr "virt-make-fs - izveidot failu sistēmu no tar arhīva vai failiem"

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs [--options] input.tar output.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs [--options] input.tar output.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs [--options] input.tar.gz output.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs [--options] input.tar.gz output.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs [--options] directory output.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs [--options] directory output.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:15
msgid ""
"Virt-make-fs is a command line tool for creating a filesystem from a tar "
"archive or some files in a directory.  It is similar to tools like "
"L<mkisofs(1)>, L<genisoimage(1)> and L<mksquashfs(1)>.  Unlike those tools, "
"it can create common filesystem types like ext2/3 or NTFS, which can be "
"useful if you want to attach these filesystems to existing virtual machines "
"(eg. to import large amounts of read-only data to a VM)."
msgstr ""
"Virt-make-fs ir komandrindas rīks failu sistēmas izveidei no tar arhīva vai "
"failiem direktorijā.  Tas ir līdzīgs tādiem rīkiem kā L<mkisofs(1)>, "
"L<genisoimage(1)> un L<mksquashfs(1)>.  Atšķirībā no tiem tas var izveidot "
"izplatītus failu sistēmu tipus, piemēram, ext2/3 vai NTFS, kas var noderēt, "
"ja vēlaties šīs failu sistēmas pievienot esošām virtuālajām mašīnām (piem., "
"lai importētu VM lielu daudzumu tikai lasāmu datu)."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:23
msgid ""
"To create blank disks, use L<virt-format(1)>.  To create complex layouts, "
"use L<guestfish(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Tukšu disku izveidei izmantojiet L<virt-format(1)>.  Sarežģītu izkārtojumu "
"izveidei izmantojiet L<guestfish(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:26
msgid "Basic usage is:"
msgstr "Pamata lietojums ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs input output.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs input output.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:30
msgid ""
"where C<input> is either a directory containing files that you want to add, "
"or a tar archive (either uncompressed tar or gzip-compressed tar); and "
"F<output.img> is a disk image.  The input type is detected automatically.  "
"The output disk image defaults to a raw ext2 sparse image unless you specify "
"extra flags (see L</OPTIONS> below)."
msgstr ""
"kur C<input> ir vai nu direktorija ar pievienojamiem failiem, vai tar arhīvs "
"(nesaspiests vai ar gzip saspiests tar), un F<output.img> ir diska attēls.  "
"Ievades tips tiek noteikts automātiski.  Izvades diska attēls pēc "
"noklusējuma ir raw ext2 retināts attēls, ja vien nenorādāt papildu karogus "
"(skatiet L</OPCIJAS> tālāk)."

#. type: =head2
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:36
msgid "FILESYSTEM TYPE"
msgstr "FAILU SISTĒMAS TIPS"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:38
msgid ""
"The default filesystem type is C<ext2>.  Just about any filesystem type that "
"libguestfs supports can be used (but I<not> read-only formats like "
"ISO9660).  Here are some of the more common choices:"
msgstr ""
"Noklusējuma failu sistēmas tips ir C<ext2>.  Var izmantot gandrīz jebkuru "
"libguestfs atbalstītu failu sistēmas tipu (bet I<ne> tikai lasāmus formātus, "
"piemēram, ISO9660).  Lūk, dažas no biežākajām izvēlēm:"

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:44
msgid "I<ext3>"
msgstr "I<ext3>"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:46
msgid ""
"Note that ext3 filesystems contain a journal, typically 1-32 MB in size.  If "
"you are not going to use the filesystem in a way that requires the journal, "
"then this is just wasted overhead."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka ext3 failu sistēmās ir žurnāls, parasti 1–32 MB liels.  Ja "
"neplānojat failu sistēmu izmantot tā, ka vajadzīgs žurnāls, tās ir tikai "
"lieki zaudējumi."

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:50
msgid "I<ntfs> or I<vfat>"
msgstr "I<ntfs> vai I<vfat>"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:52
msgid "Useful if exporting data to a Windows guest."
msgstr "Noderīgi, eksportējot datus uz Windows viesi."

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:54
msgid "I<minix>"
msgstr "I<minix>"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:56
msgid ""
"Lower overhead than C<ext2>, but certain limitations on filename length and "
"total filesystem size."
msgstr ""
"Mazāki zaudējumi nekā C<ext2>, taču ir zināmi ierobežojumi failu nosaukumu "
"garumam un kopējam failu sistēmas izmēram."

#. type: =head1
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:61 make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:80
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:113 tail/virt-tail.pod:40
msgid "EXAMPLE"
msgstr "PIEMĒRS"

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs --type=minix input minixfs.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs --type=minix input minixfs.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:65
msgid "TO PARTITION OR NOT TO PARTITION"
msgstr "NODALĪT VAI NENODALĪT"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:67
msgid "Optionally virt-make-fs can add a partition table to the output disk."
msgstr ""
"Pēc izvēles virt-make-fs var pievienot izvades diskam nodalījumu tabulu."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:69
msgid ""
"Adding a partition can make the disk image more compatible with certain "
"virtualized operating systems which don't expect to see a filesystem "
"directly located on a block device (Linux doesn't care and will happily "
"handle both types)."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījuma pievienošana var padarīt diska attēlu saderīgāku ar dažām "
"virtualizētām operētājsistēmām, kas negaida failu sistēmu tieši bloku ierīcē "
"(Linux tas neinteresē, un tas labprāt apstrādās abus tipus)."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:74
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if you have a partition table then the output image is no "
"longer a straight filesystem.  For example you cannot run L<fsck(8)> "
"directly on a partitioned disk image.  (However libguestfs tools such as "
"L<guestfish(1)> and L<virt-resize(1)> can still be used)."
msgstr ""
"No otras puses, ja ir nodalījumu tabula, izvades attēls vairs nav vienkārša "
"failu sistēma.  Piemēram, ar nodalītu diska attēlu nevar tieši palaist L<fsck"
"(8)>.  (Tomēr libguestfs rīkus, piemēram, L<guestfish(1)> un L<virt-resize"
"(1)>, joprojām var izmantot.)"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:82
msgid "Add an MBR partition:"
msgstr "Pievienot MBR nodalījumu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs --partition -- input disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs --partition -- input disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:86
msgid ""
"If the output disk image could be terabyte-sized or larger, it's better to "
"use an EFI/GPT-compatible partition table:"
msgstr ""
"Ja izvades diska attēls varētu būt terabaitu liels vai lielāks, labāk "
"izmantot ar EFI/GPT saderīgu nodalījumu tabulu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs --partition=gpt --size=+4T --format=qcow2 input disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs --partition=gpt --size=+4T --format=qcow2 input disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head2
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:91
msgid "EXTRA SPACE"
msgstr "PAPILDU VIETA"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:93
msgid ""
"Unlike formats such as tar and squashfs, a filesystem does not \"just fit\" "
"the files that it contains, but might have extra space.  Depending on how "
"you are going to use the output, you might think this extra space is wasted "
"and want to minimize it, or you might want to leave space so that more files "
"can be added later.  Virt-make-fs defaults to minimizing the extra space, "
"but you can use the I<--size> flag to leave space in the filesystem if you "
"want it."
msgstr ""
"Atšķirībā no tādiem formātiem kā tar un squashfs, failu sistēma „vienkārši "
"neietilpina” tajā esošos failus, bet tajā var būt papildu vieta.  Atkarībā "
"no tā, kā izmantosiet izvadi, varat uzskatīt šo papildu vietu par izšķiestu "
"un vēlēties to samazināt, vai arī vēlēties atstāt vietu, lai vēlāk varētu "
"pievienot vairāk failu.  Virt-make-fs pēc noklusējuma samazina papildu "
"vietu, bet, ja vēlaties, ar karogu I<--size> failu sistēmā var atstāt vietu."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:101
msgid ""
"An alternative way to leave extra space but not make the output image any "
"bigger is to use an alternative disk image format (instead of the default "
"\"raw\" format).  Using I<--format=qcow2> will use the native qemu/KVM qcow2 "
"image format (check your hypervisor supports this before using it).  This "
"allows you to choose a large I<--size> but the extra space won't actually be "
"allocated in the image until you try to store something in it."
msgstr ""
"Alternatīvs veids, kā atstāt papildu vietu, nepalielinot izvades attēlu, ir "
"izmantot alternatīvu diska attēla formātu (noklusējuma „raw” formāta vietā)"
".  I<--format=qcow2> izmantos qemu/KVM vietējo qcow2 attēla formātu (pirms "
"izmantošanas pārbaudiet, vai jūsu hipervizors to atbalsta).  Tas ļauj "
"izvēlēties lielu I<--size>, taču papildu vieta attēlā faktiski netiks "
"piešķirta, kamēr nemēģināsiet tajā kaut ko saglabāt."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:109
msgid ""
"Don’t forget that you can also use local commands including L<resize2fs(8)> "
"and L<virt-resize(1)> to resize existing filesystems, or rerun virt-make-fs "
"to build another image from scratch."
msgstr ""
"Neaizmirstiet, ka esošu failu sistēmu izmēra maiņai var izmantot arī lokālas "
"komandas, tostarp L<resize2fs(8)> un L<virt-resize(1)>, vai atkārtoti "
"palaist virt-make-fs, lai izveidotu citu attēlu no nulles."

#. type: verbatim
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-make-fs --format=qcow2 --size=+200M input output.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-make-fs --format=qcow2 --size=+200M input output.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:129
msgid "This parameter sets the sector size of the output disk image."
msgstr "Šis parametrs iestata izvades diska attēla sektora izmēru."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:131
msgid "The default is C<512> bytes."
msgstr "Noklusējums ir C<512> baiti."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:133
msgid "See also L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts>."
msgstr "Skatīt arī L<guestfs(3)/guestfs_add_drive_opts>."

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:135
msgid "B<--floppy>"
msgstr "B<--floppy>"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:137
msgid "Create a virtual floppy disk."
msgstr "Izveidot virtuālu disketi."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:139
msgid ""
"Currently this preselects the size (1440K), partition type (MBR) and "
"filesystem type (VFAT).  In future it may also choose the geometry."
msgstr ""
"Pašlaik tas iepriekš izvēlas izmēru (1440K), nodalījuma tipu (MBR) un failu "
"sistēmas tipu (VFAT).  Nākotnē tas var izvēlēties arī ģeometriju."

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:142
msgid "B<--size=>N"
msgstr "B<--size=>N"

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:144
msgid "B<--size=+>N"
msgstr "B<--size=+>N"

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:146
msgid "B<-s> N"
msgstr "B<-s> N"

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:148
msgid "B<-s> B<+>N"
msgstr "B<-s> B<+>N"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:150
msgid "Use the I<--size> (or I<-s>) option to choose the size of the output image."
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet opciju I<--size> (vai I<-s>), lai izvēlētos izvades attēla "
"izmēru."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:153
msgid ""
"If this option is I<not> given, then the output image will be just large "
"enough to contain all the files, with not much wasted space."
msgstr ""
"Ja šī opcija I<nav> norādīta, izvades attēls būs tieši tik liels, lai "
"saturētu visus failus, bez daudz izšķiestas vietas."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:156
msgid ""
"To choose a fixed size output disk, specify an absolute number followed by "
"b/K/M/G/T/P/E to mean bytes, Kilobytes, Megabytes, Gigabytes, Terabytes, "
"Petabytes or Exabytes.  This must be large enough to contain all the input "
"files, else you will get an error."
msgstr ""
"Lai izvēlētos fiksēta izmēra izvades disku, norādiet absolūtu skaitli, kam "
"seko b/K/M/G/T/P/E, kas nozīmē baitus, kilobaitus, megabaitus, gigabaitus, "
"terabaitus, petabaitus vai eksabaitus.  Tam jābūt pietiekami lielam, lai "
"saturētu visus ievades failus, citādi radīsies kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:161
msgid ""
"To leave extra space, specify C<+> (plus sign) and a number followed by "
"b/K/M/G/T/P/E to mean bytes, Kilobytes, Megabytes, Gigabytes, Terabytes, "
"Petabytes or Exabytes.  For example: I<--size=+200M> means enough space for "
"the input files, and (approximately) an extra 200 MB free space."
msgstr ""
"Lai atstātu papildu vietu, norādiet C<+> (plus zīmi) un skaitli, kam seko b/"
"K/M/G/T/P/E, kas nozīmē baitus, kilobaitus, megabaitus, gigabaitus, "
"terabaitus, petabaitus vai eksabaitus.  Piemēram: I<--size=+200M> nozīmē "
"pietiekami daudz vietas ievades failiem un (aptuveni) papildu 200 MB brīvas "
"vietas."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:167
msgid ""
"Note that virt-make-fs estimates free space, and therefore will not produce "
"filesystems containing precisely the free space requested.  (It is much more "
"expensive and time-consuming to produce a filesystem which has precisely the "
"desired free space)."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka virt-make-fs aplēš brīvo vietu, tāpēc tas neradīs failu "
"sistēmas ar precīzi pieprasīto brīvo vietu.  (Failu sistēmas ar precīzi "
"vēlamo brīvo vietu izveide ir daudz dārgāka un laikietilpīgāka.)"

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:172
msgid "B<--format=>FMT"
msgstr "B<--format=>FMT"

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:174
msgid "B<-F> FMT"
msgstr "B<-F> FMT"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:176
msgid "Choose the output disk image format."
msgstr "Izvēlēties izvades diska attēla formātu."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:178
msgid "The default is C<raw> (raw sparse disk image)."
msgstr "Noklusējums ir C<raw> (raw retināts diska attēls)."

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:180
msgid "B<--type=>FS"
msgstr "B<--type=>FS"

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:182
msgid "B<-t> FS"
msgstr "B<-t> FS"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:184
msgid "Choose the output filesystem type."
msgstr "Izvēlēties izvades failu sistēmas tipu."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:186
msgid "The default is C<ext2>."
msgstr "Noklusējums ir C<ext2>."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:188
msgid "Any filesystem which is supported read-write by libguestfs can be used here."
msgstr ""
"Šeit var izmantot jebkuru failu sistēmu, ko libguestfs atbalsta lasīšanai un "
"rakstīšanai."

#. type: =item
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:197
msgid "B<--partition=>PARTTYPE"
msgstr "B<--partition=>PARTTYPE"

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:199
msgid ""
"If specified, this flag adds an MBR partition table to the output disk "
"image."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādīts, šis karogs izvades diska attēlam pievieno MBR nodalījumu tabulu."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:202
msgid ""
"You can change the partition table type, eg. I<--partition=gpt> for large "
"disks."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījumu tabulas tipu var mainīt, piem., I<--partition=gpt> lieliem "
"diskiem."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:205
msgid "For MBR, virt-make-fs sets the partition type byte automatically."
msgstr "MBR gadījumā virt-make-fs nodalījuma tipa baitu iestata automātiski."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:211
msgid "Enable debugging information."
msgstr "Iespējot atkļūdošanas informāciju."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:221
msgid "Enable libguestfs trace."
msgstr "Iespējot libguestfs izsekošanu."

#. type: textblock
#: make-fs/virt-make-fs.pod:227
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-format(1)>, L<virt-resize(1)>, L<virt-tar-in(1)>, "
"L<mkisofs(1)>, L<genisoimage(1)>, L<mksquashfs(1)>, L<mke2fs(8)>, "
"L<resize2fs(8)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)>, L<virt-format(1)>, L<virt-resize(1)>, L<virt-tar-in(1)>, "
"L<mkisofs(1)>, L<genisoimage(1)>, L<mksquashfs(1)>, L<mke2fs(8)>, L<resize2fs"
"(8)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:3
msgid "virt-resize - Resize a virtual machine disk"
msgstr "virt-resize - mainīt virtuālās mašīnas diska izmēru"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-resize [--resize /dev/sdaN=[+/-]<size>[%]]\n"
"   [--expand /dev/sdaN] [--shrink /dev/sdaN]\n"
"   [--ignore /dev/sdaN] [--delete /dev/sdaN] [...] indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-resize [--resize /dev/sdaN=[+/-]<size>[%]]\n"
"   [--expand /dev/sdaN] [--shrink /dev/sdaN]\n"
"   [--ignore /dev/sdaN] [--delete /dev/sdaN] [...] indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:13
msgid ""
"Virt-resize is a tool which can resize a virtual machine disk, making it "
"larger or smaller overall, and resizing or deleting any partitions contained "
"within."
msgstr ""
"Virt-resize ir rīks, kas var mainīt virtuālās mašīnas diska izmēru, padarot "
"to kopumā lielāku vai mazāku, un mainīt tajā esošo nodalījumu izmēru vai tos "
"izdzēst."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:17
msgid ""
"Virt-resize B<cannot> resize disk images in-place.  Virt-resize B<should "
"not> be used on live virtual machines - for consistent results, shut the "
"virtual machine down before resizing it."
msgstr ""
"Virt-resize B<nevar> mainīt disku attēlu izmēru uz vietas.  Virt-resize "
"B<nevajadzētu> izmantot ar darbojošām virtuālajām mašīnām — konsekventiem "
"rezultātiem pirms izmēra maiņas virtuālo mašīnu izslēdziet."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:21
msgid ""
"If you are not familiar with the associated tools: L<virt-filesystems(1)> "
"and L<virt-df(1)>, we recommend you go and read those manual pages first."
msgstr ""
"Ja saistītie rīki L<virt-filesystems(1)> un L<virt-df(1)> jums nav "
"pazīstami, iesakām vispirms izlasīt to rokasgrāmatas lapas."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:31
msgid ""
"This example takes C<olddisk> and resizes it into C<newdisk>, extending one "
"of the guest’s partitions to fill the extra 5GB of space:"
msgstr ""
"Šajā piemērā C<olddisk> izmērs tiek mainīts, ierakstot to C<newdisk>, un "
"viens no viesa nodalījumiem tiek paplašināts, lai aizpildītu papildu 5GB "
"vietas:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-filesystems --long -h --all -a olddisk\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" virt-filesystems --long -h --all -a olddisk\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" truncate -r olddisk newdisk\n"
" truncate -s +5G newdisk\n"
" \n"
msgstr ""
" truncate -r olddisk newdisk\n"
" truncate -s +5G newdisk\n"
" \n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # Note \"/dev/sda2\" is a partition inside the \"olddisk\" file.\n"
" virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 olddisk newdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # Note \"/dev/sda2\" is a partition inside the \"olddisk\" file.\n"
" virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 olddisk newdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:45
msgid ""
"As above, but make the /boot partition 200MB bigger, while giving the "
"remaining space to /dev/sda2:"
msgstr ""
"Tāpat kā iepriekš, bet palielināt /boot nodalījumu par 200MB, atlikušo vietu "
"atdodot /dev/sda2:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-resize --resize /dev/sda1=+200M --expand /dev/sda2 \\\n"
"   olddisk newdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-resize --resize /dev/sda1=+200M --expand /dev/sda2 \\\n"
"   olddisk newdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:53
msgid ""
"As in the first example, but expand a logical volume as the final step.  "
"This is what you would typically use for Linux guests that use LVM:"
msgstr ""
"Tāpat kā pirmajā piemērā, bet pēdējā solī paplašināt loģisko sējumu.  To "
"parasti izmantotu Linux viesiem, kas izmanto LVM:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 --LV-expand /dev/vg_guest/lv_root \\\n"
"   olddisk newdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 --LV-expand /dev/vg_guest/lv_root \\\n"
"   olddisk newdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:62
msgid ""
"As in the first example, but the output format will be qcow2 instead of a "
"raw disk:"
msgstr ""
"Tāpat kā pirmajā piemērā, bet izvades formāts būs qcow2, nevis raw disks:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" qemu-img create -f qcow2 -o preallocation=metadata newdisk.qcow2 15G\n"
" virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 olddisk newdisk.qcow2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" qemu-img create -f qcow2 -o preallocation=metadata newdisk.qcow2 15G\n"
" virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 olddisk newdisk.qcow2\n"
"\n"

#. type: =head1
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:70
msgid "DETAILED USAGE"
msgstr "DETALIZĒTA LIETOŠANA"

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:72
msgid "EXPANDING A VIRTUAL MACHINE DISK"
msgstr "VIRTUĀLĀS MAŠĪNAS DISKA PALIELINĀŠANA"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:76
msgid "1. Shut down the virtual machine"
msgstr "1. Izslēgt virtuālo mašīnu"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:78
msgid "2. Locate input disk image"
msgstr "2. Atrast ievades diska attēlu"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:80
msgid ""
"Locate the input disk image (ie. the file or device on the host containing "
"the guest’s disk).  If the guest is managed by libvirt, you can use C<virsh "
"dumpxml> like this to find the disk image name:"
msgstr ""
"Atrodiet ievades diska attēlu (t. i., resursdatora failu vai ierīci ar viesa "
"disku).  Ja viesi pārvalda libvirt, diska attēla nosaukuma atrašanai var "
"izmantot C<virsh dumpxml> šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virsh dumpxml guestname | xpath -e /domain/devices/disk/source\n"
" Found 1 nodes:\n"
" -- NODE --\n"
" <source dev=\"/dev/vg/lv_guest\" />\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virsh dumpxml guestname | xpath -e /domain/devices/disk/source\n"
" Found 1 nodes:\n"
" -- NODE --\n"
" <source dev=\"/dev/vg/lv_guest\" />\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:89
msgid "3. Look at current sizing"
msgstr "3. Apskatīt pašreizējos izmērus"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:91
msgid "Use L<virt-filesystems(1)> to display the current partitions and sizes:"
msgstr ""
"Izmantojiet L<virt-filesystems(1)>, lai parādītu pašreizējos nodalījumus un "
"izmērus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virt-filesystems --long --parts --blkdevs -h -a /dev/vg/lv_guest\n"
" Name       Type       Size  Parent\n"
" /dev/sda1  partition  101M  /dev/sda\n"
" /dev/sda2  partition  7.9G  /dev/sda\n"
" /dev/sda   device     8.0G  -\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virt-filesystems --long --parts --blkdevs -h -a /dev/vg/lv_guest\n"
" Name       Type       Size  Parent\n"
" /dev/sda1  partition  101M  /dev/sda\n"
" /dev/sda2  partition  7.9G  /dev/sda\n"
" /dev/sda   device     8.0G  -\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:100
msgid ""
"(This example is a virtual machine with an 8 GB disk which we would like to "
"expand up to 10 GB)."
msgstr ""
"(Šajā piemērā ir virtuālā mašīna ar 8 GB disku, ko vēlamies paplašināt līdz "
"10 GB.)"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:103
msgid "4. Create output disk"
msgstr "4. Izveidot izvades disku"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:105
msgid ""
"Virt-resize cannot do in-place disk modifications.  You have to have space "
"to store the resized output disk."
msgstr ""
"Virt-resize nevar veikt disku izmaiņas uz vietas.  Jums jābūt vietai, kur "
"glabāt izvades disku ar mainīto izmēru."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:108
msgid "To store the resized disk image in a file, create a file of a suitable size:"
msgstr ""
"Lai mainītā izmēra diska attēlu glabātu failā, izveidojiet piemērota izmēra "
"failu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:111
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # rm -f outdisk\n"
" # truncate -s 10G outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # rm -f outdisk\n"
" # truncate -s 10G outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:114
msgid "Or use L<lvcreate(1)> to create a logical volume:"
msgstr "Vai izmantojiet L<lvcreate(1)>, lai izveidotu loģisko sējumu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:116
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # lvcreate -L 10G -n lv_name vg_name\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # lvcreate -L 10G -n lv_name vg_name\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:118
msgid "Or use L<virsh(1)> vol-create-as to create a libvirt storage volume:"
msgstr ""
"Vai izmantojiet L<virsh(1)> vol-create-as, lai izveidotu libvirt krātuves "
"sējumu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virsh pool-list\n"
" # virsh vol-create-as poolname newvol 10G\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virsh pool-list\n"
" # virsh vol-create-as poolname newvol 10G\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:123
msgid "5. Resize"
msgstr "5. Mainīt izmēru"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:125
msgid ""
"virt-resize takes two mandatory parameters, the input disk and the output "
"disk (both can be e.g. a device, a file, or a URI to a remote disk).  The "
"output disk is the one created in the previous step."
msgstr ""
"virt-resize pieņem divus obligātus parametrus — ievades disku un izvades "
"disku (abi var būt, piem., ierīce, fails vai URI uz attālu disku).  Izvades "
"disks ir iepriekšējā solī izveidotais."

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virt-resize indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virt-resize indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:131
msgid ""
"This command just copies disk image C<indisk> to disk image C<outdisk> "
"I<without> resizing or changing any existing partitions.  If C<outdisk> is "
"larger, then an extra, empty partition is created at the end of the disk "
"covering the extra space.  If C<outdisk> is smaller, then it will give an "
"error."
msgstr ""
"Šī komanda tikai kopē diska attēlu C<indisk> uz diska attēlu C<outdisk>, "
"I<nemainot> izmēru vai nemainot esošos nodalījumus.  Ja C<outdisk> ir "
"lielāks, diska beigās tiek izveidots papildu tukšs nodalījums, kas aizņem "
"papildu vietu.  Ja C<outdisk> ir mazāks, radīsies kļūda."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:137
msgid ""
"More realistically you'd want to expand existing partitions in the disk "
"image by passing extra options (for the full list see the L</OPTIONS> "
"section below)."
msgstr ""
"Reālāk jūs vēlētos paplašināt esošos nodalījumus diska attēlā, norādot "
"papildu opcijas (pilnu sarakstu skatiet sadaļā L</OPCIJAS> tālāk)."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:141
msgid ""
"L</--expand> is the most useful option.  It expands the named partition "
"within the disk to fill any extra space:"
msgstr ""
"L</--expand> ir visnoderīgākā opcija.  Tā paplašina nosaukto diska "
"nodalījumu, lai aizpildītu visu papildu vietu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:144
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:146
msgid ""
"(In this case, an extra partition is I<not> created at the end of the disk, "
"because there will be no unused space)."
msgstr ""
"(Šajā gadījumā diska beigās papildu nodalījums I<netiek> izveidots, jo "
"neizmantotas vietas nebūs.)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:149
msgid ""
"L</--resize> is the other commonly used option.  The following would "
"increase the size of /dev/sda1 by 200M, and expand /dev/sda2 to fill the "
"rest of the available space:"
msgstr ""
"L</--resize> ir otra bieži izmantotā opcija.  Šis palielinātu /dev/sda1 "
"izmēru par 200M un paplašinātu /dev/sda2, lai aizpildītu atlikušo pieejamo "
"vietu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:153
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virt-resize --resize /dev/sda1=+200M --expand /dev/sda2 \\\n"
"     indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virt-resize --resize /dev/sda1=+200M --expand /dev/sda2 \\\n"
"     indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:156
msgid ""
"If the expanded partition in the image contains a filesystem or LVM PV, then "
"if virt-resize knows how, it will resize the contents, the equivalent of "
"calling a command such as L<pvresize(8)>, L<resize2fs(8)>, L<ntfsresize(8)>, "
"L<btrfs(8)>, L<xfs_growfs(8)>, or L<resize.f2fs(8)>.  However virt-resize "
"does not know how to resize some filesystems, so you would have to online "
"resize them after booting the guest."
msgstr ""
"Ja paplašinātajā attēla nodalījumā ir failu sistēma vai LVM PV, virt-resize, "
"ja prot, mainīs satura izmēru, kas līdzvērtīgi tādas komandas izsaukšanai kā "
"L<pvresize(8)>, L<resize2fs(8)>, L<ntfsresize(8)>, L<btrfs(8)>, L<xfs_growfs"
"(8)> vai L<resize.f2fs(8)>.  Tomēr virt-resize neprot mainīt dažu failu "
"sistēmu izmēru, tāpēc pēc viesa sāknēšanas to izmērs būtu jāmaina tiešsaistē."

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:164
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 nbd://example.com outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virt-resize --expand /dev/sda2 nbd://example.com outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:166
msgid ""
"The input disk can be a URI, in order to use a remote disk as the source.  "
"The URI format is compatible with guestfish.  See L<guestfish(1)/ADDING "
"REMOTE STORAGE>."
msgstr ""
"Ievades disks var būt URI, lai kā avotu izmantotu attālu disku.  URI formāts "
"ir saderīgs ar guestfish.  Skatiet L<guestfish(1)/ATTĀLĀS KRĀTUVES "
"PIEVIENOŠANA>."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:170
msgid "Other options are covered below."
msgstr "Citas opcijas aprakstītas tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:172
msgid "6. Test"
msgstr "6. Testēt"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:174
msgid "Thoroughly test the new disk image I<before> discarding the old one."
msgstr "Rūpīgi testējiet jauno diska attēlu, I<pirms> atmetat veco."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:176
msgid "If you are using libvirt, edit the XML to point at the new disk:"
msgstr "Ja izmantojat libvirt, rediģējiet XML, lai norādītu uz jauno disku:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:178
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virsh edit guestname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virsh edit guestname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:180
msgid ""
"Change E<lt>source ...E<gt>, see "
"L<http://libvirt.org/formatdomain.html#elementsDisks>"
msgstr ""
"Mainiet E<lt>source ...E<gt>, skatiet L<http://libvirt.org/"
"formatdomain.html#elementsDisks>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:183
msgid "Then start up the domain with the new, resized disk:"
msgstr "Pēc tam palaidiet domēnu ar jauno, mainītā izmēra disku:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:185
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" # virsh start guestname\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" # virsh start guestname\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:187
msgid ""
"and check that it still works.  See also the L</NOTES> section below for "
"additional information."
msgstr ""
"un pārbaudiet, vai tas joprojām darbojas.  Papildu informāciju skatiet arī "
"sadaļā L</PIEZĪMES> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:190
msgid "7. Resize LVs etc inside the guest"
msgstr "7. Mainīt LV u. c. izmēru viesī"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:192
msgid "(This can also be done offline using L<guestfish(1)>)"
msgstr "(To var izdarīt arī bezsaistē ar L<guestfish(1)>)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:194
msgid ""
"Once the guest has booted you should see the new space available, at least "
"for filesystems that virt-resize knows how to resize, and for PVs.  The user "
"may need to resize LVs inside PVs, and also resize filesystem types that "
"virt-resize does not know how to expand."
msgstr ""
"Kad viesis ir sāknēts, jums vajadzētu redzēt jauno pieejamo vietu, vismaz "
"failu sistēmām, kuru izmēru virt-resize prot mainīt, un PV.  Lietotājam, "
"iespējams, jāmaina LV izmērs PV iekšpusē, kā arī to failu sistēmu tipu "
"izmērs, kurus virt-resize neprot paplašināt."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:201
msgid "SHRINKING A VIRTUAL MACHINE DISK"
msgstr "VIRTUĀLĀS MAŠĪNAS DISKA SAMAZINĀŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:203
msgid ""
"Shrinking is somewhat more complex than expanding, and only an overview is "
"given here."
msgstr ""
"Samazināšana ir nedaudz sarežģītāka nekā paplašināšana, un šeit sniegts "
"tikai pārskats."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:206
msgid ""
"Firstly virt-resize will not attempt to shrink any partition content (PVs, "
"filesystems).  The user has to shrink content before passing the disk image "
"to virt-resize, and virt-resize will check that the content has been shrunk "
"properly."
msgstr ""
"Pirmkārt, virt-resize nemēģinās samazināt nodalījumu saturu (PV, failu "
"sistēmas).  Lietotājam saturs jāsamazina pirms diska attēla nodošanas virt-"
"resize, un virt-resize pārbaudīs, vai saturs ir pareizi samazināts."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:211
msgid "(Shrinking can also be done offline using L<guestfish(1)>)"
msgstr "(Samazināšanu var veikt arī bezsaistē ar L<guestfish(1)>)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:213
msgid ""
"After shrinking PVs and filesystems, shut down the guest, and proceed with "
"steps 3 and 4 above to allocate a new disk image."
msgstr ""
"Pēc PV un failu sistēmu samazināšanas izslēdziet viesi un turpiniet ar "
"iepriekš minētajiem 3. un 4. soli, lai piešķirtu jaunu diska attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:216
msgid "Then run virt-resize with any of the I<--shrink> and/or I<--resize> options."
msgstr ""
"Pēc tam palaidiet virt-resize ar kādu no opcijām I<--shrink> un/vai I<--"
"resize>."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:219
msgid "IGNORING OR DELETING PARTITIONS"
msgstr "NODALĪJUMU IGNORĒŠANA VAI DZĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:221
msgid ""
"virt-resize also gives a convenient way to ignore or delete partitions when "
"copying from the input disk to the output disk.  Ignoring a partition speeds "
"up the copy where you don't care about the existing contents of a "
"partition.  Deleting a partition removes it completely, but note that it "
"also renumbers any partitions after the one which is deleted, which can "
"leave some guests unbootable."
msgstr ""
"virt-resize nodrošina arī ērtu veidu, kā ignorēt vai izdzēst nodalījumus, "
"kopējot no ievades diska uz izvades disku.  Nodalījuma ignorēšana paātrina "
"kopēšanu, ja nodalījuma esošais saturs nav svarīgs.  Nodalījuma dzēšana to "
"pilnībā noņem, taču ņemiet vērā, ka tas pārnumurē arī visus nodalījumus pēc "
"izdzēstā, kas var padarīt dažus viesus nesāknējamus."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:228
msgid "QCOW2 AND NON-SPARSE RAW FORMATS"
msgstr "QCOW2 UN NERETINĀTI RAW FORMĀTI"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:230
msgid ""
"If the input disk is in qcow2 format, then you may prefer that the output is "
"in qcow2 format as well.  Alternately, virt-resize can convert the format on "
"the fly.  The output format is simply determined by the format of the empty "
"output container that you provide.  Thus to create qcow2 output, use:"
msgstr ""
"Ja ievades disks ir qcow2 formātā, iespējams, vēlēsieties, lai arī izvade "
"būtu qcow2 formātā.  Alternatīvi virt-resize var pārveidot formātu lidojuma "
"laikā.  Izvades formātu vienkārši nosaka jūsu nodrošinātā tukšā izvades "
"konteinera formāts.  Tāpēc, lai izveidotu qcow2 izvadi, izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:236
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" qemu-img create -f qcow2 -o preallocation=metadata outdisk [size]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" qemu-img create -f qcow2 -o preallocation=metadata outdisk [size]\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:238
msgid "instead of the truncate command."
msgstr "komandas truncate vietā."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:240
msgid "Similarly, to get non-sparse raw output use:"
msgstr "Līdzīgi, lai iegūtu neretinātu raw izvadi, izmantojiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:242
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" fallocate -l size outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" fallocate -l size outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:244
msgid ""
"(on older systems that don’t have the L<fallocate(1)> command use C<dd "
"if=/dev/zero of=outdisk bs=1M count=..>)"
msgstr ""
"(vecākās sistēmās, kurās nav komandas L<fallocate(1)>, izmantojiet C<dd if=/"
"dev/zero of=outdisk bs=1M count=..>)"

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:247
msgid "LOGICAL PARTITIONS"
msgstr "LOĢISKIE NODALĪJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:249
msgid ""
"Logical partitions (a.k.a. F</dev/sda5+> on disks using DOS partition "
"tables) cannot be resized."
msgstr ""
"Loģisko nodalījumu (t. s. F</dev/sda5+> diskos ar DOS nodalījumu tabulām) "
"izmēru mainīt nevar."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:252
msgid ""
"To understand what is going on, firstly one of the four partitions "
"F</dev/sda1-4> will have MBR partition type C<05> or C<0f>.  This is called "
"the B<extended partition>.  Use L<virt-filesystems(1)> to see the MBR "
"partition type."
msgstr ""
"Lai saprastu, kas notiek: pirmkārt, vienam no četriem nodalījumiem F</dev/"
"sda1-4> būs MBR nodalījuma tips C<05> vai C<0f>.  To sauc par B<paplašināto "
"nodalījumu>.  MBR nodalījuma tipa apskatei izmantojiet L<virt-filesystems(1)>"
"."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:257
msgid "Logical partitions live inside the extended partition."
msgstr "Loģiskie nodalījumi atrodas paplašinātā nodalījuma iekšpusē."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:259
msgid ""
"The extended partition can be expanded, but not shrunk (unless you force it, "
"which is not advisable).  When the extended partition is copied across, all "
"the logical partitions contained inside are copied over implicitly.  "
"Virt-resize does not look inside the extended partition, so it copies the "
"logical partitions blindly."
msgstr ""
"Paplašināto nodalījumu var paplašināt, bet ne samazināt (ja vien to "
"nepiespiežat, kas nav ieteicams).  Kad paplašinātais nodalījums tiek kopēts, "
"visi tajā esošie loģiskie nodalījumi tiek kopēti netieši.  Virt-resize "
"neskatās paplašinātā nodalījuma iekšienē, tāpēc tas kopē loģiskos "
"nodalījumus akli."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:265
msgid ""
"You cannot specify a logical partition (F</dev/sda5+>) at all on the command "
"line.  Doing so will give an error."
msgstr ""
"Loģisku nodalījumu (F</dev/sda5+>) komandrindā nevar norādīt vispār.  Tas "
"izraisīs kļūdu."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:276
msgid "B<--align-first> B<auto>"
msgstr "B<--align-first> B<auto>"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:278
msgid "B<--align-first> B<never>"
msgstr "B<--align-first> B<never>"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:280
msgid "B<--align-first> B<always>"
msgstr "B<--align-first> B<always>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:282
msgid ""
"Align the first partition for improved performance (see also the "
"I<--alignment> option)."
msgstr ""
"Līdzināt pirmo nodalījumu labākai veiktspējai (skatīt arī opciju I<--"
"alignment>)."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:285
msgid ""
"The default is I<--align-first auto> which only aligns the first partition "
"if it is safe to do so.  That is, only when we know how to fix the "
"bootloader automatically, and at the moment that can only be done for "
"Windows guests."
msgstr ""
"Noklusējums ir I<--align-first auto>, kas līdzina pirmo nodalījumu tikai "
"tad, ja tas ir droši.  Tas ir, tikai tad, ja zinām, kā automātiski izlabot "
"sāknētāju, un pašlaik to var izdarīt tikai Windows viesiem."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:290
msgid ""
"I<--align-first never> means we never move the first partition.  This is the "
"safest option.  Try this if the guest does not boot after resizing."
msgstr ""
"I<--align-first never> nozīmē, ka pirmo nodalījumu nekad nepārvietojam.  Šī "
"ir drošākā opcija.  Izmēģiniet to, ja viesis pēc izmēra maiņas netiek "
"sāknēts."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:294
msgid ""
"I<--align-first always> means we always align the first partition (if it "
"needs to be aligned).  For some guests this will break the bootloader, "
"making the guest unbootable."
msgstr ""
"I<--align-first always> nozīmē, ka pirmo nodalījumu vienmēr līdzinām (ja tas "
"jālīdzina).  Dažiem viesiem tas sabojās sāknētāju, padarot viesi nesāknējamu."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:298
msgid "B<--alignment> N"
msgstr "B<--alignment> N"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:300
msgid ""
"Set the alignment of partitions to C<N> sectors.  The default in virt-resize "
"E<lt> 1.13.19 was 64 sectors, and after that is 128 sectors."
msgstr ""
"Iestatīt nodalījumu līdzinājumu uz C<N> sektoriem.  Virt-resize E<lt> "
"1.13.19 noklusējums bija 64 sektori, pēc tam — 128 sektori."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:304
msgid ""
"Assuming 512 byte sector size inside the guest, here are some suitable "
"values for this:"
msgstr ""
"Pieņemot 512 baitu sektora izmēru viesī, lūk, dažas piemērotas vērtības:"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:309
msgid "I<--alignment 1> (512 bytes)"
msgstr "I<--alignment 1> (512 baiti)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:311
msgid ""
"The partitions would be packed together as closely as possible, but would be "
"completely unaligned.  In some cases this can cause very poor performance.  "
"See L<virt-alignment-scan(1)> for further details."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījumi tiktu sakārtoti cik vien cieši iespējams, bet būtu pilnīgi "
"nelīdzināti.  Dažos gadījumos tas var izraisīt ļoti sliktu veiktspēju.  "
"Sīkāku informāciju skatiet L<virt-alignment-scan(1)>."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:315
msgid "I<--alignment 8> (4K)"
msgstr "I<--alignment 8> (4K)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:317
msgid ""
"This would be the minimum acceptable alignment for reasonable performance on "
"modern hosts."
msgstr ""
"Tas būtu minimālais pieņemamais līdzinājums saprātīgai veiktspējai mūsdienu "
"resursdatoros."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:320
msgid "I<--alignment 128> (64K)"
msgstr "I<--alignment 128> (64K)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:322
msgid ""
"This alignment provides good performance when the host is using high end "
"network storage."
msgstr ""
"Šis līdzinājums nodrošina labu veiktspēju, ja resursdators izmanto augstas "
"klases tīkla krātuvi."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:325
msgid "I<--alignment 2048> (1M)"
msgstr "I<--alignment 2048> (1M)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:327
msgid ""
"This is the standard alignment used by all newly installed guests since "
"around 2008."
msgstr ""
"Šis ir standarta līdzinājums, ko izmanto visi kopš aptuveni 2008. gada "
"jaunuzinstalētie viesi."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:341
msgid "B<-d>"
msgstr "B<-d>"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:343 win-reg/virt-win-reg.in:117
msgid "B<--debug>"
msgstr "B<--debug>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:345
msgid "(Deprecated: use I<-v> option instead)"
msgstr "(Novecojis: tā vietā izmantojiet opciju I<-v>)"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:347 resize/virt-resize.pod:626
#: win-reg/virt-win-reg.in:119
msgid "Enable debugging messages."
msgstr "Iespējot atkļūdošanas ziņojumus."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:349
msgid "B<--delete> PART"
msgstr "B<--delete> PART"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:351
msgid ""
"Delete the named partition.  It would be more accurate to describe this as "
"\"don't copy it over\", since virt-resize doesn't do in-place changes and "
"the original disk image is left intact."
msgstr ""
"Izdzēst nosaukto nodalījumu.  Precīzāk būtu to aprakstīt kā „nekopēt to”, jo "
"virt-resize neveic izmaiņas uz vietas un oriģinālais diska attēls paliek "
"neskarts."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:355
msgid ""
"Note that when you delete a partition, then anything contained in the "
"partition is also deleted.  Furthermore, this causes any partitions that "
"come after to be I<renumbered>, which can easily make your guest unbootable."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā: dzēšot nodalījumu, tiek izdzēsts arī viss nodalījumā esošais.  "
"Turklāt visi tam sekojošie nodalījumi tiek I<pārnumurēti>, kas var viegli "
"padarīt viesi nesāknējamu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:360 resize/virt-resize.pod:437
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:570 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:226
msgid "You can give this option multiple times."
msgstr "Šo opciju var norādīt vairākkārt."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:362
msgid "B<--expand> PART"
msgstr "B<--expand> PART"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:364
msgid ""
"Expand the named partition so it uses up all extra space (space left over "
"after any other resize changes that you request have been done)."
msgstr ""
"Paplašināt nosaukto nodalījumu, lai tas izmantotu visu papildu vietu (vietu, "
"kas paliek pāri pēc visām citām pieprasītajām izmēra izmaiņām)."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:367
msgid ""
"If virt-resize knows how, it will expand the direct content of the "
"partition.  For example, if the partition is an LVM PV, it will expand the "
"PV to fit (like calling L<pvresize(8)>).  Virt-resize leaves any other "
"content it doesn't know about alone."
msgstr ""
"Ja virt-resize prot, tas paplašinās nodalījuma tiešo saturu.  Piemēram, ja "
"nodalījums ir LVM PV, tas paplašinās PV atbilstoši (kā izsaucot L<pvresize"
"(8)>).  Citu saturu, ko tas nepazīst, virt-resize atstāj neskartu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:372
msgid "Currently virt-resize can resize:"
msgstr "Pašlaik virt-resize var mainīt izmēru:"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:378
msgid "ext2, ext3 and ext4 filesystems."
msgstr "ext2, ext3 un ext4 failu sistēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:382
msgid "NTFS filesystems, if libguestfs was compiled with support for NTFS."
msgstr "NTFS failu sistēmām, ja libguestfs ir kompilēta ar NTFS atbalstu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:384
msgid ""
"The filesystem must have been shut down consistently last time it was used.  "
"Additionally, L<ntfsresize(8)> marks the resized filesystem as requiring a "
"consistency check, so at the first boot after resizing Windows will check "
"the disk."
msgstr ""
"Failu sistēmai jābūt konsekventi izslēgtai pēdējā lietošanas reizē.  Turklāt "
"L<ntfsresize(8)> atzīmē mainīto failu sistēmu kā tādu, kurai vajadzīga "
"konsekvences pārbaude, tāpēc pirmajā sāknēšanā pēc izmēra maiņas Windows "
"pārbaudīs disku."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:391
msgid ""
"LVM PVs (physical volumes).  virt-resize does not usually resize anything "
"inside the PV, but see the I<--LV-expand> option.  The user could also "
"resize LVs as desired after boot."
msgstr ""
"LVM PV (fiziskajiem sējumiem).  virt-resize parasti nemaina neko PV "
"iekšpusē, taču skatiet opciju I<--LV-expand>.  Lietotājs pēc sāknēšanas var "
"arī pēc vajadzības mainīt LV izmēru."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:397
msgid "Btrfs filesystems, if libguestfs was compiled with support for btrfs."
msgstr "Btrfs failu sistēmām, ja libguestfs ir kompilēta ar btrfs atbalstu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:401
msgid "XFS filesystems, if libguestfs was compiled with support for XFS."
msgstr "XFS failu sistēmām, ja libguestfs ir kompilēta ar XFS atbalstu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:405
msgid "Linux swap partitions."
msgstr "Linux maiņatmiņas nodalījumiem."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:407
msgid ""
"Please note that libguestfs I<destroys> the existing swap content by "
"recreating it with C<mkswap>, so this should not be used when the guest is "
"suspended."
msgstr ""
"Lūdzu, ņemiet vērā, ka libguestfs I<iznīcina> esošo maiņatmiņas saturu, "
"izveidojot to no jauna ar C<mkswap>, tāpēc to nevajadzētu izmantot, ja "
"viesis ir iesnaudināts."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:413
msgid "f2fs filesystems, if libguestfs was compiled with support for f2fs."
msgstr "f2fs failu sistēmām, ja libguestfs ir kompilēta ar f2fs atbalstu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:417 resize/virt-resize.pod:598
msgid "Note that you cannot use I<--expand> and I<--shrink> together."
msgstr "Ņemiet vērā, ka I<--expand> un I<--shrink> nevar izmantot kopā."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:419
msgid "B<--format> B<raw>"
msgstr "B<--format> B<raw>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:421 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:206
msgid ""
"Specify the format of the input disk image.  If this flag is not given then "
"it is auto-detected from the image itself."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt ievades diska attēla formātu.  Ja šis karogs nav norādīts, formāts "
"tiek automātiski noteikts no paša attēla."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:427
msgid ""
"Note that this option I<does not> affect the output format.  See L</QCOW2 "
"AND NON-SPARSE RAW FORMATS>."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šī opcija I<neietekmē> izvades formātu.  Skatiet L</QCOW2 UN "
"NERETINĀTI RAW FORMĀTI>."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:430
msgid "B<--ignore> PART"
msgstr "B<--ignore> PART"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:432
msgid ""
"Ignore the named partition.  Effectively this means the partition is "
"allocated on the destination disk, but the content is not copied across from "
"the source disk.  The content of the partition will be blank (all zero "
"bytes)."
msgstr ""
"Ignorēt nosaukto nodalījumu.  Faktiski tas nozīmē, ka nodalījums tiek "
"piešķirts mērķa diskā, bet saturs no avota diska netiek kopēts.  Nodalījuma "
"saturs būs tukšs (visi nulles baiti)."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:439
msgid "B<--LV-expand> LOGVOL"
msgstr "B<--LV-expand> LOGVOL"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:441
msgid ""
"This takes the logical volume and, as a final step, expands it to fill all "
"the space available in its volume group.  A typical usage, assuming a Linux "
"guest with a single PV F</dev/sda2> and a root device called "
"F</dev/vg_guest/lv_root> would be:"
msgstr ""
"Tas ņem loģisko sējumu un pēdējā solī paplašina to, lai aizpildītu visu tā "
"sējumu grupā pieejamo vietu.  Tipisks lietojums, pieņemot Linux viesi ar "
"vienu PV F</dev/sda2> un saknes ierīci F</dev/vg_guest/lv_root>, būtu:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:446
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-resize indisk outdisk \\\n"
"   --expand /dev/sda2 --LV-expand /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-resize indisk outdisk \\\n"
"   --expand /dev/sda2 --LV-expand /dev/vg_guest/lv_root\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:449
msgid ""
"This would first expand the partition (and PV), and then expand the root "
"device to fill the extra space in the PV."
msgstr ""
"Tas vispirms paplašinātu nodalījumu (un PV) un pēc tam paplašinātu saknes "
"ierīci, lai aizpildītu papildu vietu PV."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:452
msgid ""
"The contents of the LV are also resized if virt-resize knows how to do "
"that.  You can stop virt-resize from trying to expand the content by using "
"the option I<--no-expand-content>."
msgstr ""
"Ja virt-resize prot, tiek mainīts arī LV satura izmērs.  Ar opciju I<--no-"
"expand-content> var neļaut virt-resize mēģināt paplašināt saturu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:456
msgid "Use L<virt-filesystems(1)> to list the filesystems in the guest."
msgstr "Viesa failu sistēmu uzskaitīšanai izmantojiet L<virt-filesystems(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:458
msgid ""
"You can give this option multiple times, I<but> it doesn't make sense to do "
"this unless the logical volumes you specify are all in different volume "
"groups."
msgstr ""
"Šo opciju var norādīt vairākkārt, I<taču> tam nav jēgas, ja vien norādītie "
"loģiskie sējumi nav visi dažādās sējumu grupās."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:474
msgid "Print a summary of what would be done, but don’t do anything."
msgstr "Izdrukāt kopsavilkumu par to, kas tiktu darīts, bet neko nedarīt."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:476
msgid "B<--no-copy-boot-loader>"
msgstr "B<--no-copy-boot-loader>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:478
msgid ""
"By default, virt-resize copies over some sectors at the start of the disk "
"(up to the beginning of the first partition).  Commonly these sectors "
"contain the Master Boot Record (MBR) and the boot loader, and are required "
"in order for the guest to boot correctly."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma virt-resize kopē dažus sektorus diska sākumā (līdz pirmā "
"nodalījuma sākumam).  Parasti šajos sektoros ir galvenais sāknēšanas "
"ieraksts (MBR) un sāknētājs, un tie vajadzīgi pareizai viesa sāknēšanai."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:483
msgid ""
"If you specify this flag, then this initial copy is not done.  You may need "
"to reinstall the boot loader in this case."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādāt šo karogu, šī sākotnējā kopēšana netiek veikta.  Šajā gadījumā, "
"iespējams, būs jāpārinstalē sāknētājs."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:486
msgid "B<--no-extra-partition>"
msgstr "B<--no-extra-partition>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:488
msgid ""
"By default, virt-resize creates an extra partition if there is any extra, "
"unused space after all resizing has happened.  Use this option to prevent "
"the extra partition from being created.  If you do this then the extra space "
"will be inaccessible until you run fdisk, parted, or some other partitioning "
"tool in the guest."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma virt-resize izveido papildu nodalījumu, ja pēc visām izmēra "
"izmaiņām paliek papildu neizmantota vieta.  Izmantojiet šo opciju, lai "
"papildu nodalījums netiktu izveidots.  Tādā gadījumā papildu vieta nebūs "
"pieejama, kamēr viesī neizpildīsiet fdisk, parted vai citu nodalīšanas rīku."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:494
msgid ""
"Note that if the surplus space is smaller than 10 MB, no extra partition "
"will be created."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā: ja liekā vieta ir mazāka par 10 MB, papildu nodalījums netiks "
"izveidots."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:497
msgid "B<--no-expand-content>"
msgstr "B<--no-expand-content>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:499
msgid ""
"By default, virt-resize will try to expand the direct contents of "
"partitions, if it knows how (see I<--expand> option above)."
msgstr ""
"Pēc noklusējuma virt-resize, ja prot, mēģinās paplašināt nodalījumu tiešo "
"saturu (skatiet opciju I<--expand> iepriekš)."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:502
msgid ""
"If you give the I<--no-expand-content> option then virt-resize will not "
"attempt this."
msgstr "Ja norādāt opciju I<--no-expand-content>, virt-resize to nemēģinās."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:505
msgid "B<--no-sparse>"
msgstr "B<--no-sparse>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:507
msgid "Turn off sparse copying.  See L</SPARSE COPYING> below."
msgstr "Izslēgt retināto kopēšanu.  Skatiet L</RETINĀTA KOPĒŠANA> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:509
msgid "B<--ntfsresize-force>"
msgstr "B<--ntfsresize-force>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:511
msgid ""
"Pass the I<--force> option to L<ntfsresize(8)>, allowing resizing even if "
"the NTFS disk is marked as needing a consistency check.  You have to use "
"this option if you want to resize a Windows guest multiple times without "
"booting into Windows between each resize."
msgstr ""
"Nodot L<ntfsresize(8)> opciju I<--force>, ļaujot mainīt izmēru, pat ja NTFS "
"disks ir atzīmēts kā tāds, kuram vajadzīga konsekvences pārbaude.  Šī opcija "
"jāizmanto, ja vēlaties Windows viesa izmēru mainīt vairākkārt, starp "
"izmaiņām nesāknējot Windows."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:517
msgid "B<--output-format> B<raw>"
msgstr "B<--output-format> B<raw>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:519
msgid ""
"Specify the format of the output disk image.  If this flag is not given then "
"it is auto-detected from the image itself."
msgstr ""
"Norādīt izvades diska attēla formātu.  Ja šis karogs nav norādīts, formāts "
"tiek automātiski noteikts no paša attēla."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:525
msgid ""
"Note that this option I<does not create> the output format.  This option "
"just tells libguestfs what it is so it doesn't try to guess it.  You still "
"need to create the output disk with the right format.  See L</QCOW2 AND "
"NON-SPARSE RAW FORMATS>."
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā, ka šī opcija I<neizveido> izvades formātu.  Šī opcija tikai "
"pasaka libguestfs, kāds tas ir, lai tas nemēģinātu to minēt.  Izvades disks "
"joprojām jāizveido ar pareizo formātu.  Skatiet L</QCOW2 UN NERETINĀTI RAW "
"FORMĀTI>."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:534
msgid "Don’t print the summary."
msgstr "Nedrukāt kopsavilkumu."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:536
msgid "B<--resize> PART=SIZE"
msgstr "B<--resize> PART=SIZE"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:538
msgid ""
"Resize the named partition (expanding or shrinking it) so that it has the "
"given size."
msgstr ""
"Mainīt nosauktā nodalījuma izmēru (paplašinot vai samazinot), lai tam būtu "
"norādītais izmērs."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:541
msgid ""
"C<SIZE> can be expressed as an absolute number followed by b/K/M/G to mean "
"bytes, Kilobytes, Megabytes, or Gigabytes; or as a percentage of the current "
"size; or as a relative number or percentage.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"C<SIZE> var izteikt kā absolūtu skaitli, kam seko b/K/M/G, kas nozīmē "
"baitus, kilobaitus, megabaitus vai gigabaitus; vai kā procentus no "
"pašreizējā izmēra; vai kā relatīvu skaitli vai procentus.  Piemēram:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:547
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" --resize /dev/sda2=10G\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" --resize /dev/sda2=10G\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:549
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" --resize /dev/sda4=90%\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" --resize /dev/sda4=90%\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:551
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" --resize /dev/sda2=+1G\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" --resize /dev/sda2=+1G\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:553
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" --resize /dev/sda2=-200M\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" --resize /dev/sda2=-200M\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:555
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" --resize /dev/sda1=+128K\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" --resize /dev/sda1=+128K\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:557
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" --resize /dev/sda1=+10%\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" --resize /dev/sda1=+10%\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:559
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" --resize /dev/sda1=-10%\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" --resize /dev/sda1=-10%\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:561
msgid ""
"You can increase the size of any partition.  Virt-resize will expand the "
"direct content of the partition if it knows how (see I<--expand> above)."
msgstr ""
"Jebkura nodalījuma izmēru var palielināt.  Virt-resize, ja prot, paplašinās "
"nodalījuma tiešo saturu (skatiet I<--expand> iepriekš)."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:565
msgid ""
"You can only I<decrease> the size of partitions that contain filesystems or "
"PVs which have already been shrunk.  Virt-resize will check this has been "
"done before proceeding, or else will print an error (see also "
"I<--resize-force>)."
msgstr ""
"I<Samazināt> var tikai to nodalījumu izmēru, kuros esošās failu sistēmas vai "
"PV jau ir samazinātas.  Virt-resize pirms turpināšanas pārbaudīs, vai tas "
"izdarīts, vai citādi izdrukās kļūdu (skatīt arī I<--resize-force>)."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:572
msgid "B<--resize-force> PART=SIZE"
msgstr "B<--resize-force> PART=SIZE"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:574
msgid ""
"This is the same as I<--resize> except that it will let you decrease the "
"size of any partition.  Generally this means you will lose any data which "
"was at the end of the partition you shrink, but you may not care about that "
"(eg. if shrinking an unused partition, or if you can easily recreate it such "
"as a swap partition)."
msgstr ""
"Tas ir tas pats, kas I<--resize>, izņemot to, ka tas ļaus samazināt jebkura "
"nodalījuma izmēru.  Parasti tas nozīmē, ka zaudēsiet visus datus samazināmā "
"nodalījuma beigās, taču tas var nebūt svarīgi (piem., samazinot neizmantotu "
"nodalījumu vai ja to var viegli izveidot no jauna, piemēram, maiņatmiņas "
"nodalījumu)."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:580
msgid "See also the I<--ignore> option."
msgstr "Skatīt arī opciju I<--ignore>."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:582
msgid "B<--shrink> PART"
msgstr "B<--shrink> PART"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:584
msgid ""
"Shrink the named partition until the overall disk image fits in the "
"destination.  The named partition B<must> contain a filesystem or PV which "
"has already been shrunk using another tool (eg. L<guestfish(1)> or other "
"online tools).  Virt-resize will check this and give an error if it has not "
"been done."
msgstr ""
"Samazināt nosaukto nodalījumu, līdz viss diska attēls ietilpst mērķī.  "
"Nosauktajā nodalījumā B<jābūt> failu sistēmai vai PV, kas jau samazināta ar "
"citu rīku (piem., L<guestfish(1)> vai citiem tiešsaistes rīkiem).  Virt-"
"resize to pārbaudīs un izdos kļūdu, ja tas nav izdarīts."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:590
msgid ""
"The amount by which the overall disk must be shrunk (after carrying out all "
"other operations requested by the user) is called the \"deficit\".  For "
"example, a straight copy (assume no other operations)  from a 5GB disk image "
"to a 4GB disk image results in a 1GB deficit.  In this case, virt-resize "
"would give an error unless the user specified a partition to shrink and that "
"partition had more than a gigabyte of free space."
msgstr ""
"Apjomu, par kādu jāsamazina viss disks (pēc visu citu lietotāja pieprasīto "
"darbību veikšanas), sauc par „deficītu”.  Piemēram, vienkārša kopēšana "
"(pieņemot, ka citu darbību nav) no 5GB diska attēla uz 4GB diska attēlu rada "
"1GB deficītu.  Šajā gadījumā virt-resize izdotu kļūdu, ja vien lietotājs "
"nebūtu norādījis samazināmo nodalījumu un šajā nodalījumā nebūtu vairāk nekā "
"gigabaits brīvas vietas."

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:600
msgid "B<--unknown-filesystems> B<ignore>"
msgstr "B<--unknown-filesystems> B<ignore>"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:602
msgid "B<--unknown-filesystems> B<warn>"
msgstr "B<--unknown-filesystems> B<warn>"

#. type: =item
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:604
msgid "B<--unknown-filesystems> B<error>"
msgstr "B<--unknown-filesystems> B<error>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:606
msgid ""
"Configure the behaviour of virt-resize when asking to expand a filesystem, "
"and neither libguestfs has the support it, nor virt-resize knows how to "
"expand the content of the filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Konfigurēt virt-resize rīcību, ja tiek prasīts paplašināt failu sistēmu, bet "
"ne libguestfs to atbalsta, ne virt-resize prot paplašināt failu sistēmas "
"saturu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:610
msgid ""
"I<--unknown-filesystems ignore> will cause virt-resize to silently ignore "
"such filesystems, and nothing is printed about them."
msgstr ""
"I<--unknown-filesystems ignore> liks virt-resize šādas failu sistēmas klusi "
"ignorēt, un par tām nekas netiek izdrukāts."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:613
msgid ""
"I<--unknown-filesystems warn> (the default behaviour) will cause virt-resize "
"to warn for each of the filesystem that cannot be expanded, but still "
"continuing to resize the disk."
msgstr ""
"I<--unknown-filesystems warn> (noklusējuma rīcība) liks virt-resize brīdināt "
"par katru failu sistēmu, kuru nevar paplašināt, bet tomēr turpināt diska "
"izmēra maiņu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:617
msgid ""
"I<--unknown-filesystems error> will cause virt-resize to error out at the "
"first filesystem that cannot be expanded."
msgstr ""
"I<--unknown-filesystems error> liks virt-resize izdot kļūdu pie pirmās failu "
"sistēmas, kuru nevar paplašināt."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:620
msgid ""
"See also L</\"unknown/unavailable method for expanding the TYPE filesystem "
"on DEVICE/LV\">."
msgstr ""
"Skatīt arī L</unknown/unavailable method for expanding the TYPE filesystem "
"on DEVICE/LV>."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:648
msgid ""
"The I<--machine-readable> option can be used to make the output more machine "
"friendly, which is useful when calling virt-resize from other programs, GUIs "
"etc."
msgstr ""
"Opciju I<--machine-readable> var izmantot, lai padarītu izvadi ērtāku "
"mašīnapstrādei, kas noder, izsaucot virt-resize no citām programmām, "
"grafiskām saskarnēm u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:652 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:366
msgid "There are two ways to use this option."
msgstr "Šo opciju var izmantot divos veidos."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:654
msgid ""
"Firstly use the option on its own to query the capabilities of the "
"virt-resize binary.  Typical output looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Pirmkārt, izmantojiet opciju vienu pašu, lai noskaidrotu virt-resize binārā "
"faila spējas.  Tipiska izvade izskatās šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:657
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-resize --machine-readable\n"
" virt-resize\n"
" ntfsresize-force\n"
" 32bitok\n"
" ntfs\n"
" btrfs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-resize --machine-readable\n"
" virt-resize\n"
" ntfsresize-force\n"
" 32bitok\n"
" ntfs\n"
" btrfs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:667 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:379
msgid ""
"Secondly use the option in conjunction with other options to make the "
"regular program output more machine friendly."
msgstr ""
"Otrkārt, izmantojiet opciju kopā ar citām opcijām, lai padarītu parasto "
"programmas izvadi ērtāku mašīnapstrādei."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:670 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:382
msgid "At the moment this means:"
msgstr "Pašlaik tas nozīmē:"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:676 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:388
msgid ""
"Progress bar messages can be parsed from stdout by looking for this regular "
"expression:"
msgstr ""
"Progresa joslas ziņojumus var parsēt no standartizvades, meklējot šo "
"regulāro izteiksmi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:679 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:391
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ^[0-9]+/[0-9]+$\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" ^[0-9]+/[0-9]+$\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:683 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:395
msgid ""
"The calling program should treat messages sent to stdout (except for "
"progress bar messages) as status messages.  They can be logged and/or "
"displayed to the user."
msgstr ""
"Izsaucošajai programmai standartizvadē sūtītie ziņojumi (izņemot progresa "
"joslas ziņojumus) jāuzskata par statusa ziņojumiem.  Tos var žurnalēt un/vai "
"parādīt lietotājam."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:689
msgid ""
"The calling program should treat messages sent to stderr as error messages.  "
"In addition, virt-resize exits with a non-zero status code if there was a "
"fatal error."
msgstr ""
"Izsaucošajai programmai standartkļūdu izvadē sūtītie ziņojumi jāuzskata par "
"kļūdu ziņojumiem.  Turklāt fatālas kļūdas gadījumā virt-resize iziet ar "
"statusa kodu, kas nav nulle."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:695
msgid ""
"Versions of the program prior to 1.13.9 did not support the "
"I<--machine-readable> option and will return an error."
msgstr ""
"Programmas versijas pirms 1.13.9 neatbalstīja opciju I<--machine-readable> "
"un atgriezīs kļūdu."

#. type: =head1
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:701 sysprep/virt-sysprep.pod:351
msgid "NOTES"
msgstr "PIEZĪMES"

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:703
msgid "\"Partition 1 does not end on cylinder boundary.\""
msgstr "\"Partition 1 does not end on cylinder boundary.\""

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:705
msgid ""
"Virt-resize aligns partitions to multiples of 128 sectors (see the "
"I<--alignment> parameter).  Usually this means the partitions will not be "
"aligned to the ancient CHS geometry.  However CHS geometry is meaningless "
"for disks manufactured since the early 1990s, and doubly so for virtual hard "
"drives.  Alignment of partitions to cylinders is not required by any modern "
"operating system."
msgstr ""
"Virt-resize līdzina nodalījumus pie 128 sektoru daudzkārtņiem (skatiet "
"parametru I<--alignment>).  Parasti tas nozīmē, ka nodalījumi netiks "
"līdzināti ar seno CHS ģeometriju.  Tomēr CHS ģeometrijai nav nozīmes "
"diskiem, kas ražoti kopš 1990. gadu sākuma, un vēl jo mazāk virtuāliem "
"cietajiem diskiem.  Nevienai mūsdienu operētājsistēmai nodalījumu "
"līdzināšana ar cilindriem nav vajadzīga."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:712
msgid "GUEST BOOT STUCK AT \"GRUB\""
msgstr "VIESA SĀKNĒŠANA IESTRĒGST PIE „GRUB”"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:714
msgid ""
"If a Linux guest does not boot after resizing, and the boot is stuck after "
"printing C<GRUB> on the console, try reinstalling grub."
msgstr ""
"Ja Linux viesis pēc izmēra maiņas netiek sāknēts un sāknēšana iestrēgst pēc "
"C<GRUB> izdrukāšanas konsolē, mēģiniet pārinstalēt grub."

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:717
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" guestfish -i -a newdisk\n"
" ><fs> cat /boot/grub/device.map\n"
" # check the contents of this file are sensible or\n"
" # edit the file if necessary\n"
" ><fs> grub-install / /dev/vda\n"
" ><fs> exit\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" guestfish -i -a newdisk\n"
" ><fs> cat /boot/grub/device.map\n"
" # check the contents of this file are sensible or\n"
" # edit the file if necessary\n"
" ><fs> grub-install / /dev/vda\n"
" ><fs> exit\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:724
msgid ""
"For more flexible guest reconfiguration, including if you need to specify "
"other parameters to grub-install, use L<virt-rescue(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Elastīgākai viesa pārkonfigurēšanai, ieskaitot gadījumus, kad grub-install "
"jānorāda citi parametri, izmantojiet L<virt-rescue(1)>."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:727
msgid "RESIZING WINDOWS BOOT PARTITIONS"
msgstr "WINDOWS SĀKNĒŠANAS NODALĪJUMU IZMĒRA MAIŅA"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:729
msgid ""
"In Windows Vista and later versions, Microsoft switched to using a separate "
"boot partition.  In these VMs, typically F</dev/sda1> is the boot partition "
"and F</dev/sda2> is the main (C:) drive.  Resizing the first (boot) "
"partition causes the bootloader to fail with C<0xC0000225> error.  Resizing "
"the second partition (ie. C: drive)  should work."
msgstr ""
"Windows Vista un jaunākās versijās Microsoft pārgāja uz atsevišķa sāknēšanas "
"nodalījuma izmantošanu.  Šajās VM parasti F</dev/sda1> ir sāknēšanas "
"nodalījums un F</dev/sda2> ir galvenais (C:) disks.  Pirmā (sāknēšanas) "
"nodalījuma izmēra maiņa izraisa sāknētāja kļūmi ar kļūdu C<0xC0000225>.  "
"Otrā nodalījuma (t. i., C: diska) izmēra maiņai vajadzētu darboties."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:736
msgid "WINDOWS CHKDSK"
msgstr "WINDOWS CHKDSK"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:738
msgid ""
"Windows disks which use NTFS must be consistent before virt-resize can be "
"used.  If the ntfsresize operation fails, try booting the original VM and "
"running C<chkdsk /f> on all NTFS partitions, then shut down the VM cleanly.  "
"For further information see: "
"L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=975753>"
msgstr ""
"Windows diskiem, kas izmanto NTFS, jābūt konsekventiem, pirms var izmantot "
"virt-resize.  Ja ntfsresize darbība neizdodas, mēģiniet sāknēt oriģinālo VM "
"un izpildīt C<chkdsk /f> visos NTFS nodalījumos, pēc tam pareizi izslēdziet "
"VM.  Plašāku informāciju skatiet: L<https://bugzilla.redhat.com/"
"show_bug.cgi?id=975753>"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:744
msgid ""
"I<After resize> Windows may initiate a lengthy \"chkdsk\" on first boot if "
"NTFS partitions have been expanded.  This is just a safety check and (unless "
"it find errors) is nothing to worry about."
msgstr ""
"I<Pēc izmēra maiņas> Windows pirmajā sāknēšanā var sākt ilgstošu „chkdsk”, "
"ja NTFS nodalījumi ir paplašināti.  Tā ir tikai drošības pārbaude, un (ja "
"vien tā neatrod kļūdas) par to nav jāuztraucas."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:748
msgid "WINDOWS UNMOUNTABLE_BOOT_VOLUME BSOD"
msgstr "WINDOWS UNMOUNTABLE_BOOT_VOLUME BSOD"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:750
msgid ""
"After sysprepping a Windows guest and then resizing it with virt-resize, you "
"may see the guest fail to boot with an C<UNMOUNTABLE_BOOT_VOLUME> BSOD.  "
"This error is caused by having C<ExtendOemPartition=1> in the sysprep.inf "
"file.  Removing this line before sysprepping should fix the problem."
msgstr ""
"Pēc Windows viesa sysprep un tā izmēra maiņas ar virt-resize var gadīties, "
"ka viesis netiek sāknēts ar BSOD C<UNMOUNTABLE_BOOT_VOLUME>.  Šo kļūdu "
"izraisa C<ExtendOemPartition=1> failā sysprep.inf.  Šīs rindas noņemšanai "
"pirms sysprep vajadzētu novērst problēmu."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:756 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:413
#: win-reg/virt-win-reg.in:638
msgid "WINDOWS 8"
msgstr "WINDOWS 8"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:758
msgid ""
"Windows 8 \"fast startup\" can prevent virt-resize from resizing NTFS "
"partitions.  See L<guestfs(3)/WINDOWS HIBERNATION AND WINDOWS 8 FAST "
"STARTUP>."
msgstr ""
"Windows 8 „ātrā startēšana” var neļaut virt-resize mainīt NTFS nodalījumu "
"izmēru.  Skatiet L<guestfs(3)/WINDOWS HIBERNĀCIJA UN WINDOWS 8 ĀTRĀ "
"STARTĒŠANA>."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:762
msgid "SPARSE COPYING"
msgstr "RETINĀTA KOPĒŠANA"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:764
msgid "You should create a fresh, zeroed target disk image for virt-resize to use."
msgstr ""
"Virt-resize izmantošanai jāizveido jauns, ar nullēm aizpildīts mērķa diska "
"attēls."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:767
msgid ""
"Virt-resize by default performs sparse copying.  This means that it does not "
"copy blocks from the source disk which are all zeroes.  This improves speed "
"and efficiency, but will produce incorrect results if the target disk image "
"contains unzeroed data."
msgstr ""
"Virt-resize pēc noklusējuma veic retināto kopēšanu.  Tas nozīmē, ka tas "
"nekopē avota diska blokus, kas sastāv tikai no nullēm.  Tas uzlabo ātrumu un "
"efektivitāti, taču radīs nepareizus rezultātus, ja mērķa diska attēlā ir "
"nenullēti dati."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:772
msgid ""
"The main time this can be a problem is if the target is a host partition "
"(eg. S<C<virt-resize source.img /dev/sda4>>) because the usual partitioning "
"tools tend to leave whatever data happened to be on the disk before."
msgstr ""
"Galvenokārt tā var būt problēma, ja mērķis ir resursdatora nodalījums "
"(piem., S<C<virt-resize source.img /dev/sda4>>), jo parastie nodalīšanas "
"rīki mēdz atstāt jebkurus datus, kas diskā bija iepriekš."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:777
msgid ""
"If you have to reuse a target which contains data already, you should use "
"the I<--no-sparse> option.  Note this can be much slower."
msgstr ""
"Ja jāizmanto atkārtoti mērķis, kurā jau ir dati, izmantojiet opciju I<--no-"
"sparse>.  Ņemiet vērā, ka tas var būt daudz lēnāk."

#. type: =head2
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:780
msgid ""
"\"unknown/unavailable method for expanding the TYPE filesystem on "
"DEVICE/LV\""
msgstr ""
"\"unknown/unavailable method for expanding the TYPE filesystem on DEVICE/LV\""

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:782
msgid ""
"Virt-resize was asked to expand a partition or a logical volume containing a "
"filesystem with the type C<TYPE>, but there is no available nor known "
"expanding method for that filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Virt-resize tika lūgts paplašināt nodalījumu vai loģisko sējumu ar C<TYPE> "
"tipa failu sistēmu, taču šai failu sistēmai nav pieejamas vai zināmas "
"paplašināšanas metodes."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:786
msgid "This may be due to either of the following:"
msgstr "Tam var būt kāds no šiem iemesliem:"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:792
msgid ""
"There corresponding filesystem is not available in libguestfs, because there "
"is no proper package in the host with utilities for it.  This is usually the "
"case for C<btrfs>, C<ntfs>, C<xfs>, and C<f2fs> filesystems."
msgstr ""
"Attiecīgā failu sistēma libguestfs nav pieejama, jo resursdatorā nav "
"piemērotas pakotnes ar tās utilītām.  Parasti tā ir C<btrfs>, C<ntfs>, "
"C<xfs> un C<f2fs> failu sistēmām."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:797
msgid "Check the results of:"
msgstr "Pārbaudiet šīs komandas rezultātus:"

#. type: verbatim
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:799
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-resize --machine-readable\n"
" guestfish -a /dev/null run : available\n"
" guestfish -a /dev/null run : filesystem_available TYPE\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-resize --machine-readable\n"
" guestfish -a /dev/null run : available\n"
" guestfish -a /dev/null run : filesystem_available TYPE\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:803
msgid ""
"In this case, it is enough to install the proper packages adding support for "
"them.  For example, C<libguestfs-xfs> on Red Hat Enterprise Linux, CentOS, "
"Debian, Ubuntu, and distributions derived from them, for supporting the "
"C<xfs> filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Šajā gadījumā pietiek instalēt piemērotās pakotnes, kas pievieno to "
"atbalstu.  Piemēram, C<libguestfs-xfs> Red Hat Enterprise Linux, CentOS, "
"Debian, Ubuntu un no tām atvasinātās distribūcijās failu sistēmas C<xfs> "
"atbalstam."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:810
msgid "Virt-resize has no support for expanding that type of filesystem."
msgstr "Virt-resize neatbalsta šāda tipa failu sistēmas paplašināšanu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:812
msgid ""
"In this case, there’s nothing that can be done to let virt-resize expand "
"that type of filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Šajā gadījumā neko nevar darīt, lai virt-resize paplašinātu šāda tipa failu "
"sistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:817
msgid ""
"In both cases, virt-resize will not expand the mentioned filesystem; the "
"result (unless I<--unknown-filesystems error> is specified)  is that the "
"partitions containing such filesystems will be actually bigger as requested, "
"but the filesystems will still be usable at their older sizes."
msgstr ""
"Abos gadījumos virt-resize minēto failu sistēmu nepaplašinās; rezultāts (ja "
"vien nav norādīts I<--unknown-filesystems error>) ir tāds, ka nodalījumi ar "
"šādām failu sistēmām faktiski būs lielāki, kā pieprasīts, bet failu sistēmas "
"joprojām būs lietojamas savos vecajos izmēros."

#. type: =head1
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:823
msgid "ALTERNATIVE TOOLS"
msgstr "ALTERNATĪVI RĪKI"

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:825
msgid ""
"There are several proprietary tools for resizing partitions.  We won't "
"mention any here."
msgstr ""
"Nodalījumu izmēra maiņai ir vairāki patentēti rīki.  Šeit tos neminēsim."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:828
msgid ""
"L<parted(8)> and its graphical shell gparted can do some types of resizing "
"operations on disk images.  They can resize and move partitions, but I don't "
"think they can do anything with the contents, and they certainly don't "
"understand LVM."
msgstr ""
"L<parted(8)> un tā grafiskā čaula gparted var veikt dažus izmēra maiņas "
"darbību veidus disku attēlos.  Tie var mainīt nodalījumu izmēru un tos "
"pārvietot, taču, manuprāt, ar saturu tie neko darīt nevar, un LVM tie "
"noteikti nesaprot."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:833
msgid ""
"L<guestfish(1)> can do everything that virt-resize can do and a lot more, "
"but at a much lower level.  You will probably end up hand-calculating sector "
"offsets, which is something that virt-resize was designed to avoid.  If you "
"want to see the guestfish-equivalent commands that virt-resize runs, use the "
"I<--debug> flag."
msgstr ""
"L<guestfish(1)> var darīt visu, ko var virt-resize, un daudz ko vairāk, taču "
"daudz zemākā līmenī.  Visticamāk, nāksies manuāli rēķināt sektoru nobīdes — "
"tieši no tā virt-resize bija paredzēts izvairīties.  Ja vēlaties redzēt "
"guestfish ekvivalentās komandas, ko izpilda virt-resize, izmantojiet karogu "
"I<--debug>."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:839
msgid ""
"L<dracut(8)> includes a module called C<dracut-modules-growroot> which can "
"be used to grow the root partition when the guest first boots up.  There is "
"documentation for this module in an associated README file."
msgstr ""
"L<dracut(8)> ietver moduli C<dracut-modules-growroot>, ko var izmantot "
"saknes nodalījuma palielināšanai viesa pirmajā sāknēšanā.  Šī moduļa "
"dokumentācija ir saistītajā README failā."

#. type: textblock
#: resize/virt-resize.pod:850
msgid ""
"L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-df(1)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, "
"L<lvm(8)>, L<pvresize(8)>, L<lvresize(8)>, L<resize2fs(8)>, "
"L<ntfsresize(8)>, L<btrfs(8)>, L<xfs_growfs(8)>, L<resize.f2fs(8)>, "
"L<virsh(1)>, L<parted(8)>, L<truncate(1)>, L<fallocate(1)>, L<grub(8)>, "
"L<grub-install(8)>, L<virt-rescue(1)>, L<virt-sparsify(1)>, "
"L<virt-alignment-scan(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-df(1)>, L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<lvm"
"(8)>, L<pvresize(8)>, L<lvresize(8)>, L<resize2fs(8)>, L<ntfsresize(8)>, "
"L<btrfs(8)>, L<xfs_growfs(8)>, L<resize.f2fs(8)>, L<virsh(1)>, L<parted(8)>, "
"L<truncate(1)>, L<fallocate(1)>, L<grub(8)>, L<grub-install(8)>, L<virt-"
"rescue(1)>, L<virt-sparsify(1)>, L<virt-alignment-scan(1)>, L<http://"
"libguestfs.org/>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:3
msgid "virt-sparsify - Make a virtual machine disk sparse"
msgstr "virt-sparsify - padarīt virtuālās mašīnas disku retinātu"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify [--options] indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify [--options] indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify [--options] --in-place disk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify [--options] --in-place disk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:13
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify is a tool which can make a virtual machine disk (or any disk "
"image) sparse a.k.a. thin-provisioned.  This means that free space within "
"the disk image can be converted back to free space on the host."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify ir rīks, kas var padarīt virtuālās mašīnas disku (vai jebkuru "
"diska attēlu) retinātu jeb plāni nodrošinātu.  Tas nozīmē, ka brīvo vietu "
"diska attēlā var pārvērst atpakaļ par brīvu vietu resursdatorā."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:18
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify can locate and sparsify free space in most filesystems "
"(eg. ext2/3/4, btrfs, NTFS, etc.), and also in LVM physical volumes."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify var atrast un retināt brīvo vietu vairumā failu sistēmu "
"(piem., ext2/3/4, btrfs, NTFS u. c.), kā arī LVM fiziskajos sējumos."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:21
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify can also convert between some disk formats, for example "
"converting a raw disk image to a thin-provisioned qcow2 image."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify var arī pārveidot starp dažiem disku formātiem, piemēram, "
"pārveidot raw diska attēlu par plāni nodrošinātu qcow2 attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:24
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify can operate on any disk image, not just ones from virtual "
"machines.  However if a virtual machine has multiple disks and uses volume "
"management, then virt-sparsify will work but not be very effective "
"(L<http://bugzilla.redhat.com/887826>)."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify var strādāt ar jebkuru diska attēlu, ne tikai ar virtuālo "
"mašīnu attēliem.  Tomēr, ja virtuālajai mašīnai ir vairāki diski un tā "
"izmanto sējumu pārvaldību, virt-sparsify darbosies, bet nebūs ļoti efektīvs "
"(L<http://bugzilla.redhat.com/887826>)."

#. type: =head2
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:29
msgid "IMPORTANT NOTE ABOUT SPARSE OUTPUT IMAGES"
msgstr "SVARĪGA PIEZĪME PAR RETINĀTIEM IZVADES ATTĒLIEM"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:31
msgid ""
"If the input is raw, then the default output is raw sparse.  B<You must "
"check the output size using a tool that understands sparseness> such as C<du "
"-sh>.  It can make a huge difference:"
msgstr ""
"Ja ievade ir raw, noklusējuma izvade ir raw retināts.  B<Izvades izmērs "
"jāpārbauda ar rīku, kas saprot retinātību>, piemēram, C<du -sh>.  Atšķirība "
"var būt milzīga:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ ls -lh test1.img\n"
" -rw-rw-r--. 1 rjones rjones 100M Aug  8 08:08 test1.img\n"
" $ du -sh test1.img\n"
" 3.6M\ttest1.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ ls -lh test1.img\n"
" -rw-rw-r--. 1 rjones rjones 100M Aug  8 08:08 test1.img\n"
" $ du -sh test1.img\n"
" 3.6M\ttest1.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:40
msgid "(Compare the apparent size B<100M> vs the actual size B<3.6M>)"
msgstr "(Salīdziniet šķietamo izmēru B<100M> ar faktisko izmēru B<3.6M>)"

#. type: =head2
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:42
msgid "IMPORTANT LIMITATIONS"
msgstr "SVARĪGI IEROBEŽOJUMI"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:48
msgid "The virtual machine I<must be shut down> before using this tool."
msgstr "Pirms šī rīka izmantošanas virtuālajai mašīnai I<jābūt izslēgtai>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:52
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify may require up to 2x the virtual size of the source disk image "
"(1 temporary copy + 1 destination image).  This is in the worst case and "
"usually much less space is required."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify var būt vajadzīgs līdz 2x avota diska attēla virtuālajam "
"izmēram (1 pagaidu kopija + 1 mērķa attēls).  Tas ir sliktākajā gadījumā, un "
"parasti vajadzīgs daudz mazāk vietas."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:56 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:444
msgid ""
"If you are using the I<--in-place> option, then large amounts of temporary "
"space are B<not> required."
msgstr ""
"Ja izmantojat opciju I<--in-place>, liels pagaidu vietas apjoms B<nav> "
"vajadzīgs."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:61
msgid "Virt-sparsify cannot resize disk images.  To do that, use L<virt-resize(1)>."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify nevar mainīt disku attēlu izmēru.  Tam izmantojiet L<virt-"
"resize(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:66
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify cannot handle encrypted disks.  Libguestfs supports encrypted "
"disks, but encrypted disks themselves cannot be sparsified."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify nevar apstrādāt šifrētus diskus.  Libguestfs atbalsta šifrētus "
"diskus, taču pašus šifrētos diskus nevar retināt."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:71
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify cannot yet sparsify the space between partitions.  Note that "
"this space is often used for critical items like bootloaders so it's not "
"really unused."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify vēl nevar retināt vietu starp nodalījumiem.  Ņemiet vērā, ka "
"šo vietu bieži izmanto kritiski svarīgiem elementiem, piemēram, sāknētājiem, "
"tāpēc tā patiesībā nav neizmantota."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:77
msgid ""
"In copy mode, qcow2 internal snapshots are not copied over to the "
"destination image."
msgstr ""
"Kopēšanas režīmā qcow2 iekšējie momentuzņēmumi netiek kopēti uz mērķa attēlu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:82
msgid ""
"You may also want to read the manual pages for the associated tools "
"L<virt-filesystems(1)> and L<virt-df(1)> before starting."
msgstr ""
"Pirms sākšanas, iespējams, vēlēsieties izlasīt arī saistīto rīku L<virt-"
"filesystems(1)> un L<virt-df(1)> rokasgrāmatas lapas."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:87
msgid "Typical usage is:"
msgstr "Tipisks lietojums ir:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:91
msgid ""
"which copies C<indisk> to C<outdisk>, making the output sparse.  C<outdisk> "
"is created, or overwritten if it already exists.  The format of the input "
"disk is detected (eg. qcow2) and the same format is used for the output "
"disk."
msgstr ""
"kas kopē C<indisk> uz C<outdisk>, padarot izvadi retinātu.  C<outdisk> tiek "
"izveidots vai pārrakstīts, ja tas jau eksistē.  Ievades diska formāts tiek "
"noteikts (piem., qcow2), un tas pats formāts tiek izmantots izvades diskam."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:96
msgid "To convert between formats, use the I<--convert> option:"
msgstr "Lai pārveidotu starp formātiem, izmantojiet opciju I<--convert>:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify disk.raw --convert qcow2 disk.qcow2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify disk.raw --convert qcow2 disk.qcow2\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:100
msgid ""
"Virt-sparsify tries to zero and sparsify free space on every filesystem it "
"can find within the source disk image.  You can get it to ignore (don't zero "
"free space on) certain filesystems by doing:"
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify mēģina nullēt un retināt brīvo vietu katrā failu sistēmā, ko "
"tas var atrast avota diska attēlā.  Lai tas ignorētu noteiktas failu "
"sistēmas (nenullētu to brīvo vietu), izpildiet:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:104
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify --ignore /dev/sda1 indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify --ignore /dev/sda1 indisk outdisk\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:106
msgid "See L<virt-filesystems(1)> to get a list of filesystems within a disk image."
msgstr ""
"Diska attēla failu sistēmu sarakstu var iegūt ar L<virt-filesystems(1)>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:109
msgid ""
"Since virt-sparsify E<ge> 1.26, you can now sparsify a disk image in place "
"by doing:"
msgstr "Kopš virt-sparsify E<ge> 1.26 diska attēlu var retināt uz vietas šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:112 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:350
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify --in-place disk.img\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify --in-place disk.img\n"
"\n"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:122
msgid "B<--check-tmpdir> B<ignore>"
msgstr "B<--check-tmpdir> B<ignore>"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:124
msgid "B<--check-tmpdir> B<continue>"
msgstr "B<--check-tmpdir> B<continue>"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:126
msgid "B<--check-tmpdir> B<warn>"
msgstr "B<--check-tmpdir> B<warn>"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:128
msgid "B<--check-tmpdir> B<fail>"
msgstr "B<--check-tmpdir> B<fail>"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:130
msgid ""
"Check if L</TMPDIR> or I<--tmp> directory has enough space to complete the "
"operation.  This is just an estimate."
msgstr ""
"Pārbaudīt, vai L</TMPDIR> vai I<--tmp> direktorijā ir pietiekami daudz "
"vietas darbības pabeigšanai.  Tas ir tikai aplēse."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:133
msgid "If the check indicates a problem, then you can either:"
msgstr "Ja pārbaude norāda uz problēmu, varat:"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:139
msgid "B<ignore> it,"
msgstr "B<ignorēt> to,"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:143
msgid "print a warning and B<continue>,"
msgstr "izdrukāt brīdinājumu un B<turpināt>,"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:147
msgid ""
"B<warn> and wait for the user to press the Return key (this is the default), "
"or:"
msgstr ""
"B<brīdināt> un gaidīt, līdz lietotājs nospiež taustiņu Return (tas ir "
"noklusējums), vai:"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:152
msgid "B<fail> and exit."
msgstr "B<neizdoties> un iziet."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:156 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:172
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:193 sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:257
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:279
msgid "You cannot use this option and I<--in-place> together."
msgstr "Šo opciju nevar izmantot kopā ar I<--in-place>."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:167
msgid "B<--compress>"
msgstr "B<--compress>"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:169
msgid ""
"Compress the output file.  This I<only> works if the output format is "
"C<qcow2>."
msgstr ""
"Saspiest izvades failu.  Tas darbojas I<tikai> tad, ja izvades formāts ir "
"C<qcow2>."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:174
msgid "B<--convert> raw"
msgstr "B<--convert> raw"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:176
msgid "B<--convert> qcow2"
msgstr "B<--convert> qcow2"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:178
msgid "B<--convert> [other formats]"
msgstr "B<--convert> [other formats]"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:180
msgid ""
"Use C<output-format> as the format for the destination image.  If this is "
"not specified, then the input format is used."
msgstr ""
"Izmantot C<output-format> kā mērķa attēla formātu.  Ja tas nav norādīts, "
"tiek izmantots ievades formāts."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:183
msgid "Supported and known-working output formats are: C<raw>, C<qcow2>, C<vdi>."
msgstr ""
"Atbalstītie un zināmi strādājoši izvades formāti ir: C<raw>, C<qcow2>, C<vdi>"
"."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:185
msgid ""
"You can also use any format supported by the L<qemu-img(1)> program, "
"eg. C<vmdk>, but support for other formats is reliant on qemu."
msgstr ""
"Varat izmantot arī jebkuru programmas L<qemu-img(1)> atbalstītu formātu, "
"piem., C<vmdk>, taču citu formātu atbalsts ir atkarīgs no qemu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:188
msgid ""
"Specifying the I<--convert> option is usually a good idea, because then "
"virt-sparsify doesn't need to try to guess the input format."
msgstr ""
"Opcijas I<--convert> norādīšana parasti ir laba doma, jo tad virt-sparsify "
"nav jāmēģina uzminēt ievades formāts."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:191
msgid "For fine-tuning the output format, see: I<--compress>, I<-o>."
msgstr "Izvades formāta precizēšanai skatiet: I<--compress>, I<-o>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:197
msgid ""
"When prompting for keys and passphrases, virt-sparsify normally turns "
"echoing off so you cannot see what you are typing.  If you are not worried "
"about Tempest attacks and there is no one else in the room you can specify "
"this flag to see what you are typing."
msgstr ""
"Pieprasot atslēgas un paroles frāzes, virt-sparsify parasti izslēdz atbalsi, "
"lai nevarētu redzēt, ko rakstāt.  Ja neuztraucaties par Tempest uzbrukumiem "
"un telpā neviena cita nav, varat norādīt šo karogu, lai redzētu, ko rakstāt."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:212
msgid "B<--ignore> filesystem"
msgstr "B<--ignore> filesystem"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:214
msgid "B<--ignore> volgroup"
msgstr "B<--ignore> volgroup"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:216
msgid "Ignore the named filesystem."
msgstr "Ignorēt nosaukto failu sistēmu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:218
msgid ""
"When not using I<--in-place>: Free space on the filesystem will not be "
"zeroed, but existing blocks of zeroes will still be sparsified."
msgstr ""
"Neizmantojot I<--in-place>: failu sistēmas brīvā vieta netiks nullēta, bet "
"esošie nulles bloki tomēr tiks retināti."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:221
msgid "When using I<--in-place>, the filesystem is ignored completely."
msgstr "Izmantojot I<--in-place>, failu sistēma tiek pilnībā ignorēta."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:223
msgid ""
"In the second form, this ignores the named volume group.  Use the volume "
"group name without the F</dev/> prefix, eg. I<--ignore vg_foo>"
msgstr ""
"Otrajā formā tiek ignorēta nosauktā sējumu grupa.  Izmantojiet sējumu grupas "
"nosaukumu bez priedēkļa F</dev/>, piem., I<--ignore vg_foo>"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:228
msgid "B<--in-place>"
msgstr "B<--in-place>"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:230
msgid ""
"Do in-place sparsification instead of copying sparsification.  See "
"L</IN-PLACE SPARSIFICATION> below."
msgstr ""
"Veikt retināšanu uz vietas, nevis kopējošu retināšanu.  Skatiet L</"
"RETINĀŠANA UZ VIETAS> tālāk."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:245
msgid "B<-o> option[,option,...]"
msgstr "B<-o> option[,option,...]"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:247
msgid ""
"Pass I<-o> option(s) to the L<qemu-img(1)> command to fine-tune the output "
"format.  Options available depend on the output format (see I<--convert>) "
"and the installed version of the qemu-img program."
msgstr ""
"Nodot komandai L<qemu-img(1)> I<-o> opciju(-as), lai precizētu izvades "
"formātu.  Pieejamās opcijas ir atkarīgas no izvades formāta (skatiet I<--"
"convert>) un instalētās qemu-img programmas versijas."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:251
msgid ""
"You should use I<-o> at most once.  To pass multiple options, separate them "
"with commas, eg:"
msgstr ""
"I<-o> jāizmanto ne vairāk kā vienreiz.  Lai nodotu vairākas opcijas, "
"atdaliet tās ar komatiem, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:254
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" virt-sparsify --convert qcow2 \\\n"
"   -o cluster_size=512,preallocation=metadata ...\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" virt-sparsify --convert qcow2 \\\n"
"   -o cluster_size=512,preallocation=metadata ...\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:263
msgid "This disables progress bars and other unnecessary output."
msgstr "Tas atspējo progresa joslas un citu nevajadzīgu izvadi."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:265
msgid "B<--tmp> block_device"
msgstr "B<--tmp> block_device"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:267
msgid "B<--tmp> dir"
msgstr "B<--tmp> dir"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:269
msgid ""
"In copying mode only, use the named device or directory as the location of "
"the temporary overlay (see also L</TMPDIR> below)."
msgstr ""
"Tikai kopēšanas režīmā izmantot nosaukto ierīci vai direktoriju kā pagaidu "
"pārklājuma atrašanās vietu (skatīt arī L</TMPDIR> tālāk)."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:272
msgid ""
"If the parameter given is a block device, then the block device is written "
"to directly.  B<Note this erases the existing contents of the block device>."
msgstr ""
"Ja norādītais parametrs ir bloku ierīce, rakstīšana notiek tieši bloku "
"ierīcē.  B<Ņemiet vērā, ka tas izdzēš bloku ierīces esošo saturu>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:276
msgid ""
"If the parameter is a directory, then this is the same as setting the "
"L</TMPDIR> environment variable."
msgstr ""
"Ja parametrs ir direktorija, tas ir tas pats, kas iestatīt vides mainīgo L</"
"TMPDIR>."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:281
msgid "B<--tmp> prebuilt:file"
msgstr "B<--tmp> prebuilt:file"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:283
msgid ""
"In copying mode only, the specialized option I<--tmp prebuilt:file> (where "
"C<prebuilt:> is a literal string) causes virt-sparsify to use the qcow2 "
"C<file> as temporary space."
msgstr ""
"Tikai kopēšanas režīmā specializētā opcija I<--tmp prebuilt:file> (kur "
"C<prebuilt:> ir burtiska virkne) liek virt-sparsify kā pagaidu vietu "
"izmantot qcow2 failu C<file>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:291
msgid ""
"The file B<must> be freshly formatted as qcow2, with indisk as the backing "
"file."
msgstr "Failam B<jābūt> tikko formatētam kā qcow2, ar indisk kā pamatfailu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:296
msgid "If you rerun virt-sparsify, you B<must> recreate the file before each run."
msgstr ""
"Ja virt-sparsify palaižat atkārtoti, fails B<jāizveido> no jauna pirms "
"katras palaišanas."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:301
msgid "Virt-sparsify does not delete the file."
msgstr "Virt-sparsify neizdzēš failu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:305
msgid ""
"This option is used by oVirt which requires a specially formatted temporary "
"file."
msgstr "Šo opciju izmanto oVirt, kam vajadzīgs īpaši formatēts pagaidu fails."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:330
msgid "B<--zero> partition"
msgstr "B<--zero> partition"

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:332
msgid "B<--zero> logvol"
msgstr "B<--zero> logvol"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:334
msgid ""
"Zero the contents of the named partition or logical volume in the guest.  "
"All data on the device is lost, but sparsification is excellent! You can "
"give this option multiple times."
msgstr ""
"Nullēt nosauktā viesa nodalījuma vai loģiskā sējuma saturu.  Visi ierīces "
"dati tiek zaudēti, bet retināšana ir lieliska! Šo opciju var norādīt "
"vairākkārt."

#. type: =head1
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:340
msgid "IN-PLACE SPARSIFICATION"
msgstr "RETINĀŠANA UZ VIETAS"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:342
msgid ""
"Since virt-sparsify E<ge> 1.26, the tool is able to do in-place "
"sparsification (instead of copying from an input disk to an output disk).  "
"This is more efficient.  It is not able to recover quite as much space as "
"copying sparsification."
msgstr ""
"Kopš virt-sparsify E<ge> 1.26 rīks spēj veikt retināšanu uz vietas (nevis "
"kopēt no ievades diska uz izvades disku).  Tas ir efektīvāk.  Tas nespēj "
"atgūt tikpat daudz vietas kā kopējošā retināšana."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:347
msgid "To use this mode, specify a disk image which will be modified in place:"
msgstr ""
"Lai izmantotu šo režīmu, norādiet diska attēlu, kas tiks mainīts uz vietas:"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:352
msgid ""
"Some options are not compatible with this mode: I<--convert>, I<--compress> "
"and I<-o> because they require wholesale disk format changes; "
"I<--check-tmpdir> because large amounts of temporary space are not required."
msgstr ""
"Dažas opcijas nav saderīgas ar šo režīmu: I<--convert>, I<--compress> un I<-"
"o>, jo tām vajadzīgas pilnīgas diska formāta izmaiņas; I<--check-tmpdir>, jo "
"liels pagaidu vietas apjoms nav vajadzīgs."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:357
msgid "In-place sparsification works using discard (a.k.a trim or unmap)  support."
msgstr ""
"Retināšana uz vietas darbojas, izmantojot discard (t. s. trim vai unmap) "
"atbalstu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:362
msgid ""
"The I<--machine-readable> option can be used to make the output more machine "
"friendly, which is useful when calling virt-sparsify from other programs, "
"GUIs etc."
msgstr ""
"Opciju I<--machine-readable> var izmantot, lai padarītu izvadi ērtāku "
"mašīnapstrādei, kas noder, izsaucot virt-sparsify no citām programmām, "
"grafiskām saskarnēm u. c."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:368
msgid ""
"Firstly use the option on its own to query the capabilities of the "
"virt-sparsify binary.  Typical output looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Pirmkārt, izmantojiet opciju vienu pašu, lai noskaidrotu virt-sparsify "
"binārā faila spējas.  Tipiska izvade izskatās šādi:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:371
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" $ virt-sparsify --machine-readable\n"
" virt-sparsify\n"
" ntfs\n"
" btrfs\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" $ virt-sparsify --machine-readable\n"
" virt-sparsify\n"
" ntfs\n"
" btrfs\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:401
msgid ""
"The calling program should treat messages sent to stderr as error messages.  "
"In addition, virt-sparsify exits with a non-zero status code if there was a "
"fatal error."
msgstr ""
"Izsaucošajai programmai standartkļūdu izvadē sūtītie ziņojumi jāuzskata par "
"kļūdu ziņojumiem.  Turklāt fatālas kļūdas gadījumā virt-sparsify iziet ar "
"statusa kodu, kas nav nulle."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:407
msgid ""
"All versions of virt-sparsify have supported the I<--machine-readable> "
"option."
msgstr ""
"Visas virt-sparsify versijas ir atbalstījušas opciju I<--machine-readable>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:415
msgid ""
"Windows 8 \"fast startup\" can prevent virt-sparsify from working.  See "
"L<guestfs(3)/WINDOWS HIBERNATION AND WINDOWS 8 FAST STARTUP>."
msgstr ""
"Windows 8 „ātrā startēšana” var neļaut virt-sparsify darboties.  Skatiet "
"L<guestfs(3)/WINDOWS HIBERNĀCIJA UN WINDOWS 8 ĀTRĀ STARTĒŠANA>."

#. type: =item
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:422
msgid "TMPDIR"
msgstr "TMPDIR"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:424
msgid ""
"Location of the temporary directory used for the potentially large temporary "
"overlay file."
msgstr ""
"Pagaidu direktorijas atrašanās vieta potenciāli lielajam pagaidu pārklājuma "
"failam."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:427
msgid ""
"In virt-sparsify E<ge> 1.28, you can override this environment variable "
"using the I<--tmp> option."
msgstr ""
"Virt-sparsify E<ge> 1.28 šo vides mainīgo var pārdefinēt ar opciju I<--tmp>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:430
msgid ""
"You should ensure there is enough free space in the worst case for a full "
"copy of the source disk (I<virtual> size), or else set C<$TMPDIR> to point "
"to another directory that has enough space."
msgstr ""
"Jānodrošina, ka sliktākajā gadījumā ir pietiekami daudz brīvas vietas pilnai "
"avota diska kopijai (I<virtuālais> izmērs), vai arī jāiestata C<$TMPDIR> uz "
"citu direktoriju ar pietiekami daudz vietas."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:434
msgid "This defaults to F</tmp>."
msgstr "Noklusējums ir F</tmp>."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:436
msgid ""
"Note that if C<$TMPDIR> is a tmpfs (eg. if F</tmp> is on tmpfs, or if you "
"use C<TMPDIR=/dev/shm>), tmpfs defaults to a maximum size of I<half> of "
"physical RAM.  If virt-sparsify exceeds this, it will hang.  The solution is "
"either to use a real disk, or to increase the maximum size of the tmpfs "
"mountpoint, eg:"
msgstr ""
"Ņemiet vērā: ja C<$TMPDIR> ir tmpfs (piem., ja F</tmp> ir tmpfs vai ja "
"izmantojat C<TMPDIR=/dev/shm>), tmpfs maksimālais izmērs pēc noklusējuma ir "
"I<puse> no fiziskās RAM.  Ja virt-sparsify to pārsniedz, tas uzkārsies.  "
"Risinājums ir vai nu izmantot īstu disku, vai palielināt tmpfs montēšanas "
"punkta maksimālo izmēru, piem.:"

#. type: verbatim
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:442
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" mount -o remount,size=10G /tmp\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" mount -o remount,size=10G /tmp\n"
"\n"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:453
msgid ""
"This program returns 0 if the operation completed without errors.  (This "
"doesn't necessarily mean that space could be freed up.)"
msgstr ""
"Šī programma atgriež 0, ja darbība pabeigta bez kļūdām.  (Tas ne vienmēr "
"nozīmē, ka vietu izdevās atbrīvot.)"

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:456
msgid "A non-zero exit code indicates an error."
msgstr "Izejas kods, kas nav nulle, norāda uz kļūdu."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:458
msgid ""
"If the exit code is C<3> and the I<--in-place> option was used, that "
"indicates that discard support is not available in libguestfs, so copying "
"mode must be used instead."
msgstr ""
"Ja izejas kods ir C<3> un tika izmantota opcija I<--in-place>, tas norāda, "
"ka libguestfs nav pieejams discard atbalsts, tāpēc tā vietā jāizmanto "
"kopēšanas režīms."

#. type: textblock
#: sparsify/virt-sparsify.pod:464
msgid ""
"L<virt-df(1)>, L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-resize(1)>, L<virt-rescue(1)>, "
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<truncate(1)>, L<fallocate(1)>, "
"L<qemu-img(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."
msgstr ""
"L<virt-df(1)>, L<virt-filesystems(1)>, L<virt-resize(1)>, L<virt-rescue(1)>, "
"L<guestfs(3)>, L<guestfish(1)>, L<truncate(1)>, L<fallocate(1)>, L<qemu-img"
"(1)>, L<http://libguestfs.org/>."

